-...she said.

3
00:00:06,666 --> 00:00:09,666
-He that is more than a youth 
is not for me,

4
00:00:09,700 --> 00:00:13,000
and he that is less than a man, 
I am not for him!

5
00:00:13,033 --> 00:00:14,666
-...he said... 
-Lady, as you are mine,

6
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:16,233
I am yours. 
-...she said...

7
00:00:16,266 --> 00:00:17,400
-I do.

8
00:00:17,433 --> 00:00:19,766
-...but a not-so-simple case 
of they said.

9
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:21,766
-What was it 
you told me of today,

10
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:24,700
that your niece, Beatrice,

11
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:27,033
was in love 
with Signior Benedick?

12
00:00:27,066 --> 00:00:29,733
-Oh, aye!

13
00:00:29,766 --> 00:00:33,733
-Are you sure that Benedick 
loves Beatrice?

14
00:00:33,766 --> 00:00:34,900
-Ooh!

15
00:00:34,933 --> 00:00:36,800
-I came hither to tell you

16
00:00:36,833 --> 00:00:38,633
the lady is disloyal.

17
00:00:38,666 --> 00:00:40,100
-Hilarity, heartache, and love

18
00:00:40,133 --> 00:00:42,466
ensue under the stars 
with the Public Theater's

19
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:45,000
Free Shakespeare In The Park 
presentation of the Bard's

20
00:00:45,033 --> 00:00:47,500
comedic masterpiece 
"Much Ado About Nothing."

21
00:00:47,533 --> 00:00:52,166
-Against my will, I am sent 
to bid you come in to dinner.

22
00:00:52,200 --> 00:00:54,666
-There's a double meaning 
in that.

23
