[ Cheers and applause ]

60
00:04:16,933 --> 00:04:18,833
-You showed up! 
-Yes!

61
00:04:18,866 --> 00:04:20,366
-I learned in this letter

62
00:04:20,399 --> 00:04:22,400
that Don Pedro of Aragon 
comes this night.

63
00:04:22,433 --> 00:04:24,666
-He was not three leagues off 
when I left him.

64
00:04:24,700 --> 00:04:26,200
-How many have you lost 
in this action?

65
00:04:26,233 --> 00:04:28,900
-But few of any sort. 
-I find here that Don Pedro

66
00:04:28,933 --> 00:04:31,266
hath bestowed much honor 
on young Claudio!

67
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,133
-Much deserved on his part.

68
00:04:33,166 --> 00:04:36,133
He hath borne himself beyond 
the promise of his age,

69
00:04:36,166 --> 00:04:39,133
doing in the figure of a lamb 
the feats of a lion.

70
00:04:39,166 --> 00:04:41,800
-I pray you, 
is Signior Mountanto

71
00:04:41,833 --> 00:04:43,700
returned from the wars or no?

72
00:04:43,733 --> 00:04:45,300
-I know none 
of that name, lady.

73
00:04:45,333 --> 00:04:47,633
There was none such in the army 
of any sort.

74
00:04:47,666 --> 00:04:49,600
-What is he that you 
ask for, niece?

75
00:04:49,633 --> 00:04:51,900
-My cousin means 
Signior Benedick.

76
00:04:51,933 --> 00:04:55,066
-Oh, he's returned 
and as pleasant as ever he was.

77
00:04:55,100 --> 00:04:58,833
-I pray you, how many hath he 
killed and eaten in these wars?

78
00:04:58,866 --> 00:05:00,200
But how many hath he killed?

79
00:05:00,233 --> 00:05:03,533
For indeed, I promised to eat 
all of his killings.

80
00:05:03,566 --> 00:05:06,233
-Faith, niece, you tax 
Signior Benedick too much.

81
00:05:06,266 --> 00:05:08,233
But he'll be meet with you! 
I doubt it not!

82
00:05:08,266 --> 00:05:10,400
-He hath done good service, 
lady, in these wars.

83
00:05:10,433 --> 00:05:11,933
-He is a very 
valiant trenchman.

84
00:05:11,966 --> 00:05:13,400
He hath an excellent stomach.

85
00:05:13,433 --> 00:05:15,200
-And a good soldier too, lady.

86
00:05:15,233 --> 00:05:19,600
-And a good soldier

87
00:05:15,233 --> 00:05:19,600
to

88
00:05:15,233 --> 00:05:19,600
a lady. 
But what is he to a lord?

89
00:05:19,633 --> 00:05:21,766
-A lord to a lord, 
a man to a man,

90
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:23,533
stuffed with 
all honorable virtue.

91
00:05:23,566 --> 00:05:24,566
-It is so indeed!

92
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:26,733
He is no less 
than a stuffed man,

93
00:05:26,766 --> 00:05:31,433
but for the stuffing, 
well, we're all mortal.

94
00:05:31,466 --> 00:05:32,966
-You must not mistake my niece.

95
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:36,200
There's a kind of merry war 
'twixt Signior Benedick and her.

96
00:05:36,233 --> 00:05:38,700
They never meet, but there's 
a skirmish of wit between them.

97
00:05:38,733 --> 00:05:39,466
-Mm-hmm. 
-Huh.

98
00:05:39,500 --> 00:05:41,266
-Who is his companion now?

99
00:05:41,300 --> 00:05:43,600
He hath every month 
a new sworn brother.

100
00:05:43,633 --> 00:05:45,800
-'Tis possible. 
-Very easily possible.

101
00:05:45,833 --> 00:05:48,100
-I see, lady, the gentleman 
is not in your books.

102
00:05:48,133 --> 00:05:51,066
-No, and he were, 
I would burn my study,

103
00:05:51,100 --> 00:05:53,366
but I pray you, 
who is his companion?

104
00:05:53,400 --> 00:05:55,400
Is there no young squarer now

105
00:05:55,433 --> 00:05:58,133
that will make a voyage with him 
to the devil?

106
00:05:58,166 --> 00:06:01,600
-He is most in the company 
of the right, noble Claudio.

107
00:06:01,633 --> 00:06:03,866
-Oh, Lord, he will hang 
upon him like a disease.

108
00:06:03,900 --> 00:06:05,900
He is sooner caught 
than the pestilence,

109
00:06:05,933 --> 00:06:08,100
and the taker run presently mad!

110
00:06:08,133 --> 00:06:10,166
God, help the noble Claudio.

111
00:06:10,200 --> 00:06:12,166
-I will hold friends 
with you, lady.

112
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:13,700
-Do, good friend.

113
00:06:13,733 --> 00:06:18,966
-Don Pedro is approached! 
[ Car horn honks ]

114
00:06:19,000 --> 00:06:22,466
-♪ Left, right, left, right, 
oh, left, right, left ♪

115
00:06:22,500 --> 00:06:24,466
♪ Right, oh, left

116
