♪ Left, right, left, right, 
oh, left, right, left ♪

118
00:06:30,400 --> 00:06:32,166
♪ Right, oh, left

119
00:06:32,200 --> 00:06:34,166
♪ Right, oh, left

120
00:06:34,200 --> 00:06:38,033
♪ Left, right, left, right, 
oh, left, right, left ♪

121
00:06:38,066 --> 00:06:39,900
♪ Right, oh, left

122
00:06:39,933 --> 00:06:42,300
♪ Right, oh, left

123
00:06:42,333 --> 00:06:45,733
♪ Left, right, left, right, 
oh, left, right, left ♪

124
00:06:45,766 --> 00:06:47,566
♪ Right, oh, left

125
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:48,966
♪ Right, oh, left

126
00:06:49,000 --> 00:06:51,400
Company, halt!

127
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:53,766
Right face!

128
00:06:53,800 --> 00:06:54,866
Huh! 
-Huh!

129
00:06:54,900 --> 00:06:55,733
-Huh! 
-Huh!

130
00:06:55,766 --> 00:06:57,733
-Aaaah!

131
00:06:57,766 --> 00:07:00,166
Oh, good Signior Leonato!

132
00:07:00,200 --> 00:07:01,866
Are you come to meet 
your trouble!

133
00:07:01,900 --> 00:07:03,933
The fashion of the world 
is to avoid cost,

134
00:07:03,966 --> 00:07:05,133
and you encounter it!

135
00:07:05,166 --> 00:07:06,533
-Never came trouble to my house

136
00:07:06,566 --> 00:07:08,133
in the likeness of your grace,

137
00:07:08,166 --> 00:07:10,700
for trouble being gone, 
comfort should remain,

138
00:07:10,733 --> 00:07:13,400
but when you depart from me, 
sorrow abounds,

139
00:07:13,433 --> 00:07:15,133
and happiness takes his leave!

140
00:07:15,166 --> 00:07:17,566
-You embrace your charge 
too willingly!

141
00:07:17,600 --> 00:07:19,600
I think this is your daughter.

142
00:07:19,633 --> 00:07:24,100
-Her mother hath many times 
told me so.

143
00:07:24,133 --> 00:07:26,533
-Were you in doubt, sir, 
that you asked her?

144
00:07:26,566 --> 00:07:30,366
-Signior Benedick, no, 
for then were you a child.

145
00:07:30,400 --> 00:07:31,600
-You have it full, Benedick.

146
00:07:31,633 --> 00:07:34,000
We may guess by this 
what you are, being a man.

147
00:07:34,033 --> 00:07:37,566
-Truly, the lady 
fathers herself.

148
00:07:37,600 --> 00:07:41,266
Be happy, lady, for you are 
like an honorable father.

149
00:07:46,833 --> 00:07:49,533
-If Signior Leonato 
be her father,

150
00:07:49,566 --> 00:07:52,166
she would not have his head 
on her shoulders

151
00:07:52,200 --> 00:07:53,766
as like a man she is.

152
00:07:53,800 --> 00:07:57,166
-I wonder that you will still 
be talking, Signior Benedick!

153
00:07:57,200 --> 00:07:59,166
Nobody marks you!

154
00:07:59,200 --> 00:08:02,566
-What, my dear Lady Disdain, 
are you yet living?

155
00:08:02,600 --> 00:08:04,400
-Is it possible disdain 
should die

156
00:08:04,433 --> 00:08:08,400
while she hath such meet food 
to feed it as Signior Benedick?

157
00:08:08,433 --> 00:08:10,566
Courtesy itself must 
convert to disdain

158
00:08:10,600 --> 00:08:11,933
if you come in her presence.

159
00:08:11,966 --> 00:08:14,266
-Mm. 
-Then is courtesy a turncoat?

160
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:16,600
But it is certain I am loved 
of all ladies...

161
00:08:16,633 --> 00:08:19,300
-Ha! 
-...only you excepted,

162
00:08:19,333 --> 00:08:21,533
and I would I could 
find in my heart

163
00:08:21,566 --> 00:08:25,433
that I had not a hard heart, 
for truly I love none.

164
00:08:25,466 --> 00:08:28,566
-A dear happiness to women.

165
00:08:28,600 --> 00:08:30,333
They would else have 
been troubled

166
00:08:30,366 --> 00:08:31,566
with a pernicious suitor.

167
00:08:31,600 --> 00:08:33,600
I thank God and my cold blood

168
00:08:33,633 --> 00:08:34,933
I am of your humor for that.

169
00:08:34,966 --> 00:08:38,266
I had rather hear my dog 
bark at a crow

170
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:40,500
than a man swear he loves me.

171
00:08:40,533 --> 00:08:43,000
-Ooh, God, keep your ladyship

172
00:08:43,033 --> 00:08:45,533
still in that mind 
so some gentleman or other

173
00:08:45,566 --> 00:08:47,733
shall escape a predestined 
scratched face.

174
00:08:47,766 --> 00:08:49,133
-Scratching could not 
make it worse

175
00:08:49,166 --> 00:08:51,833
to such a face as yours were!

176
00:08:51,866 --> 00:08:53,600
-Oh! 
-Ooh!

177
00:08:53,633 --> 00:08:56,433
-Oh, come on! 
Get him!

178
00:08:56,466 --> 00:08:59,866
-Well, you are 
a rare parrot teacher.

179
00:08:59,900 --> 00:09:02,866
-Bird of my tongue is better 
than a beast of yours.

180
00:09:02,900 --> 00:09:07,033
-I would my horse had 
the speed of your tongue

181
00:09:07,066 --> 00:09:10,000
and so good a continuer, 
but keep your ways.

182
00:09:10,033 --> 00:09:11,866
In God's name, I have done.

183
00:09:11,900 --> 00:09:14,166
-You always end 
with a jade's trick.

184
00:09:14,200 --> 00:09:15,333
I know you of old.

185
00:09:15,366 --> 00:09:17,100
-That is the sum of all, 
Leonato.

186
00:09:17,133 --> 00:09:18,766
Signior Claudio 
and Signior Benedick,

187
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:22,200
my dear friend, Leonato, 
hath invited you all!

188
00:09:22,233 --> 00:09:25,366
I tell him we shall stay here 
at the least a month,

189
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:28,700
and he heartily prays some 
occasion may detain us longer.

190
00:09:28,733 --> 00:09:31,033
-Let me bid you welcome, 
my lord.

191
00:09:31,066 --> 00:09:35,000
Being reconciled to Don John, 
your brother,

192
00:09:35,033 --> 00:09:36,866
I owe you all duty.

193
00:09:36,900 --> 00:09:38,600
-I thank you.

194
00:09:38,633 --> 00:09:41,800
I am not of many words, 
but I thank you.

195
00:09:43,466 --> 00:09:46,200
-Please it, your grace, lead on.

196
00:09:46,233 --> 00:09:49,633
-Your hand, Leonato. 
We will go together.

197
00:09:49,666 --> 00:09:51,633
♪♪

198
00:09:51,666 --> 00:09:53,166
[ Both laugh ]

199
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:58,766
♪♪

200
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:04,333
♪♪

201
00:10:04,366 --> 00:10:06,266
-Go ahead.

202
00:10:06,300 --> 00:10:11,000
♪♪

203
00:10:11,033 --> 00:10:14,100
-Benedick, didst thousand note 
the daughter of Signior Leonato?

204
00:10:14,133 --> 00:10:16,566
-I noted her not, 
but I looked on her.

205
00:10:16,600 --> 00:10:18,433
-Is she not 
a modest young lady?

206
00:10:18,466 --> 00:10:20,533
-Do you question me 
as an honest man should do

207
00:10:20,566 --> 00:10:22,566
for my simple true judgement,

208
00:10:22,600 --> 00:10:25,366
or would you have me 
speak after my customs

209
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:27,266
being a professed tyrant 
to their sex?

210
00:10:27,300 --> 00:10:30,266
-No, I pray thee speak 
in sober judgement.

211
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:32,900
-Only this commendation 
I can afford her,

212
00:10:32,933 --> 00:10:34,933
that were she other than she is,

213
00:10:34,966 --> 00:10:36,366
she were unhandsome,

214
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:38,600
and being no other 
but as she is,

215
00:10:38,633 --> 00:10:39,666
I do not like her.

216
00:10:39,700 --> 00:10:41,566
-Thou thinkest I am in sport.

217
00:10:41,600 --> 00:10:43,900
I pray thee tell me truly 
how thou likest her.

218
00:10:43,933 --> 00:10:47,066
-Would you buy her, 
that you inquire after her?

219
00:10:47,100 --> 00:10:48,233
-In mine eye,

220
00:10:48,266 --> 00:10:51,400
she is the sweetest lady 
that ever I looked on.

221
00:10:51,433 --> 00:10:53,266
-I can see yet 
without spectacles,

222
00:10:53,300 --> 00:10:55,366
and I see no such matter.

223
00:10:55,400 --> 00:10:56,500
There's her cousin,

224
00:10:56,533 --> 00:10:58,433
and she were not possessed 
with a fury,

225
00:10:58,466 --> 00:11:00,333
exceeds her as much in beauty

226
00:11:00,366 --> 00:11:03,166
as the first of May 
doth the last of December,

227
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:06,900
but I hope you have no intent 
to turn husband, have you?

228
00:11:06,933 --> 00:11:10,333
-I would scarce trust myself 
though I had sworn the contrary

229
00:11:10,366 --> 00:11:13,066
if Hero would be my wife. 
-It's come to this?

230
00:11:13,100 --> 00:11:15,733
Shall I never see a bachelor 
of three-score again?

231
00:11:15,766 --> 00:11:17,100
Oh, go to in faith,

232
00:11:17,133 --> 00:11:19,266
and thou wilt needs thrust 
thy neck into a yoke,

233
00:11:19,300 --> 00:11:23,000
wear the print of it 
and sigh away Sundays!

234
00:11:23,033 --> 00:11:25,733
Look, Don Pedro has returned 
to seek you.

235
00:11:25,766 --> 00:11:27,233
-What secret hath held you here

236
00:11:27,266 --> 00:11:28,800
that you follow not 
to Leonato's?

237
00:11:28,833 --> 00:11:31,033
-I would your grace would 
constrain me to tell.

238
00:11:31,066 --> 00:11:32,700
-I charge thee 
on they allegiance.

239
00:11:32,733 --> 00:11:35,100
-You hear, Count Claudio, 
I can be secret as a dumb man.

240
00:11:35,133 --> 00:11:37,766
I would have you think so, 
but on my allegiance...

241
00:11:37,800 --> 00:11:39,366
-Yes. 
-...he is in love.

242
00:11:39,400 --> 00:11:42,466
With who? 
Hero, Leonato's daughter!

243
00:11:42,500 --> 00:11:44,666
-If this were so, 
so it were uttered.

244
00:11:44,700 --> 00:11:47,500
-Like the old tale, my lord, 
it is not so, nor it was not so,

245
00:11:47,533 --> 00:11:49,500
but indeed, 
God forbid it should be so.

246
00:11:49,533 --> 00:11:52,066
-If my passion 
change not shortly,

247
00:11:52,100 --> 00:11:54,033
God forbid 
it should be otherwise.

248
00:11:54,066 --> 00:11:57,833
-Amen if you love her for 
the lady is very well worthy.

249
00:11:57,866 --> 00:11:59,700
-You speak this to fetch me in, 
my lord.

250
00:11:59,733 --> 00:12:01,433
-By my troth, 
I speak my thought.

251
00:12:01,466 --> 00:12:04,000
-And in faith, my lord, 
I spoke mine.

252
00:12:04,033 --> 00:12:05,800
-And by my two faiths 
and troths, my lord,

253
00:12:05,833 --> 00:12:09,266
I spoke mine. 
-That I love her, I feel.

254
00:12:09,300 --> 00:12:10,866
-That she is worthy, I know.

255
00:12:10,900 --> 00:12:13,033
-That I neither feel 
how she should be loved

256
00:12:13,066 --> 00:12:14,733
nor know 
how she should be worthy

257
00:12:14,766 --> 00:12:17,300
is the opinion that fire 
cannot melt out of me.

258
00:12:17,333 --> 00:12:19,066
I will die in it at the stake.

259
00:12:19,100 --> 00:12:21,800
-Thou wast ever 
an obstinate heretic

260
00:12:21,833 --> 00:12:22,833
in the despite of beauty.

261
00:12:22,866 --> 00:12:24,866
-And never could maintain 
his part

262
00:12:24,900 --> 00:12:27,700
but in the force of his will.

263
00:12:27,733 --> 00:12:30,866
-That a woman conceived me, 
I thank her.

264
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,866
That she brought me up, 
I likewise give her

265
00:12:32,900 --> 00:12:36,833
most humble thanks, 
but all women shall pardon me.

266
00:12:36,866 --> 00:12:39,500
Because I will not do them 
the wrong to mistrust any,

267
00:12:39,533 --> 00:12:42,000
I will do myself 
the right to trust none.

268
00:12:42,033 --> 00:12:44,066
-Ah. 
-And the fine is,

269
00:12:44,100 --> 00:12:46,800
or the which I may go the finer,

270
00:12:46,833 --> 00:12:49,666
I will live a bachelor.

271
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:52,666
-I shall see thee, ere I die,

272
00:12:52,700 --> 00:12:55,300
look pale with love.

273
00:12:55,333 --> 00:12:58,300
-With anger, with sickness 
or with hunger, my lord,

274
00:12:58,333 --> 00:12:59,600
not with love.

275
00:12:59,633 --> 00:13:02,100
Prove that ever I lose 
more blood with love

276
00:13:02,133 --> 00:13:03,966
than I will get again 
with drinking,

277
00:13:04,000 --> 00:13:06,700
pick out mine eyes 
with a ballad maker's pen

278
00:13:06,733 --> 00:13:08,866
and hang me up at the door 
of a brothel house

279
00:13:08,900 --> 00:13:10,866
for the sign of blind Cupid.

280
00:13:13,633 --> 00:13:16,633
-Well, if ever thou dost 
fall from this faith,

281
00:13:16,666 --> 00:13:18,300
thou wilt prove 
a notable argument.

282
00:13:18,333 --> 00:13:19,466
In the meantime,

283
00:13:19,500 --> 00:13:21,600
good Signior Benedick, 
repair to Leonato's.

284
00:13:21,633 --> 00:13:24,100
Commend me to him and tell him 
I will not fail him at supper

285
00:13:24,133 --> 00:13:27,033
for indeed he hath made 
great preparation.

286
00:13:27,066 --> 00:13:29,066
-And so I leave you.

287
00:13:34,566 --> 00:13:37,000
-My liege, your highness 
now may do me good.

288
00:13:37,033 --> 00:13:39,200
-My love is thine to teach.

289
00:13:39,233 --> 00:13:41,633
Teach it but how, 
and thou shalt see how apt it is

290
00:13:41,666 --> 00:13:43,933
to learn any hard lesson 
that may do thee good.

291
00:13:43,966 --> 00:13:45,900
-Hath Leonato any son, my lord?

292
00:13:45,933 --> 00:13:47,100
-No child but Hero.

293
00:13:47,133 --> 00:13:49,000
She's his only heir.

294
00:13:49,033 --> 00:13:50,666
Dost thou affect her, Claudio?

295
00:13:50,700 --> 00:13:53,133
-Oh, my lord.

296
00:13:53,166 --> 00:13:55,400
When you went onward 
on this ended action,

297
00:13:55,433 --> 00:13:57,900
I looked upon her 
with a soldier's eye that liked

298
00:13:57,933 --> 00:13:59,266
but had a rougher task in hand

299
00:13:59,300 --> 00:14:01,666
than to drive liking 
to the name of love,

300
00:14:01,700 --> 00:14:03,200
but now I am returned,

301
00:14:03,233 --> 00:14:05,666
and that war thoughts 
have left their places vacant,

302
00:14:05,700 --> 00:14:09,233
in their rooms come thronging 
soft and delicate desires

303
00:14:09,266 --> 00:14:11,700
all prompting me 
how fair young Hero is,

304
00:14:11,733 --> 00:14:13,933
saying I liked her 
ere I went to wars.

305
00:14:13,966 --> 00:14:16,533
-Thou wilt be like a lover 
presently

306
00:14:16,566 --> 00:14:18,766
and tire the hearer 
with a book of words.

307
00:14:18,800 --> 00:14:21,900
If thou dost love fair Hero, 
cherish it,

308
00:14:21,933 --> 00:14:23,566
and I will break with her 
and with her father,

309
00:14:23,600 --> 00:14:25,133
and thou shalt have her.

310
00:14:25,166 --> 00:14:26,566
Was it not to this end 
that thou beganest

311
00:14:26,600 --> 00:14:27,833
to twist so fine a story?

312
00:14:27,866 --> 00:14:29,366
-How sweetly you do 
minister to love

313
00:14:29,400 --> 00:14:31,500
that knows love's grief 
by its complexion,

314
00:14:31,533 --> 00:14:33,533
but lest my liking might 
too sudden seem,

315
00:14:33,566 --> 00:14:35,166
I would've salved it 
with a longer treatise.

316
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:37,433
-Oh, I will fit thee 
with the remedy!

317
00:14:45,600 --> 00:14:46,466
I know.

318
00:14:46,500 --> 00:14:48,300
We shall have reveling tonight.

319
00:14:48,333 --> 00:14:50,900
I will assume thy part 
in some disguise

320
00:14:50,933 --> 00:14:54,666
and tell fair Hero I am Claudio,

321
00:14:54,700 --> 00:14:57,666
and in her bosom, 
I'll unclasp my heart

322
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,300
and take her hearing prison

323
00:14:59,333 --> 00:15:03,233
with the force and strong 
encounter of my amorous tale.

324
00:15:03,266 --> 00:15:06,233
Then after to her father 
will I break,

325
00:15:06,266 --> 00:15:10,033
and the conclusion is, 
she shall be thine, huh?

326
00:15:10,066 --> 00:15:13,866
In practice let us 
put it presently.

327
00:15:13,900 --> 00:15:15,866
♪♪

328
00:15:15,900 --> 00:15:18,966
[ Applause ]

329
00:15:19,000 --> 00:15:22,666
-Brother, 
I can tell you strange news

330
00:15:22,700 --> 00:15:25,400
that you yet dreamt not of.

331
00:15:25,433 --> 00:15:26,700
-Are they good?

332
00:15:26,733 --> 00:15:28,733
-The prince and Count Claudio

333
00:15:28,766 --> 00:15:32,266
were thus much overheard 
by a man of mine.

334
00:15:32,300 --> 00:15:36,333
The prince discovered to Claudio 
that he loved my niece,

335
00:15:36,366 --> 00:15:38,133
your daughter,

336
00:15:38,166 --> 00:15:41,266
and meant to acknowledge it 
this night in a dance,

337
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:43,900
and if he found her accordant,

338
00:15:43,933 --> 00:15:47,400
he meant to instantly 
break with you of it.

339
00:15:47,433 --> 00:15:49,533
-Hath the fellow any wit 
that told you this?

340
00:15:49,566 --> 00:15:51,900
-A good, sharp fellow.

341
00:15:51,933 --> 00:15:54,500
I will send for him 
and question him yourself.

342
00:15:54,533 --> 00:15:56,600
-No, no.

343
00:15:56,633 --> 00:16:01,400
We will hold it as a dream 
till it appear itself,

344
00:16:01,433 --> 00:16:03,466
but I will acquaint my daughter 
with all

345
00:16:03,500 --> 00:16:05,866
that she may be the better 
prepared for an answer

346
00:16:05,900 --> 00:16:09,733
if peradventure this to be true!

347
00:16:13,666 --> 00:16:16,366
-My lord, why are you thus 
out of measure sad?

348
00:16:16,400 --> 00:16:19,233
-There is no measure 
in the occasion that breeds.

349
00:16:19,266 --> 00:16:20,966
Therefore, the sadness 
is without limit.

350
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:22,233
-You should hear reason.

351
00:16:22,266 --> 00:16:24,700
-And when I have heard it, 
what blessing brings it?

352
00:16:24,733 --> 00:16:27,366
-If not a present remedy, 
at least a patient sufferance.

353
00:16:27,400 --> 00:16:30,400
-I cannot hide what I am!

354
00:16:30,433 --> 00:16:34,800
I must be sad when I have cause 
and smile at no man's jests,

355
00:16:34,833 --> 00:16:37,900
eat when I have stomach 
and wait for no man's leisure,

356
00:16:37,933 --> 00:16:41,400
sleep when I am drowsy 
and tend on no man's business.

357
00:16:41,433 --> 00:16:43,366
-Yea, but you must not make 
the full show of this

358
00:16:43,400 --> 00:16:45,900
till you may do it 
without controlment!

359
00:16:45,933 --> 00:16:48,400
You have of late stood out 
against your brother,

360
00:16:48,433 --> 00:16:50,366
and he hath ta'en you newly 
into his grace

361
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:52,600
where it is impossible 
you should take true root

362
00:16:52,633 --> 00:16:55,500
but by the fair weather 
that you make yourself.

363
00:16:55,533 --> 00:16:58,200
It is needful that you frame 
the season for your own harvest.

364
00:16:58,233 --> 00:17:00,500
-I had rather be 
a canker in a hedge

365
00:17:00,533 --> 00:17:02,633
than a rose in his grace!

366
00:17:02,666 --> 00:17:06,099
Though I cannot be said to be 
a flattering, honest man,

367
00:17:06,133 --> 00:17:07,800
it must not be denied,

368
00:17:07,833 --> 00:17:12,700
but I am a plain-dealing 
villain.

369
00:17:12,733 --> 00:17:16,966
I am trusted with a muzzle 
and enfranchised with a clog,

370
00:17:17,000 --> 00:17:20,433
therefore have decreed 
not to sing in my cage.

371
00:17:20,466 --> 00:17:24,066
If I had my mouth, I would bite.

372
00:17:24,099 --> 00:17:25,800
If I had my liberty,

373
00:17:25,833 --> 00:17:27,566
I would do my liking.

374
00:17:27,599 --> 00:17:29,266
In the meantime...

375
00:17:29,300 --> 00:17:32,833
let me be that I am, 
and seek not to alter me!

376
00:17:32,866 --> 00:17:34,633
-Can you make no use 
of your discontent?

377
00:17:34,666 --> 00:17:37,333
-I make all use of it 
for I use it only.

378
00:17:37,366 --> 00:17:39,166
Who comes here?

379
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,400
What news, Borachio?

380
00:17:40,433 --> 00:17:42,800
-I came yonder 
from a great supper.

381
00:17:42,833 --> 00:17:46,966
The prince, your brother, is 
royally entertained by Leonato,

382
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,866
and I can give you intelligence 
of an intended marriage.

383
00:17:49,900 --> 00:17:52,666
-Will it serve for any model 
to build mischief on?

384
00:17:52,700 --> 00:17:56,533
What is he for a fool that 
betroths himself to unquietness?

385
00:17:56,566 --> 00:17:58,600
-Marry, it is 
your brother's right hand.

386
00:17:58,633 --> 00:18:00,366
-Who? 
The most exquisite Claudio?

387
00:18:00,400 --> 00:18:02,000
-Even he. 
-A proper squire.

388
00:18:02,033 --> 00:18:04,400
Which way looks he? 
-Marry, on Hero,

389
00:18:04,433 --> 00:18:06,800
the daughter and heir 
of Leonato.

390
00:18:06,833 --> 00:18:09,033
-A very forward March-chick.

391
00:18:09,066 --> 00:18:10,333
How came you to this?

392
00:18:10,366 --> 00:18:13,100
-As I was smoking, comes me 
the prince and Claudio

393
00:18:13,133 --> 00:18:16,000
hand in hand in sad conference.

394
00:18:16,033 --> 00:18:19,133
I whipped me behind the arras, 
and there heard it agreed

395
00:18:19,166 --> 00:18:22,366
upon that the prince should 
woo Hero for himself and,

396
00:18:22,400 --> 00:18:25,566
having obtained her, 
give her to Count Claudio.

397
00:18:25,600 --> 00:18:29,000
-Come! Come! 
Let us thither.

398
00:18:29,033 --> 00:18:31,166
This may prove food

399
00:18:31,200 --> 00:18:32,800
to my displeasure.

400
00:18:32,833 --> 00:18:36,466
That young start-up hath 
all the glory of my overthrow.

401
00:18:36,500 --> 00:18:38,900
If I can cross him any way,

402
00:18:38,933 --> 00:18:40,900
I bless myself every way.

403
00:18:40,933 --> 00:18:42,600
You are both sure 
and will assist me?

404
00:18:42,633 --> 00:18:45,200
-To the death, my lord. 
-Let us to the great supper.

405
00:18:45,233 --> 00:18:47,400
Shall we go prove 
what's to be done?

406
00:18:47,433 --> 00:18:49,900
-We'll wait upon your lordship.

407
00:18:49,933 --> 00:18:52,566
[ Laughter ]

408
00:18:52,600 --> 00:18:55,766
[ Indistinct talking ]

409
00:18:59,566 --> 00:19:01,800
-Was not Count John 
here at supper?

410
00:19:01,833 --> 00:19:02,866
-I saw him not.

411
00:19:02,900 --> 00:19:04,600
-How tartly 
that gentleman looks.

412
00:19:04,633 --> 00:19:05,933
I never can see him,

413
00:19:05,966 --> 00:19:08,233
but I'm heart-burned 
an hour after.

414
00:19:08,266 --> 00:19:11,266
-He is of a very 
melancholy disposition.

415
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:12,933
-He were an excellent man 
that were made

416
00:19:12,966 --> 00:19:16,100
just in the midway 
between him and Benedick.

417
00:19:16,133 --> 00:19:18,833
The one is too like an image 
and says nothing

418
00:19:18,866 --> 00:19:21,533
and the other evermore tattling.

419
00:19:21,566 --> 00:19:24,700
-Then half Signior Benedick's 
tongue and Count John's mouth

420
00:19:24,733 --> 00:19:27,866
and half Count John's melancholy 
and Signior Benedick's face!

421
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:30,200
-With a good leg 
and a good foot, Uncle,

422
00:19:30,233 --> 00:19:31,833
and money enough in his purse,

423
00:19:31,866 --> 00:19:34,266
such a man would win 
any woman in the world

424
00:19:34,300 --> 00:19:36,100
if he could get her goodwill.

425
00:19:36,133 --> 00:19:37,766
-[ Laughs ] By my troth, niece,

426
00:19:37,800 --> 00:19:39,033
thou wilt never 
get thee a husband

427
00:19:39,066 --> 00:19:40,900
if thou be so shrewd 
of thy tongue.

428
00:19:40,933 --> 00:19:42,933
-In faith, she's too cursed.

429
00:19:42,966 --> 00:19:45,366
-Too cursed is 
more than cursed.

430
00:19:45,400 --> 00:19:48,166
I shall lessen God's sending 
that way for it is said

431
00:19:48,200 --> 00:19:50,500
God send a cursed cow 
short horns,

432
00:19:50,533 --> 00:19:53,700
but to a cow too cursed, 
he send none.

433
00:19:53,733 --> 00:19:56,100
-So by being too cursed,

434
00:19:56,133 --> 00:19:58,000
God will send you no horns!

435
00:19:58,033 --> 00:20:01,500
-Just if he send me no husband 
for the which blessing

436
00:20:01,533 --> 00:20:05,000
I am at him upon my knees 
every morning and evening!

437
00:20:05,033 --> 00:20:07,766
Lord, I could not 
endure a husband

438
00:20:07,800 --> 00:20:09,800
with a beard on his face!

439
00:20:09,833 --> 00:20:11,500
I had rather lie in the woollen.

440
00:20:11,533 --> 00:20:14,200
-You may light on a husband 
that hath no beard!

441
00:20:14,233 --> 00:20:15,800
-What should I do with him?

442
00:20:15,833 --> 00:20:17,466
Dress him in my apparel

443
00:20:17,500 --> 00:20:20,700
and make him 
my waiting gentlewoman?

444
00:20:20,733 --> 00:20:23,066
He that hath a beard 
is more than a youth,

445
00:20:23,100 --> 00:20:25,800
and he that hath no beard 
is less than a man,

446
00:20:25,833 --> 00:20:29,133
and he that is more than a youth 
is not for me,

447
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:32,900
and he that is less than a man, 
I am not for him!

448
00:20:32,933 --> 00:20:34,700
Therefore, I will even take

449
00:20:34,733 --> 00:20:36,966
sixpence in earnest 
of the bear-ward

450
00:20:37,000 --> 00:20:39,100
and lead his apes into Hell.

451
00:20:39,133 --> 00:20:42,000
-Well, then go you into Hell? 
-No!

452
00:20:42,033 --> 00:20:44,600
But to the gate,

453
00:20:44,633 --> 00:20:47,566
and there will be the Devil

454
00:20:47,600 --> 00:20:49,266
meet me like an old cuckold

455
00:20:49,300 --> 00:20:51,666
with horns on his head and said,

456
00:20:51,700 --> 00:20:53,766
"Get you to heaven, Beatrice!

457
00:20:53,800 --> 00:20:55,433
Get you to heaven!

458
00:20:55,466 --> 00:20:57,633
Here is no place for you maids!"

459
00:20:57,666 --> 00:20:59,700
So deliver I up my apes

460
00:20:59,733 --> 00:21:02,000
and away to Saint Peter 
for the heavens.

461
00:21:02,033 --> 00:21:04,400
He shows me where 
the bachelors sit,

462
00:21:04,433 --> 00:21:08,800
and there live we 
as merry as the day is long!

463
00:21:08,833 --> 00:21:10,633
-Well, niece!

464
00:21:10,666 --> 00:21:13,866
I trust you will be 
ruled by your father.

465
00:21:13,900 --> 00:21:16,466
-Yes, faith, 
it is my cousin's duty

466
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:18,033
to make curtsy and say,

467
00:21:18,066 --> 00:21:20,833
"Father, as it please you."

468
00:21:20,866 --> 00:21:23,700
But for all that, cousin, 
let him be a handsome fella,

469
00:21:23,733 --> 00:21:26,000
or else make another curtsy 
and say,

470
00:21:26,033 --> 00:21:28,666
"Father, as it please me."

471
00:21:28,700 --> 00:21:30,833
Okurrr!

472
00:21:30,866 --> 00:21:33,000
[ Laughter ]

473
00:21:33,033 --> 00:21:34,866
-Well, niece,

474
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:38,200
I hope to see you one day 
fitted with a husband!

475
00:21:38,233 --> 00:21:42,000
-Not till God make men 
of some other metal than earth.

476
00:21:42,033 --> 00:21:44,500
Would it not grieve a woman

477
00:21:44,533 --> 00:21:48,666
to be overmastered 
with a piece of valiant dust?

478
00:21:48,700 --> 00:21:50,566
No, uncle, I'll none.

479
00:21:50,600 --> 00:21:52,200
Adam's sons are my brethren,

480
00:21:52,233 --> 00:21:55,333
and truly I hold it a sin 
to match in my kindred.

481
00:21:55,366 --> 00:21:57,233
-Daughter, remember 
what I told you.

482
00:21:57,266 --> 00:21:59,833
If the prince do solicit you 
in that kind,

483
00:21:59,866 --> 00:22:01,333
you know your answer.

484
00:22:01,366 --> 00:22:03,700
-The fault will be 
in the music, cousin,

485
00:22:03,733 --> 00:22:06,033
if you be not wooed 
in good time!

486
00:22:06,066 --> 00:22:08,500
-Cousin, you apprehend 
passing shrewdly!

487
00:22:08,533 --> 00:22:10,700
-I have a good eye, uncle!

488
00:22:10,733 --> 00:22:13,100
I can see a church by daylight!

489
00:22:13,133 --> 00:22:14,100
[ Indistinct shouting ]

490
00:22:14,133 --> 00:22:16,166
-The revelers are entering!

491
00:22:16,200 --> 00:22:20,166
[ Indistinct talking, laughter ]

492
00:22:20,200 --> 00:22:24,500
♪♪

493
00:22:24,533 --> 00:22:29,766
-♪ Let's take a chance and 
we can dance all night through ♪

494
00:22:29,800 --> 00:22:32,900
♪ Baby, me and you

495
00:22:32,933 --> 00:22:35,300
♪ Let's see what happens, 
see what happens ♪

496
00:22:35,333 --> 00:22:37,200
♪ See what happens if we

497
00:22:37,233 --> 00:22:41,100
♪ We make the magic, baby, 
we can make it happen maybe ♪

498
00:22:41,133 --> 00:22:46,666
♪ Let's take a chance, and 
we can dance all night through ♪

499
00:22:46,700 --> 00:22:49,433
♪ Baby, me and you

500
00:22:49,466 --> 00:22:52,866
-Lady, will you walk about 
with your friend?

501
00:22:52,900 --> 00:22:56,666
-So you walk softly and look 
sweetly and say nothing,

502
00:22:56,700 --> 00:23:01,266
I am yours for the walk, 
and especially when I walk away.

503
00:23:01,300 --> 00:23:03,133
-With me in your company?

504
00:23:03,166 --> 00:23:05,100
-I may say so when I please.

505
00:23:05,133 --> 00:23:07,433
-And when please you to say so?

506
00:23:07,466 --> 00:23:08,733
-When I like your favor.

507
00:23:08,766 --> 00:23:11,400
-Speak low if you speak love.

508
00:23:11,433 --> 00:23:13,766
-Well, I would you did like me.

509
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:16,033
-So would not I 
for your own sake

510
00:23:16,066 --> 00:23:18,966
for I have many ill qualities. 
-Which is one?

511
00:23:19,000 --> 00:23:22,000
-I say my prayers aloud. 
-I love you the better.

512
00:23:22,033 --> 00:23:24,233
The hearers may cry, "Amen."

513
00:23:24,266 --> 00:23:26,066
-God match me with 
a good dancer.

514
00:23:26,100 --> 00:23:27,033
-Amen.

515
00:23:27,066 --> 00:23:28,833
-And God keep him 
out of my sight

516
00:23:28,866 --> 00:23:30,266
when the dance is done.

517
00:23:30,300 --> 00:23:31,933
-No more words?

518
00:23:31,966 --> 00:23:33,733
-♪ Let's see what happens, 
see what happens ♪

519
00:23:33,766 --> 00:23:35,466
♪ See what happens if we

520
00:23:35,500 --> 00:23:39,566
♪ We make the magic, baby, 
we can make it happen maybe ♪

521
00:23:39,600 --> 00:23:45,166
♪ Let's take a chance, and 
we can dance all night long ♪

522
00:23:45,200 --> 00:23:48,466
♪ Baby, me and you

523
00:23:48,500 --> 00:23:49,866
-I know you well enough!

524
00:23:49,900 --> 00:23:52,933
You are Signior Antonio! 
-At a word, I am not.

525
00:23:52,966 --> 00:23:55,833
-I know you by the waggling 
of your head.

526
00:23:55,866 --> 00:23:58,366
-To tell you true, 
I counterfeit him.

527
00:23:58,400 --> 00:24:00,200
-You could never do him 
so ill well

528
00:24:00,233 --> 00:24:02,066
unless you are the very man!

529
00:24:02,100 --> 00:24:04,000
You are he! 
You are he!

530
00:24:04,033 --> 00:24:07,466
-At a word, I am not. 
-Come, come, do you think

531
00:24:07,500 --> 00:24:09,933
I do not know you 
by your excellent wit?

532
00:24:09,966 --> 00:24:12,233
Can virtue hide itself?

533
00:24:12,266 --> 00:24:13,933
Go to, mum! 
You are he!

534
00:24:13,966 --> 00:24:17,333
Graces will appear, 
and there's an end!

535
00:24:17,366 --> 00:24:19,400
-Will you not tell me 
who told you so?

536
00:24:19,433 --> 00:24:21,066
-No, you shall pardon me.

537
00:24:21,100 --> 00:24:23,100
-Nor will you not tell me 
who you are?

538
00:24:23,133 --> 00:24:25,900
-Ooh, not now. 
-That I was disdainful, well,

539
00:24:25,933 --> 00:24:28,200
this was Signior Benedick 
that said so.

540
00:24:28,233 --> 00:24:29,266
-What's he?

541
00:24:29,300 --> 00:24:30,866
-I'm sure you know him 
well enough.

542
00:24:30,900 --> 00:24:33,500
-Not I, believe me. 
-Did he never make you laugh?

543
00:24:33,533 --> 00:24:35,500
-I pray you, what is he?

544
00:24:35,533 --> 00:24:38,100
-Why, he's the prince's jester,

545
00:24:38,133 --> 00:24:39,500
a very dull fool.

546
00:24:39,533 --> 00:24:41,433
I'm sure he's in the fleet. 
[ Giggles ]

547
00:24:41,466 --> 00:24:43,100
-When I know the gentleman,

548
00:24:43,133 --> 00:24:44,600
I'll tell him what you say.

549
00:24:44,633 --> 00:24:47,533
-Do. Do.

550
00:24:47,566 --> 00:24:50,700
We must follow the leaders! 
-Hey!

551
00:24:50,733 --> 00:24:53,100
♪ Let's see what happens, 
see what happens ♪

552
00:24:53,133 --> 00:24:54,933
♪ See what happens if we

553
00:24:54,966 --> 00:24:59,066
♪ We make the magic, baby, 
we can make it happen maybe ♪

554
00:24:59,100 --> 00:25:04,333
♪ Let's take a chance, and 
we can dance all night through ♪

555
00:25:04,366 --> 00:25:07,833
♪ Baby, me and you

556
00:25:07,866 --> 00:25:10,666
-Hey, hey!

557
00:25:10,700 --> 00:25:15,800
♪♪

558
00:25:15,833 --> 00:25:21,133
-♪ Let's take a chance, and 
we can dance all night through ♪

559
00:25:21,166 --> 00:25:24,200
♪ Baby, me and you

560
00:25:24,233 --> 00:25:26,466
♪ Let's see what happens, 
see what happens ♪

561
00:25:26,500 --> 00:25:28,500
♪ See what happens

562
00:25:28,533 --> 00:25:31,366
[ Cheers and applause ]

563
00:25:34,300 --> 00:25:38,300
-Sure, my brother 
is amorous on Hero

564
00:25:38,333 --> 00:25:41,166
and hath withdrawn her father 
to break with him about it.

565
00:25:41,200 --> 00:25:43,833
The ladies follow her, 
and but one visor remains.

566
00:25:43,866 --> 00:25:46,833
-And that is Claudio. 
I know him by his bearing.

567
00:25:46,866 --> 00:25:49,400
-Are you not Signior Benedick?

568
00:25:49,433 --> 00:25:52,466
-You know me well. 
I am he.

569
00:25:52,500 --> 00:25:56,533
-Signior, you are very near 
my brother in his love.

570
00:25:56,566 --> 00:25:59,133
He is enamored on Hero.

571
00:25:59,166 --> 00:26:01,333
I pray you dissuade him 
from her.

572
00:26:01,366 --> 00:26:03,233
She is no equal for his birth.

573
00:26:03,266 --> 00:26:05,000
You may do the part 
of an honest man in it.

574
00:26:05,033 --> 00:26:06,400
-How know you he loves her?

575
00:26:06,433 --> 00:26:08,300
-I heard him swear 
his affection.

576
00:26:08,333 --> 00:26:11,566
-So did I, too, and swore 
he would marry her tonight.

577
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:14,266
-Come, let us to the banquet.

578
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:19,600
-Thus answer I 
in the name of Benedick

579
00:26:19,633 --> 00:26:23,733
but hear these ill news 
with the ears of Claudio.

580
00:26:23,766 --> 00:26:27,366
Tis certain so the prince 
woos for himself.

581
00:26:27,400 --> 00:26:29,233
Friendship is constant 
in all other things

582
00:26:29,266 --> 00:26:31,933
save in the office 
and affairs of love.

583
00:26:31,966 --> 00:26:35,133
Therefore, all hearts 
in love use their own tongues.

584
00:26:35,166 --> 00:26:37,200
Let every eye negotiate 
for itself

585
00:26:37,233 --> 00:26:39,800
and trust no agent 
for beauty is a witch

586
00:26:39,833 --> 00:26:43,966
against whose charms faith 
melteth into blood.

587
00:26:44,000 --> 00:26:45,700
Farewell therefore, Hero!

588
00:26:53,666 --> 00:26:56,266
-Count Claudio!

589
00:26:56,300 --> 00:26:57,466
-Yea, the same.

590
00:26:57,500 --> 00:26:59,933
-Come, will you go with me? 
-Whither?

591
00:26:59,966 --> 00:27:01,766
-Even to the next willow

592
00:27:01,800 --> 00:27:03,800
about your own business, county.

593
00:27:03,833 --> 00:27:07,133
What fashion will you 
wear the garland of,

594
00:27:07,166 --> 00:27:09,466
about your neck 
like an usurer's chain,

595
00:27:09,500 --> 00:27:11,766
under your arm 
like a lieutenant's scarf?

596
00:27:11,800 --> 00:27:14,733
You must wear it one way for 
the prince hath got your Hero!

597
00:27:14,766 --> 00:27:16,666
-I wish him joy of her.

598
00:27:16,700 --> 00:27:18,900
-But did you think the prince 
would've served you thus?

599
00:27:18,933 --> 00:27:20,100
-I pray you, leave me.

600
00:27:20,133 --> 00:27:22,633
-Ho-ho, now you strike 
like the blind man.

601
00:27:22,666 --> 00:27:25,500
-If it will not be, 
I'

602
00:27:22,666 --> 00:27:25,500
ll

603
00:27:22,666 --> 00:27:25,500
leave you.

604
00:27:26,300 --> 00:27:28,600
-Clau--

605
00:27:28,633 --> 00:27:31,033
Alas, poor hurt fowl!

606
00:27:31,066 --> 00:27:34,566
Now will he creep in the sedges.

607
00:27:34,600 --> 00:27:38,233
But that my Lady Beatrice 
should know me and not know me!

608
00:27:38,266 --> 00:27:40,100
The prince's fool, ha!

609
00:27:40,133 --> 00:27:44,166
It may be I go under that title 
because I am merry.

610
00:27:44,200 --> 00:27:47,533
Yea, but so am I apt 
to do myself wrong.

611
00:27:47,566 --> 00:27:49,566
I am not so reputed.

612
00:27:49,600 --> 00:27:52,500
It is the base, though bitter, 
disposition of Beatrice

613
00:27:52,533 --> 00:27:55,000
that puts the world 
into her person

614
00:27:55,033 --> 00:27:57,000
and so gives me out.

615
00:27:57,033 --> 00:27:59,800
Well, I'll be revenged as I may.

616
00:27:59,833 --> 00:28:01,900
-Now, signior, 
where's the count?!

617
00:28:01,933 --> 00:28:03,666
Did you see him? 
-[ Coughs ] I found him here

618
00:28:03,700 --> 00:28:06,033
as melancholy 
as a lodge in a warren.

619
00:28:06,066 --> 00:28:08,333
I told him, 
and I think I told him true,

620
00:28:08,366 --> 00:28:11,333
that your grace had got 
the goodwill of this young lady.

621
00:28:11,366 --> 00:28:12,500
-Ah!

622
00:28:12,533 --> 00:28:14,466
-And I offered him my company 
to a willow tree

623
00:28:14,500 --> 00:28:17,233
either to make him a garland 
as being forsaken

624
00:28:17,266 --> 00:28:21,000
or to bind him up a rod 
as being worthy to be whipped.

625
00:28:21,033 --> 00:28:22,766
-To be whipped? 
What's his fault?

626
00:28:22,800 --> 00:28:24,866
-The flat transgression 
of a schoolboy who,

627
00:28:24,900 --> 00:28:27,266
being overjoyed 
with finding a birds' nest,

628
00:28:27,300 --> 00:28:29,666
shows it his companion, 
and he steals it.

629
00:28:29,700 --> 00:28:31,800
-Wilt thou make a trust 
a transgression?

630
00:28:31,833 --> 00:28:33,366
The transgression 
is in the stealer.

631
00:28:33,400 --> 00:28:36,033
-Yet it had not been amiss 
the rod had been made

632
00:28:36,066 --> 00:28:37,433
and the garland, too,

633
00:28:37,466 --> 00:28:39,966
for the garland 
he might have worn himself,

634
00:28:40,000 --> 00:28:42,266
and the rod he might 
have bestowed on you,

635
00:28:42,300 --> 00:28:46,133
who, as I take it, 
have stolen his birds' nest.

636
00:28:46,166 --> 00:28:48,166
-I will but teach them to sing

637
00:28:48,200 --> 00:28:49,733
and restore them to the owner.

638
00:28:49,766 --> 00:28:52,500
-If their singing 
answer your saying,

639
00:28:52,533 --> 00:28:54,166
by my faith, you say honestly.

640
00:28:54,200 --> 00:28:57,066
-Mm-hmm, the Lady Beatrice 
hath a quarrel to you.

641
00:28:57,100 --> 00:28:58,666
The gentleman that danced 
with her told her

642
00:28:58,700 --> 00:29:00,000
she is much wronged by you.

643
00:29:00,033 --> 00:29:03,566
-Oh, she misused me past 
the endurance of a block.

644
00:29:03,600 --> 00:29:06,333
She speaks poniards 
and every word stabs.

645
00:29:06,366 --> 00:29:08,900
I would not marry her, 
though she were endowed

646
00:29:08,933 --> 00:29:12,766
with all that Adam had left him 
before he transgressed.

647
00:29:12,800 --> 00:29:14,866
I would to God some scholar 
would conjure her,

648
00:29:14,900 --> 00:29:16,900
for certainly while she is here

649
00:29:16,933 --> 00:29:19,866
a man may live as quiet in Hell 
as in a sanctuary,

650
00:29:19,900 --> 00:29:23,166
and people sin upon purpose 
because they would go thither.

651
00:29:23,200 --> 00:29:24,866
So, indeed, all disquiet,

652
00:29:24,900 --> 00:29:26,966
horror, and perturbation 
follows her.

653
00:29:27,000 --> 00:29:27,933
-Oh, look. 
Here she comes.

654
00:29:27,966 --> 00:29:30,066
-Oh, will your grace command me

655
00:29:30,100 --> 00:29:31,700
any service to the world's end?

656
00:29:31,733 --> 00:29:33,333
I will go 
on the slightest errand now

657
00:29:33,366 --> 00:29:36,066
to the Antipodes that you 
can devise to send me on.

658
00:29:36,100 --> 00:29:38,633
I will fetch you a toothpick now 
from the furthest inch of Asia

659
00:29:38,666 --> 00:29:42,366
rather than hold three words 
conference with this harpy.

660
00:29:42,400 --> 00:29:44,766
You have no employment for me?

661
00:29:44,800 --> 00:29:45,900
-None...

662
00:29:45,933 --> 00:29:47,700
but to desire your good company.

663
00:29:47,733 --> 00:29:49,366
-Oh, God, sir!

664
00:29:49,400 --> 00:29:51,166
Here's a dish I love not.

665
00:29:51,200 --> 00:29:54,466
I cannot endure my Lady Tongue.

666
00:29:54,500 --> 00:29:55,966
-Come.

667
00:29:56,000 --> 00:29:58,633
Lady, come.

668
00:29:58,666 --> 00:30:00,000
-[ Sighs ]

669
00:30:03,000 --> 00:30:05,466
-You have lost the heart 
of Signior Benedick.

670
00:30:05,500 --> 00:30:06,966
-Indeed, my lord.

671
00:30:07,000 --> 00:30:09,633
He lent it me awhile, 
and I gave him use for it,

672
00:30:09,666 --> 00:30:11,800
a double heart 
for his single one.

673
00:30:11,833 --> 00:30:14,833
Marry, once before he won 
it of me with false dice,

674
00:30:14,866 --> 00:30:18,533
therefore your grace 
may well say I have lost it.

675
00:30:18,566 --> 00:30:20,866
-You have put him down, lady. 
You have put him down!

676
00:30:20,900 --> 00:30:22,866
-I would not he should do me, 
my lord,

677
00:30:22,900 --> 00:30:25,266
lest I should prove 
the mother of fools.

678
00:30:25,300 --> 00:30:27,200
-Now come -- 
-I have brought Count Claudio,

679
00:30:27,233 --> 00:30:29,366
whom you sent me to seek.

680
00:30:29,400 --> 00:30:32,733
-Why, how now, count?

681
00:30:32,766 --> 00:30:34,333
Wherefore are you sad?

682
00:30:34,366 --> 00:30:35,700
-Not sad, my lord.

683
00:30:35,733 --> 00:30:37,933
-How then? Sick? 
-Neither, my lord.

684
00:30:37,966 --> 00:30:40,466
-The count is neither sad, 
nor sick, nor merry, nor well,

685
00:30:40,500 --> 00:30:43,666
but civil count, 
civil as an orange,

686
00:30:43,700 --> 00:30:47,166
and something of that 
[whispers] jealous complexion.

687
00:30:47,200 --> 00:30:49,333
-[ Chuckles ] Well, 
in faith, lady,

688
00:30:49,366 --> 00:30:55,033
I'll be sworn, if he be so, 
his conceit is false!

689
00:30:55,066 --> 00:30:57,366
Here, Claudio, 
I have wooed in thy name,

690
00:30:57,400 --> 00:30:59,533
and fair Hero is won.

691
00:30:59,566 --> 00:31:02,466
I have broke with her father 
and his good will obtained.

692
00:31:02,500 --> 00:31:06,866
Name the day of marriage, 
and God give thee joy!

693
00:31:06,900 --> 00:31:14,033
-Count, take of me 
my daughter...

694
00:31:14,066 --> 00:31:17,133
and with her my fortunes.

695
00:31:17,166 --> 00:31:19,966
His grace hath made the match,

696
00:31:20,000 --> 00:31:22,800
and all grace say Amen to it.

697
00:31:22,833 --> 00:31:25,166
-Amen.

698
00:31:32,100 --> 00:31:35,100
[ Cheers and applause ]

699
00:31:39,500 --> 00:31:41,833
[ Laughter ]

700
00:31:41,866 --> 00:31:44,366
[ Cheers and applause ]

701
00:31:52,566 --> 00:31:55,566
-Speak, count. 
'Tis your cue.

702
00:31:58,066 --> 00:32:01,433
-Silence is the perfectest 
herald of joy.

703
00:32:01,466 --> 00:32:04,500
I were but little happy 
if I could say how much.

704
00:32:04,533 --> 00:32:07,466
Lady, as you are mine, 
I am yours.

705
00:32:07,500 --> 00:32:09,066
I give away myself for you

706
00:32:09,100 --> 00:32:11,433
and dote upon the exchange.

707
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:17,100
[ Sighs ]

708
00:32:19,966 --> 00:32:23,333
-Hootie hoo!

709
00:32:23,366 --> 00:32:24,666
Speak, cousin,

710
00:32:24,700 --> 00:32:26,933
or if you cannot, 
stop his mouth with a kiss

711
00:32:26,966 --> 00:32:29,466
and let not him speak neither.

712
00:32:34,200 --> 00:32:36,466
-In faith, lady,

713
00:32:36,500 --> 00:32:38,500
you have a merry heart. 
-Yea, my lord.

714
00:32:38,533 --> 00:32:43,033
I thank it, poor fool, it keeps 
on the windy side of care.

715
00:32:43,066 --> 00:32:45,800
My cousin tells him in his ear 
that he is in her heart.

716
00:32:45,833 --> 00:32:48,333
-And so she doth, cousin.

717
00:32:48,366 --> 00:32:50,833
-Good Lord, for alliance.

718
00:32:50,866 --> 00:32:53,600
Thus goes everyone to the world 
but I.

719
00:32:53,633 --> 00:32:57,133
I may sit in a corner 
and cry heigh-ho for a husband.

720
00:32:57,166 --> 00:32:59,033
-Lady Beatrice,

721
00:32:59,066 --> 00:33:00,633
I will get you one.

722
00:33:00,666 --> 00:33:03,200
-I would rather have one 
of your father's getting.

723
00:33:03,233 --> 00:33:05,566
Hath your grace ne'er a brother 
like you?

724
00:33:05,600 --> 00:33:07,566
Your father's got 
excellent husbands,

725
00:33:07,600 --> 00:33:09,833
if a maid could come by them.

726
00:33:09,866 --> 00:33:13,333
-Will you have me, lady?

727
00:33:13,366 --> 00:33:14,500
-Oh!

728
00:33:14,533 --> 00:33:16,533
[ Grunting ]

729
00:33:20,433 --> 00:33:22,733
No, my lord.

730
00:33:22,766 --> 00:33:26,000
Unless I may have another 
for working days.

731
00:33:26,033 --> 00:33:29,300
Your grace is too costly 
to wear every day,

732
00:33:29,333 --> 00:33:30,900
but I beseech 
your grace, pardon.

733
00:33:30,933 --> 00:33:33,833
I as born to speak all mirth 
and no matter.

734
00:33:33,866 --> 00:33:37,166
[ Sighs deeply ]

735
00:33:37,200 --> 00:33:40,633
-Your silence most offends me,

736
00:33:40,666 --> 00:33:43,333
and to be merry best 
becomes you,

737
00:33:43,366 --> 00:33:46,100
for out of question, 
you were born in a merry hour.

738
00:33:46,133 --> 00:33:49,133
-No, sure, my lord, 
my mother cried,

739
00:33:49,166 --> 00:33:50,533
and then there was 
a star danced,

740
00:33:50,566 --> 00:33:52,133
and under that was I born.

741
00:33:52,166 --> 00:33:56,300
Oh, cousin. 
God give you joy!

742
00:33:56,333 --> 00:33:59,300
-Niece, will you look 
to those things I told you of?

743
00:33:59,333 --> 00:34:02,200
-I cry you mercy, uncle.

744
00:34:02,233 --> 00:34:04,733
[ Sighs ]

745
00:34:04,766 --> 00:34:06,933
By your grace's pardon.

746
00:34:09,566 --> 00:34:10,900
[ Sighs ]

747
00:34:13,100 --> 00:34:17,000
-By my troth, 
a pleasant-spirited lady.

748
00:34:17,033 --> 00:34:18,833
-There is little of 
the melancholy element

749
00:34:18,866 --> 00:34:20,300
in her, my lord.

750
00:34:20,333 --> 00:34:22,333
She is never sad, 
but when she sleeps,

751
00:34:22,366 --> 00:34:23,966
not ever sad then,

752
00:34:24,000 --> 00:34:25,166
for I have heard my daughter say

753
00:34:25,199 --> 00:34:27,500
she hath often dreamt 
of unhappiness

754
00:34:27,533 --> 00:34:30,233
and waked herself with laughing.

755
00:34:30,266 --> 00:34:32,766
-She cannot endure to hear 
tell of a husband.

756
00:34:32,800 --> 00:34:34,500
-Oh, by no means.

757
00:34:34,533 --> 00:34:38,933
She mocks all her wooers 
out of suit.

758
00:34:38,966 --> 00:34:42,600
-She were an excellent wife 
for Benedick.

759
00:34:42,633 --> 00:34:45,666
-Oh, lord -- 
My lord...

760
00:34:45,699 --> 00:34:48,233
If they were but a week married, 
they'd talk themselves mad.

761
00:34:48,266 --> 00:34:50,400
-County Claudio, when mean 
you to go to church?

762
00:34:50,433 --> 00:34:52,000
-Tomorrow, my lord.

763
00:34:52,033 --> 00:34:54,633
Time goes on crutches 
until love have all his rites.

764
00:34:54,666 --> 00:34:55,866
-Not until Monday, my dear son,

765
00:34:55,900 --> 00:34:57,500
which is hence 
a just sevennight,

766
00:34:57,533 --> 00:35:00,266
and a time too brief, too,

767
00:35:00,300 --> 00:35:01,933
to have all things 
answer my mind.

768
00:35:01,966 --> 00:35:03,100
-Come.

769
00:35:03,133 --> 00:35:04,566
You shake the head at so long 
a breathing,

770
00:35:04,600 --> 00:35:06,433
but I warrant thee, Claudio.

771
00:35:06,466 --> 00:35:09,300
The time shall not 
go dully by us.

772
00:35:09,333 --> 00:35:13,133
I will in the interim undertake 
one of Hercules' labors,

773
00:35:13,166 --> 00:35:14,600
which is to bring 
Signior Benedick

774
00:35:14,633 --> 00:35:17,166
and the Lady Beatrice 
into a mountain of affection,

775
00:35:17,200 --> 00:35:18,300
the one with the other.

776
00:35:18,333 --> 00:35:20,433
I would fain have it a match,

777
00:35:20,466 --> 00:35:23,733
and I doubt not but 
to fashion it if you three will

778
00:35:23,766 --> 00:35:26,300
but minister such assistance 
as I shall give you direction.

779
00:35:26,333 --> 00:35:27,600
-My lord, I am for you,

780
00:35:27,633 --> 00:35:30,066
though it cost me 
10 nights' watchings.

781
00:35:30,100 --> 00:35:31,266
-And I, my lord.

782
00:35:31,300 --> 00:35:32,633
-And you, too, gentle Hero?

783
00:35:32,666 --> 00:35:35,266
-I will do any modest office, 
my lord,

784
00:35:35,300 --> 00:35:37,800
to help my cousin 
to a good husband.

785
00:35:37,833 --> 00:35:39,400
-And Benedick is not

786
00:35:39,433 --> 00:35:42,066
the unhopefullest husband 
that I know.

787
00:35:42,100 --> 00:35:43,800
Thus far can I praise him.

788
00:35:43,833 --> 00:35:45,333
He is of a noble strain,

789
00:35:45,366 --> 00:35:48,000
of approved valor 
and confirmed honesty.

790
00:35:48,033 --> 00:35:50,166
I will teach you how 
to humor your cousin,

791
00:35:50,200 --> 00:35:52,266
that she shall fall in love 
with Benedick,

792
00:35:52,300 --> 00:35:55,433
and I, with your two helps, 
will so practice on Benedick

793
00:35:55,466 --> 00:35:58,200
that in despite of his quick wit 
and his queasy stomach,

794
00:35:58,233 --> 00:36:00,833
he shall fall in love 
with Beatrice.

795
00:36:00,866 --> 00:36:03,166
If we can do this,

796
00:36:03,200 --> 00:36:05,000
Cupid is no longer an archer.

797
00:36:05,033 --> 00:36:08,533
His glory shall be ours, 
for we are the only love gods.

798
00:36:08,566 --> 00:36:10,433
[ Applause ]

799
00:36:10,466 --> 00:36:11,733
Go in with me,

800
00:36:11,766 --> 00:36:14,333
and I will tell you 
my drift, huh?

801
00:36:14,366 --> 00:36:22,700
♪♪

802
00:36:22,733 --> 00:36:26,100
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey

803
00:36:26,133 --> 00:36:29,366
♪ Hey, hey, hey, hey

804
00:36:29,400 --> 00:36:33,366
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah

805
00:36:33,400 --> 00:36:37,033
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah

806
00:36:37,066 --> 00:36:40,366
[ Indistinct shouting, 
laughter ]

807
00:36:40,400 --> 00:36:43,066
-Hi. 
-Hey!

808
00:36:43,100 --> 00:36:44,566
I have been waiting 
for this moment.

809
00:36:44,600 --> 00:36:46,033
-For me? 
-All night.

810
00:36:46,066 --> 00:36:47,833
-[ Clears throat ]

811
00:36:47,866 --> 00:36:50,866
♪♪

812
00:36:50,900 --> 00:36:53,533
-[ Giggles ]

813
00:36:53,566 --> 00:36:55,300
-It is so!

814
00:36:55,333 --> 00:36:57,366
Count Claudio shall marry 
the daughter of Leonato.

815
00:36:57,400 --> 00:36:58,966
-Yea, my lord, 
but I can cross it.

816
00:36:59,000 --> 00:37:01,133
-Any bar, any cross,

817
00:37:01,166 --> 00:37:03,866
any impediment 
will be medicinable to me.

818
00:37:03,900 --> 00:37:06,200
I am sick in displeasure to him,

819
00:37:06,233 --> 00:37:08,866
and whatsoever comes 
athwart his affection

820
00:37:08,900 --> 00:37:10,800
ranges evenly with mine.

821
00:37:10,833 --> 00:37:12,200
How canst thou cross 
this marriage?

822
00:37:12,233 --> 00:37:14,933
-Not honestly, my lord, 
but so covertly

823
00:37:14,966 --> 00:37:17,000
that no dishonesty 
shall appear in me.

824
00:37:17,033 --> 00:37:18,666
-Show me briefly how.

825
00:37:18,700 --> 00:37:21,166
-I think I told your lordship 
a year since how much I am

826
00:37:21,200 --> 00:37:22,866
in the favor of Margaret,

827
00:37:22,900 --> 00:37:24,400
the waiting gentlewoman to Hero.

828
00:37:24,433 --> 00:37:27,366
-I remember. 
-I can, at any unseasonable

829
00:37:27,400 --> 00:37:28,733
instant of the night,

830
00:37:28,766 --> 00:37:30,933
appoint her to look out 
at her lady's chamber window.

831
00:37:30,966 --> 00:37:33,300
-What life is in that to be 
the death of this marriage?

832
00:37:33,333 --> 00:37:36,366
-The poison of that lies in you 
to temper.

833
00:37:36,400 --> 00:37:38,533
Go you to the prince, 
your brother.

834
00:37:38,566 --> 00:37:41,900
Spare not to tell him 
that he hath wronged his honor

835
00:37:41,933 --> 00:37:44,233
in marrying 
the renowned Claudio,

836
00:37:44,266 --> 00:37:47,000
whose estimation do you 
mightily hold up,

837
00:37:47,033 --> 00:37:49,833
to a contaminated stale, 
such a one as Hero.

838
00:37:49,866 --> 00:37:51,300
-What proof shall 
I make of that?

839
00:37:51,333 --> 00:37:52,733
-Proof enough to 
misuse the prince,

840
00:37:52,766 --> 00:37:53,933
to vex Claudio,

841
00:37:53,966 --> 00:37:57,266
to undo Hero, and kill Leonato.

842
00:37:57,300 --> 00:37:58,466
Look you for any other issue?

843
00:37:58,500 --> 00:38:00,000
-Only to despite them,

844
00:38:00,033 --> 00:38:02,366
I will endeavor anything. 
-Go then.

845
00:38:02,400 --> 00:38:04,600
Find me a meet hour 
to draw Don Pedro

846
00:38:04,633 --> 00:38:07,000
and the Count Claudio alone.

847
00:38:07,033 --> 00:38:10,800
Tell them that you know 
that Hero loves me.

848
00:38:10,833 --> 00:38:13,800
Intend a kind of zeal both 
to the prince and Claudio,

849
00:38:13,833 --> 00:38:16,600
as in love 
of your brother's honor,

850
00:38:16,633 --> 00:38:18,366
who hath made this match,

851
00:38:18,400 --> 00:38:20,166
and his friend's reputation,

852
00:38:20,200 --> 00:38:23,200
who is thus like to be cozened 
with the semblance of a maid,

853
00:38:23,233 --> 00:38:25,666
that you have discovered thus.

854
00:38:25,700 --> 00:38:28,800
They will scarcely believe this 
without trial.

855
00:38:28,833 --> 00:38:32,666
Offer them instances which 
shall bear no less likelihood

856
00:38:32,700 --> 00:38:35,300
than to see me 
at her chamber window.

857
00:38:35,333 --> 00:38:38,300
Hear me call Margaret Hero,

858
00:38:38,333 --> 00:38:39,500
and bring them to see this

859
00:38:39,533 --> 00:38:41,733
the very night before 
the intended wedding,

860
00:38:41,766 --> 00:38:43,100
for in the meantime,

861
00:38:43,133 --> 00:38:47,033
I will so fashion the matter 
that Hero shall be absent,

862
00:38:47,066 --> 00:38:50,466
and there shall appear 
such seeming truth

863
00:38:50,500 --> 00:38:52,166
to Hero's disloyalty

864
00:38:52,200 --> 00:38:54,333
that jealousy shall be 
called assurance

865
00:38:54,366 --> 00:38:57,666
and all the preparation 
overthrown.

866
00:38:57,700 --> 00:39:00,266
-Be cunning in the working this

867
00:39:00,300 --> 00:39:01,800
and thy fee is 
a thousand ducats.

868
00:39:01,833 --> 00:39:03,700
-Be you constant 
in the accusation,

869
00:39:03,733 --> 00:39:06,000
and my cunning 
shall not shame me.

870
00:39:06,033 --> 00:39:08,800
-I will presently go learn 
their day of marriage.

871
00:39:08,833 --> 00:39:10,800
[ Laughs ]

872
00:39:10,833 --> 00:39:13,333
-I do much wonder that one man,

873
00:39:13,366 --> 00:39:16,333
seeing how much another man 
is a fool

874
00:39:16,366 --> 00:39:18,566
when he dedicates 
his behaviors to love,

875
00:39:18,600 --> 00:39:20,733
will, after he hath laughed

876
00:39:20,766 --> 00:39:22,900
at such shallow follies 
in others,

877
00:39:22,933 --> 00:39:25,400
become the argument 
of his own scorn

878
00:39:25,433 --> 00:39:28,133
by falling in love.

879
00:39:28,166 --> 00:39:30,366
Such a man is Claudio.

880
00:39:30,400 --> 00:39:32,833
He was won't to speak plain 
and to the purpose,

881
00:39:32,866 --> 00:39:35,366
like an honest man 
and a soldier,

882
00:39:35,400 --> 00:39:38,600
and now is 
he turned orthography.

883
00:39:38,633 --> 00:39:42,900
His words are a very 
fantastical banquet,

884
00:39:42,933 --> 00:39:45,966
just so many strange dishes.

885
00:39:46,000 --> 00:39:49,166
May I be so converted 
and see with these eyes?

886
00:39:49,200 --> 00:39:51,566
I think not. 
I cannot tell.

887
00:39:51,600 --> 00:39:53,033
I will not be sworn,

888
00:39:53,066 --> 00:39:56,866
but love may transform me 
to an oyster,

889
00:39:56,900 --> 00:39:58,400
but I'll take my oath on it.

890
00:39:58,433 --> 00:40:00,500
Till he hath made an oyster 
of me,

891
00:40:00,533 --> 00:40:03,733
he shall never make me 
such a fool.

892
00:40:03,766 --> 00:40:06,066
One woman is fair,

893
00:40:06,100 --> 00:40:08,000
yet I am well.

894
00:40:08,033 --> 00:40:11,300
Another is wise, 
yet I am well.

895
00:40:11,333 --> 00:40:15,266
Another virtuous, 
yet I am well,

896
00:40:15,300 --> 00:40:18,233
but until all graces 
be in one woman,

897
00:40:18,266 --> 00:40:22,433
one woman shall not 
come in my grace.

898
00:40:22,466 --> 00:40:26,600
Rich she shall be, 
that's certain,

899
00:40:26,633 --> 00:40:29,433
wise or I'll none,

900
00:40:29,466 --> 00:40:32,966
virtuous 
or I'll never cheapen her,

901
00:40:33,000 --> 00:40:36,000
fair or I'll never look on her,

902
00:40:36,033 --> 00:40:39,133
mild or come not near me,

903
00:40:39,166 --> 00:40:42,633
noble or not I for an angel,

904
00:40:42,666 --> 00:40:44,300
