993
00:44:52,600 --> 00:44:54,733
-By my troth, my lord, 
I cannot tell what to make of it

994
00:44:54,766 --> 00:44:58,200
but that she loves him 
with an enraged affection.

995
00:44:58,233 --> 00:45:00,300
It is past the infinite 
of thought.

996
00:45:00,333 --> 00:45:02,300
-Kobe!

997
00:45:02,333 --> 00:45:04,500
[ Laughter ]

998
00:45:08,533 --> 00:45:11,933
-Maybe she doth 
but counterfeit.

999
00:45:11,966 --> 00:45:14,033
-Faith, like enough. 
-Oh, God, counterfeit.

1000
00:45:14,066 --> 00:45:15,866
There was never counterfeit 
of passion

1001
00:45:15,900 --> 00:45:18,933
came so near the life of passion 
as she discovers it.

1002
00:45:18,966 --> 00:45:22,400
-Why, what effects 
of passion shows she?

1003
00:45:22,433 --> 00:45:23,500
-Bait the hook well.

1004
00:45:23,533 --> 00:45:25,000
This fish will bite.

1005
00:45:25,033 --> 00:45:26,866
-What effects, my lord?

1006
00:45:28,900 --> 00:45:31,366
Uh...

1007
00:45:31,400 --> 00:45:35,066
She -- She will sit you,

1008
00:45:35,100 --> 00:45:38,600
You heard my daughter 
tell you how.

1009
00:45:40,833 --> 00:45:42,800
-She did, indeed.

1010
00:45:42,833 --> 00:45:45,666
-But

1011
00:45:42,833 --> 00:45:45,666
how?

1012
00:45:45,700 --> 00:45:47,633
How?!

1013
00:45:47,666 --> 00:45:49,766
I pray you.

1014
00:45:49,800 --> 00:45:51,666
You amaze me.

1015
00:45:51,700 --> 00:45:55,200
I would have thought her spirit 
had been invincible

1016
00:45:55,233 --> 00:45:57,133
against all assaults 
of affection.

1017
00:45:57,166 --> 00:45:58,666
-I would have sworn it had, 
my lord,

1018
00:45:58,700 --> 00:46:01,433
especially against Benedick.

1019
00:46:07,300 --> 00:46:10,400
-He hath ta'en the infection. 
Hold it up.

1020
00:46:10,433 --> 00:46:12,966
-Hath she made her affection 
known to Benedick?

1021
00:46:13,000 --> 00:46:16,400
-No, swears she never will. 
That's her torment.

1022
00:46:16,433 --> 00:46:18,700
-Tis true indeed, 
so your daughter says.

1023
00:46:18,733 --> 00:46:19,933
"Shall I," she says,

1024
00:46:19,966 --> 00:46:22,033
"that have so oft 
encountered him with scorn,

1025
00:46:22,066 --> 00:46:23,600
write to him that I love him?"

1026
00:46:23,633 --> 00:46:26,566
-This says she now when she is 
beginning to write to him,

1027
00:46:26,600 --> 00:46:29,366
for she'll be up 
20 times a night,

1028
00:46:29,400 --> 00:46:31,133
and there will she sit 
in her smock

1029
00:46:31,166 --> 00:46:33,266
until she hath writ 
a sheet of paper.

1030
00:46:33,300 --> 00:46:34,400
My daughter tell us all.

1031
00:46:34,433 --> 00:46:36,366
-And know you talk 
of a sheet of paper,

1032
00:46:36,400 --> 00:46:39,400
I remember a pretty jest 
your daughter told us of.

1033
00:46:39,433 --> 00:46:41,533
-Oh?

1034
00:46:41,566 --> 00:46:42,666
Um...

1035
00:46:42,700 --> 00:46:46,400
When she had writ it 
and was reading it over,

1036
00:46:46,433 --> 00:46:49,966
she found Benedick and Beatrice

1037
00:46:50,000 --> 00:46:51,866
between the sheets.

1038
00:46:51,900 --> 00:46:53,966
-That. 
-Oh!

1039
00:46:54,000 --> 00:46:57,333
She ripped the letter 
into a thousand halfpence,

1040
00:46:57,366 --> 00:47:00,666
railed at herself 
that she should be so immodest

1041
00:47:00,700 --> 00:47:04,133
to write to one 
that she knew would flout her.

1042
00:47:04,166 --> 00:47:07,000
"I measure him," says she,

1043
00:47:07,033 --> 00:47:10,500
"by my own spirit.

1044
00:47:10,533 --> 00:47:14,766
I should flout him 
if he writ to me.

1045
00:47:14,800 --> 00:47:18,800
Yea, though I love him,

1046
00:47:18,833 --> 00:47:20,466
I should."

1047
00:47:20,500 --> 00:47:24,266
-Then down upon her knees 
she falls, weeps...

1048
00:47:24,300 --> 00:47:25,266
-[ Sobbing ]

1049
00:47:25,300 --> 00:47:27,500
-...sobs, beats her heart,

1050
00:47:27,533 --> 00:47:31,633
tears her hair, prays, curses,

1051
00:47:31,666 --> 00:47:33,566
"Oh, sweet Benedick!

1052
00:47:33,600 --> 00:47:35,700
God give me patience!"

1053
00:47:35,733 --> 00:47:38,600
-She doth, indeed. 
-[ Chuckles ]

1054
00:47:38,633 --> 00:47:40,500
-My daughter says so,

1055
00:47:40,533 --> 00:47:44,300
and the ecstasy hath 
so much overborne her

1056
00:47:44,333 --> 00:47:45,733
that my daughter 
is sometimes afeared

1057
00:47:45,766 --> 00:47:47,966
she may do a desperate outrage 
to herself.

1058
00:47:48,000 --> 00:47:49,300
-It is very true.

1059
00:47:49,333 --> 00:47:52,166
It were good that Benedick 
knew of it by some other

1060
00:47:52,200 --> 00:47:54,366
if she will not discover it. 
-To what end?

1061
00:47:54,400 --> 00:47:57,166
He will but make a sport of it 
and torment the poor lady worse.

1062
00:47:57,200 --> 00:47:59,166
-And he should, 
it were an alms to hang him.

1063
00:47:59,200 --> 00:48:01,433
She's an excellent, sweet lady,

1064
00:48:01,466 --> 00:48:03,700
and out of all suspicion, 
she is virtuous.

1065
00:48:03,733 --> 00:48:05,400
-And she is exceeding wise.

1066
00:48:05,433 --> 00:48:07,833
-In everything 
but in loving Benedick.

1067
00:48:07,866 --> 00:48:10,300
-Mm.

1068
00:48:10,333 --> 00:48:12,766
-I'm sorry for her, 
as I have just cause,

1069
00:48:12,800 --> 00:48:14,633
being her uncle 
and her guardian.

1070
00:48:14,666 --> 00:48:17,933
-I would she had bestowed 
this dotage on me.

1071
00:48:17,966 --> 00:48:21,266
I pray you, tell Benedick of it 
and hear what he will say.

1072
00:48:21,300 --> 00:48:22,433
-Were it good, think you?

1073
00:48:22,466 --> 00:48:23,866
-Never tell him, my lord.

1074
00:48:23,900 --> 00:48:25,833
Let her wear it out 
with good counsel.

1075
00:48:25,866 --> 00:48:27,800
-Nay, that's impossible.

1076
00:48:27,833 --> 00:48:30,166
She may wear her heart out 
first.

1077
00:48:30,200 --> 00:48:31,366
-What?

1078
00:48:33,066 --> 00:48:34,900
-[ Chuckles ]

1079
00:48:34,933 --> 00:48:38,500
-Well, we will hear further 
of it by your daughter.

1080
00:48:38,533 --> 00:48:40,066
Let it cool the while.

1081
00:48:40,100 --> 00:48:42,533
I love Benedick well, 
and I could wish he would

1082
00:48:42,566 --> 00:48:45,533
modestly examine himself 
to see how much he is

1083
00:48:45,566 --> 00:48:47,833
unworthy so good a lady.

1084
00:48:47,866 --> 00:48:51,533
-My lord, will you walk? 
Dinner is ready.

1085
00:48:51,566 --> 00:48:53,466
-If he do not dote on her 
upon this,

1086
00:48:53,500 --> 00:48:55,300
I will never trust 
my expectation.

1087
00:48:55,333 --> 00:48:56,800
-Let there be the same 
net spread for her,

1088
00:48:56,833 --> 00:48:59,533
and that must your daughter 
and her gentlewomen carry.

1089
00:48:59,566 --> 00:49:02,066
The sport will be, 
when they hold one

1090
00:49:02,100 --> 00:49:05,566
an opinion of another's dotage 
and no such matter.

1091
00:49:05,600 --> 00:49:07,600
Let us send her to call him in 
to dinner.

1092
00:49:07,633 --> 00:49:09,300
-[ Laughs ]

1093
00:49:17,300 --> 00:49:19,300
-This can be no trick.

1094
00:49:22,066 --> 00:49:24,433
The conference was sadly borne.

1095
00:49:24,466 --> 00:49:26,666
They have the truth of this 
from Hero.

1096
00:49:26,700 --> 00:49:29,666
They seem to pity the lady.

1097
00:49:29,700 --> 00:49:33,800
It seems her affections 
have their full bent.

1098
00:49:33,833 --> 00:49:36,500
Love me!

1099
00:49:36,533 --> 00:49:38,666
Why, it must be requited.

1100
00:49:38,700 --> 00:49:41,100
I hear how I am censured.

1101
00:49:41,133 --> 00:49:43,633
They say I will bear myself 
proudly,

1102
00:49:43,666 --> 00:49:46,500
if I perceive the love 
come from her.

1103
00:49:46,533 --> 00:49:48,200
They say, too, that 
she will rather die

1104
00:49:48,233 --> 00:49:50,133
than give any sign of affection.

1105
00:49:50,166 --> 00:49:52,033
I did never think to marry.

1106
00:49:52,066 --> 00:49:53,633
I must not seem proud.

1107
00:49:53,666 --> 00:49:55,866
Happy are they that 
hear their detractions

1108
00:49:55,900 --> 00:49:58,100
and can put them to mending.

1109
00:49:58,133 --> 00:50:01,466
They say the lady is fair. 
'Tis a truth.

1110
00:50:01,500 --> 00:50:03,600
I can bear them witness!

1111
00:50:03,633 --> 00:50:05,166
And virtuous --

1112
00:50:05,200 --> 00:50:07,233
'Tis so, I cannot reprove it.

1113
00:50:07,266 --> 00:50:10,166
And wise, but for loving me --

1114
00:50:10,200 --> 00:50:13,466
by my troth, 
it is no addition to her wit,

1115
00:50:13,500 --> 00:50:15,533
nor no great argument 
of her folly,

1116
00:50:15,566 --> 00:50:17,533
for I will be...

1117
00:50:17,566 --> 00:50:20,066
horribly in love with her.

1118
00:50:21,966 --> 00:50:24,100
I may chance have 
some odd quirks

1119
00:50:24,133 --> 00:50:25,700
and remnants of wit broken on me

1120
00:50:25,733 --> 00:50:29,300
because I've railed 
so long against marriage,

1121
00:50:29,333 --> 00:50:33,600
but doth not the appetite alter?

1122
00:50:33,633 --> 00:50:35,633
A man loves the meat 
in his youth

1123
00:50:35,666 --> 00:50:38,200
that he cannot endure 
in his age.

1124
00:50:38,233 --> 00:50:39,733
Shall quips and sentences

1125
00:50:39,766 --> 00:50:42,933
and these paper bullets 
of the brain awe a man

1126
00:50:42,966 --> 00:50:46,633
from the career of his humor?

1127
00:50:46,666 --> 00:50:48,933
No!

1128
00:50:48,966 --> 00:50:51,533
The world must be peopled.

1129
00:50:54,033 --> 00:50:57,566
When I said 
I would die a bachelor,

1130
00:50:57,600 --> 00:51:02,166
I did not think I should live 
till I were married.

1131
00:51:02,200 --> 00:51:03,766
Here comes Beatrice.

1132
00:51:03,800 --> 00:51:06,866
By this day, 
she's a fair lady.

1133
00:51:06,900 --> 00:51:09,700
I do spy some marks of love 
in her.

1134
00:51:09,733 --> 00:51:12,700
[ Grunting ] Million-one, 
million-two, million-three,

1135
00:51:12,733 --> 00:51:16,000
million-four, million-five,

1136
00:51:16,033 --> 00:51:19,066
million-six, million-seven, 
million-eight...

1137
00:51:19,100 --> 00:51:20,233
-Against my will,

1138
00:51:20,266 --> 00:51:22,433
I am sent to bid you 
come in to dinner.

1139
00:51:22,466 --> 00:51:27,066
-Fair Beatrice, 
I thank you for your pains.

1140
00:51:27,100 --> 00:51:30,033
[ Laughter ]

1141
00:51:30,066 --> 00:51:32,533
-I took no more pains 
for those thanks

1142
00:51:32,566 --> 00:51:34,700
than you take pains to thank me.

1143
00:51:34,733 --> 00:51:38,433
If it had been painful, 
I would not have come.

1144
00:51:38,466 --> 00:51:40,933
-You take pleasure then...

1145
00:51:40,966 --> 00:51:42,300
in the message?

1146
00:51:42,333 --> 00:51:45,466
-Yea, just so much as you may 
take upon a knife's point

1147
00:51:45,500 --> 00:51:47,700
and choke a daw withal.

1148
00:51:47,733 --> 00:51:50,766
You have no stomach, signior. 
Fare you well.

1149
00:51:52,933 --> 00:51:56,566
-Ooh!

1150
00:51:56,600 --> 00:51:58,333
"Against my will

1151
00:51:58,366 --> 00:52:00,200
I am sent to bid you

1152
00:52:00,233 --> 00:52:03,333
come in to dinner."

1153
00:52:03,366 --> 00:52:06,933
There's a double meaning 
in that.

1154
00:52:06,966 --> 00:52:09,033
"I took no more pains 
for those thanks

1155
00:52:09,066 --> 00:52:11,300
than you took pains 
to thank me."

1156
00:52:11,333 --> 00:52:13,166
That's as much to say 
that any pains

1157
00:52:13,200 --> 00:52:14,866
I take for you

1158
00:52:14,900 --> 00:52:18,766
is as easy as thanks.

1159
00:52:18,800 --> 00:52:22,133
If I do not take pity of her, 
I am a villain.

1160
00:52:22,166 --> 00:52:24,500
I will go get her picture.

1161
00:52:26,233 --> 00:52:29,700
[ Cheers and applause ]

1162
00:52:29,733 --> 00:52:31,733
-Good Margaret.

1163
00:52:35,900 --> 00:52:37,500
Good Margaret.

1164
00:52:41,366 --> 00:52:42,666
Run thee to the parlor.

1165
00:52:42,700 --> 00:52:44,266
There shalt thou find 
my cousin, Beatrice,

1166
00:52:44,300 --> 00:52:46,266
conversing with the prince 
and Claudio.

1167
00:52:46,300 --> 00:52:49,366
Whisper her ear and tell her 
I and Ursula walk in the orchard

1168
00:52:49,400 --> 00:52:52,800
and our whole discourse 
is all of her.

1169
00:52:52,833 --> 00:52:54,333
Say that thou overheardst us,

1170
00:52:54,366 --> 00:52:56,500
and bid her steal 
into the pleached bower.

1171
00:52:56,533 --> 00:52:57,833
There will she hide her.

1172
00:52:57,866 --> 00:53:01,100
-I'll make her come, 
I warrant you, presently.

1173
00:53:01,133 --> 00:53:03,800
-Now, Ursula, 
when Beatrice doth come,

1174
00:53:03,833 --> 00:53:06,666
our talk must only 
be of Benedick.

1175
00:53:06,700 --> 00:53:09,100
When I do name him, 
let it be thy part to praise him

1176
00:53:09,133 --> 00:53:12,366
more than ever man did merit.

1177
00:53:12,400 --> 00:53:13,800
My talk to thee must be

1178
00:53:13,833 --> 00:53:18,066
how Benedick is sick in love 
with Beatrice.

1179
00:53:18,100 --> 00:53:20,833
Of this matter is little Cupid's 
crafty arrow made

1180
00:53:20,866 --> 00:53:23,100
that only wounds by hearsay.

1181
00:53:23,133 --> 00:53:24,800
[ Both chuckle ]

1182
00:53:24,833 --> 00:53:26,733
-Ooh!

1183
00:53:26,766 --> 00:53:28,433
Now begin,

1184
00:53:28,466 --> 00:53:29,900
for look where Beatrice, 
like a lapwing,

1185
00:53:29,933 --> 00:53:32,333
runs close by the ground 
to hear our conference.

1186
00:53:32,366 --> 00:53:35,933
-The pleasant'st angling 
is to the see fish cut

1187
00:53:35,966 --> 00:53:38,466
with her golden oars 
the silver stream

1188
00:53:38,500 --> 00:53:41,300
and greedily devour 
the treacherous bait.

1189
00:53:41,333 --> 00:53:44,300
-Then go we near her, 
that her ear lose nothing

1190
00:53:44,333 --> 00:53:47,666
of the false sweet bait 
that we lay for it.

1191
00:53:50,466 --> 00:53:53,866
No, truly, Ursula, 
she is too disdainful.

1192
00:53:53,900 --> 00:54:00,233
-But are you sure that Benedick 
loves Beatrice so entirely?

1193
00:54:00,266 --> 00:54:02,366
-So says the prince 
and my new-trothed lord.

1194
00:54:02,400 --> 00:54:04,266
-And did they bid you 
tell her of it, madam?

1195
00:54:04,300 --> 00:54:06,400
-They did entreat me 
to acquaint her of it,

1196
00:54:06,433 --> 00:54:08,400
but I persuaded them, 
if they loved Benedick,

1197
00:54:08,433 --> 00:54:10,200
to wish him wrestle 
with affection

1198
00:54:10,233 --> 00:54:12,433
and never to let Beatrice 
know of it.

1199
00:54:12,466 --> 00:54:14,266
-Why did you so?

1200
00:54:14,300 --> 00:54:16,800
Doth not the gentleman 
deserve as full,

1201
00:54:16,833 --> 00:54:20,000
as fortunate a bed 
as ever Beatrice

1202
00:54:20,033 --> 00:54:21,066
shall couch upon?

1203
00:54:21,100 --> 00:54:24,466
-Oh, god of love!

1204
00:54:24,500 --> 00:54:28,566
I know he doth deserve as much 
as may be yielded to a man,

1205
00:54:28,600 --> 00:54:32,466
but nature never framed 
a woman's heart of prouder stuff

1206
00:54:32,500 --> 00:54:34,066
than that of Beatrice.

1207
00:54:34,100 --> 00:54:37,366
Disdain and scorn ride 
sparkling in her eyes,

1208
00:54:37,400 --> 00:54:39,100
misprising what they look on,

1209
00:54:39,133 --> 00:54:42,666
and her wit [chuckles] values 
itself so highly that to her,

1210
00:54:42,700 --> 00:54:44,366
all matter else seems weak.

1211
00:54:44,400 --> 00:54:46,100
She cannot love,

1212
00:54:46,133 --> 00:54:48,366
nor take no shape nor project 
of affection.

1213
00:54:48,400 --> 00:54:50,366
She is so self-endeared.

1214
00:54:50,400 --> 00:54:53,300
[ Laughter ]

1215
00:54:53,333 --> 00:54:55,166
-Sure, I think so,

1216
00:54:55,200 --> 00:54:57,900
and therefore certainly it were 
not good she knew his love,

1217
00:54:57,933 --> 00:54:59,533
lest she'll make sport at it.

1218
00:54:59,566 --> 00:55:01,533
-Why, you speak truth.

1219
00:55:01,566 --> 00:55:06,033
I never yet saw a man, 
how wise, how noble, young,

1220
00:55:06,066 --> 00:55:07,633
how rarely featured,

1221
00:55:07,666 --> 00:55:10,266
but she would 
spell him backward.

1222
00:55:10,300 --> 00:55:12,433
If fair-faced, she would 
swear the gentleman

1223
00:55:12,466 --> 00:55:14,066
should be her sister.

1224
00:55:14,100 --> 00:55:18,933
If tall, a Lance ill-headed.

1225
00:55:18,966 --> 00:55:22,833
If low, an agate, 
very viley cut,

1226
00:55:22,866 --> 00:55:26,000
If speaking, like a vane 
blown with all winds.

1227
00:55:26,033 --> 00:55:29,500
If silent, why a block 
moved with none.

1228
00:55:29,533 --> 00:55:33,366
So turns she every man 
the wrong side out

1229
00:55:33,400 --> 00:55:35,033
and never gives 
to truth and virtue

1230
00:55:35,066 --> 00:55:37,933
that which simpleness 
and merit purchaseth.

1231
00:55:37,966 --> 00:55:39,100
-Sure, sure.

1232
00:55:39,133 --> 00:55:41,666
Such carping is not commendable.

1233
00:55:41,700 --> 00:55:44,266
-No, not to be so odd

1234
00:55:44,300 --> 00:55:46,433
and from all fashions 
as Beatrice is

1235
00:55:46,466 --> 00:55:48,166
cannot be commendable,

1236
00:55:48,200 --> 00:55:49,800
but who dare tell her so?

1237
00:55:49,833 --> 00:55:52,933
If I should speak, 
she would mock me into air.

1238
00:55:52,966 --> 00:55:54,066
[ Chuckling ] Oh!

1239
00:55:54,100 --> 00:55:56,800
She would laugh me 
out of myself,

1240
00:55:56,833 --> 00:55:59,900
press me to death with wit.

1241
00:55:59,933 --> 00:56:04,400
Therefore, let Benedick, 
like covered fire,

1242
00:56:04,433 --> 00:56:06,833
consume away in sighs,

1243
00:56:06,866 --> 00:56:08,966
waste inwardly.

1244
00:56:09,000 --> 00:56:10,666
It were a better death 
than die with mocks,

1245
00:56:10,700 --> 00:56:13,233
which is as bad 
as die with tickling.

1246
00:56:13,266 --> 00:56:14,966
-Yet tell her of it.

1247
00:56:15,000 --> 00:56:16,833
Hear what she will say. 
-No.

1248
00:56:16,866 --> 00:56:18,833
Rather, I will go to Benedick

1249
00:56:18,866 --> 00:56:21,533
and counsel him to fight 
against his passion,

1250
00:56:21,566 --> 00:56:25,266
and truly, I'll devise 
some honest slanders

1251
00:56:25,300 --> 00:56:27,233
to stain my cousin with.

1252
00:56:27,266 --> 00:56:31,133
One doth not know how much 
an ill word may empoison liking.

1253
00:56:31,166 --> 00:56:34,466
-Oh, do not do your cousin 
such a wrong.

1254
00:56:34,500 --> 00:56:36,800
-That's what I'm saying!

1255
00:56:36,833 --> 00:56:40,566
-She cannot be so much 
without true judgment,

1256
00:56:40,600 --> 00:56:43,400
having so swift 
and excellent a wit

1257
00:56:43,433 --> 00:56:44,800
as she is prized to have,

1258
00:56:44,833 --> 00:56:47,433
as to refuse so rare a gentleman

1259
00:56:47,466 --> 00:56:49,166
as Signior Benedick.

1260
00:56:49,200 --> 00:56:52,766
-He is the only man. 
-Ah!

1261
00:56:52,800 --> 00:56:55,266
-Always excepting 
my dear Claudio.

1262
00:56:55,300 --> 00:56:57,200
-I pray you, 
be not angry with me,

1263
00:56:57,233 --> 00:56:59,033
madam, speaking my fancy.

1264
00:56:59,066 --> 00:57:03,266
Signior Benedick, for shape, 
for bearing, argument,

1265
00:57:03,300 --> 00:57:04,733
and valor,

1266
00:57:04,766 --> 00:57:06,800
goes foremost in report.

1267
00:57:06,833 --> 00:57:10,766
-Indeed! 
He hath an excellent good name.

1268
00:57:10,800 --> 00:57:12,700
-His excellence did earn it,

1269
00:57:12,733 --> 00:57:14,300
ere he had it.

1270
00:57:14,333 --> 00:57:15,666
[ Laughter ]

1271
00:57:15,700 --> 00:57:17,500
Wait, when are you 
married, madam?

1272
00:57:17,533 --> 00:57:20,433
-Why, every day, tomorrow.

1273
00:57:20,466 --> 00:57:22,066
Come, go in.

1274
00:57:22,100 --> 00:57:25,166
I'll show thee some attires, 
and have thy counsel,

1275
00:57:25,200 --> 00:57:27,366
which is the best 
to furnish me tomorrow.

1276
00:57:27,400 --> 00:57:28,466
-Ooh!

1277
00:57:28,500 --> 00:57:29,666
-[ Chuckles ]

1278
00:57:29,700 --> 00:57:32,700
-[ Groans ]

1279
00:57:32,733 --> 00:57:35,033
-She's limed, I warrant you.

1280
00:57:35,066 --> 00:57:36,900
We have caught her, madam.

1281
00:57:36,933 --> 00:57:39,933
-If it proves so, 
then loving goes by haps.

1282
00:57:39,966 --> 00:57:41,666
Some Cupid kills with arrows,

1283
00:57:41,700 --> 00:57:43,233
some with...

1284
00:57:43,266 --> 00:57:44,800
traps.

1285
00:57:44,833 --> 00:57:47,500
-Ha!

1286
00:57:47,533 --> 00:57:49,833
[ Cheers and applause ]

1287
00:57:54,433 --> 00:57:55,800
-[ Sighs ]

1288
00:57:55,833 --> 00:57:59,533
What fire is in mine ears?

1289
00:57:59,566 --> 00:58:02,366
Can this be true?

1290
00:58:02,400 --> 00:58:04,166
Stand I...

1291
00:58:04,200 --> 00:58:05,600
condemned for pride

1292
00:58:05,633 --> 00:58:08,600
and scorn so much?

1293
00:58:08,633 --> 00:58:10,600
[ Sighs deeply ]

1294
00:58:10,633 --> 00:58:13,733
Contempt, farewell.

1295
00:58:13,766 --> 00:58:16,333
Maiden pride, adieu.

1296
00:58:16,366 --> 00:58:20,266
No glory lives 
behind the back of such.

1297
00:58:20,300 --> 00:58:21,533
[ Chuckles ]

1298
00:58:21,566 --> 00:58:25,533
And Benedick, love on --

1299
00:58:25,566 --> 00:58:27,266
I will requite thee,

1300
00:58:27,300 --> 00:58:32,300
taming my wild heart 
to thy loving hand.

1301
00:58:32,333 --> 00:58:34,700
If thou dost love,

1302
00:58:34,733 --> 00:58:37,466
my kindness shall incite thee

1303
00:58:37,500 --> 00:58:41,300
to bind our loves up 
in a holy band

1304
00:58:41,333 --> 00:58:44,233
for others say 
thou dost deserve,

1305
00:58:44,266 --> 00:58:47,433
and I believe it better 
than reportingly.

1306
00:58:47,466 --> 00:58:49,433
Aaaah!

1307
00:58:49,466 --> 00:58:55,833
♪♪

1308
00:58:55,866 --> 00:58:57,600
♪ Hey, hey

1309
00:58:57,633 --> 00:59:00,033
♪ No, no, no, no, no

1310
00:59:00,066 --> 00:59:01,566
♪ Yeah

1311
00:59:01,600 --> 00:59:03,600
♪ Yeah

1312
00:59:03,633 --> 00:59:07,400
♪ Yeah, yeah, yeah, 
yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah ♪

1313
00:59:07,433 --> 00:59:09,400
♪ Hey

1314
00:59:09,433 --> 00:59:11,900
♪♪

1315
00:59:11,933 --> 00:59:15,966
[ Cheers and applause ]

1316
00:59:16,000 --> 00:59:21,466
Gallants, 
I am not as I have been.

1317
00:59:21,500 --> 00:59:22,900
-So say I.

1318
00:59:22,933 --> 00:59:24,400
Methinks you are sadder.

1319
00:59:24,433 --> 00:59:25,533
-[ Laughs ]

1320
00:59:25,566 --> 00:59:28,233
-I hope he be in love. 
-Hang him, truant.

1321
00:59:28,266 --> 00:59:29,966
There is no true drop of blood 
in him

1322
00:59:30,000 --> 00:59:31,800
to be truly touched with love.

1323
00:59:31,833 --> 00:59:34,633
If he be sad, he wants money.

1324
00:59:34,666 --> 00:59:36,300
-If he be not in love 
with some woman,

1325
00:59:36,333 --> 00:59:38,333
there is no believing old signs.

1326
00:59:38,366 --> 00:59:40,133
He brushes his hat 
on the mornings.

1327
00:59:40,166 --> 00:59:41,233
What should that bode?

1328
00:59:41,266 --> 00:59:43,033
-Has any man seen him 
at the barber's?

1329
00:59:43,066 --> 00:59:46,866
-No, but the barber's man 
has been seen with him.

1330
00:59:46,900 --> 00:59:48,466
-Ooh.

1331
00:59:48,500 --> 00:59:50,733
-And the old ornament 
of his cheek hath already

1332
00:59:50,766 --> 00:59:52,166
stuffed tennis balls.

1333
00:59:52,200 --> 00:59:54,166
-Indeed, 
he looks younger than he did

1334
00:59:54,200 --> 00:59:55,933
by the loss of a beard.

1335
00:59:55,966 --> 00:59:58,100
-Nay, he rubs himself 
with civet.

1336
00:59:58,133 --> 00:59:59,800
Can you smell him out by that?

1337
00:59:59,833 --> 01:00:02,666
-[ Sniffs ] Ew!

1338
01:00:02,700 --> 01:00:04,100
That's as much as to say.

1339
01:00:04,133 --> 01:00:05,466
The sweet youth is in love.

1340
01:00:05,500 --> 01:00:07,766
-The greatest note of it 
is his melancholy.

1341
01:00:07,800 --> 01:00:09,700
-And when was he wont 
to wash his face?

1342
01:00:09,733 --> 01:00:12,933
-Yea, or to paint himself?

1343
01:00:12,966 --> 01:00:14,333
Conclude!

1344
01:00:14,366 --> 01:00:15,800
Conclude he is in love.

1345
01:00:15,833 --> 01:00:19,333
-Nay, but I know who loves him.

1346
01:00:19,366 --> 01:00:21,233
-That one I know, too.

1347
01:00:21,266 --> 01:00:23,733
-Oh, Signor, 
walk aside with me.

1348
01:00:23,766 --> 01:00:25,533
I have studied eight 
or nine wise words

1349
01:00:25,566 --> 01:00:28,166
to speak to you which 
these hobbyhorses

1350
01:00:28,200 --> 01:00:30,033
must not hear.

1351
01:00:38,666 --> 01:00:40,900
-For my life, to break 
with him about Beatrice!

1352
01:00:40,933 --> 01:00:41,966
-'Tis even so.

1353
01:00:42,000 --> 01:00:43,200
Hero and Margaret have by this

1354
01:00:43,233 --> 01:00:44,766
played their parts 
with Beatrice,

1355
01:00:44,800 --> 01:00:47,533
and then the two bears will not 
bite one another when they meet.

1356
01:00:47,566 --> 01:00:50,366
-My lord and brother, 
God save you.

1357
01:00:50,400 --> 01:00:51,466
-Good evening, brother.

1358
01:00:51,500 --> 01:00:52,900
-If your leisure serves,

1359
01:00:52,933 --> 01:00:55,000
I would speak with you. 
-In private?

1360
01:00:55,033 --> 01:00:57,266
-If it please you, 
yet Count Claudio may hear,

1361
01:00:57,300 --> 01:00:59,266
for what I would speak of 
concerns him.

1362
01:00:59,300 --> 01:01:00,566
-What's the matter?

1363
01:01:00,600 --> 01:01:02,900
-Means your lordship 
to be married tomorrow?

1364
01:01:02,933 --> 01:01:04,866
-You know he does. 
-I know not that

1365
01:01:04,900 --> 01:01:06,533
when he knows what I know.

1366
01:01:06,566 --> 01:01:08,933
-If there be any impediment, 
I pray you discover it.

1367
01:01:08,966 --> 01:01:10,766
-You may think I love you not.

1368
01:01:10,800 --> 01:01:12,633
Let that appear hereafter,

1369
01:01:12,666 --> 01:01:15,833
and aim better at me 
by that I now manifest.

1370
01:01:15,866 --> 01:01:18,600
For my brother, 
I think he holds you well

1371
01:01:18,633 --> 01:01:20,266
and in dearness of heart

1372
01:01:20,300 --> 01:01:23,066
hath hoped to affect 
your ensuing marriage,

1373
01:01:23,100 --> 01:01:25,400
surely suit ill spent 
and labor ill bestowed.

1374
01:01:25,433 --> 01:01:28,733
-What's the matter? 
-I came hither to tell you

1375
01:01:28,766 --> 01:01:30,566
the lady is disloyal.

1376
01:01:30,600 --> 01:01:31,700
-Who, Hero?

1377
01:01:31,733 --> 01:01:34,000
-Even she -- Leonato's Hero,

1378
01:01:34,033 --> 01:01:37,000
your Hero, every man's Hero.

1379
01:01:37,033 --> 01:01:38,100
-Disloyal?

1380
01:01:38,133 --> 01:01:39,766
-The world is too good

1381
01:01:39,800 --> 01:01:41,133
to paint out her wickedness.

1382
01:01:41,166 --> 01:01:43,166
I could say she were worse.

1383
01:01:43,200 --> 01:01:46,300
Think you of a worse title, 
and I will fit her to it.

1384
01:01:46,333 --> 01:01:48,000
Wonder not till further warrant.

1385
01:01:48,033 --> 01:01:49,500
Go but with me tonight.

1386
01:01:49,533 --> 01:01:51,500
You shall see her chamber window

1387
01:01:51,533 --> 01:01:53,900
entered even the night before 
her wedding day.

1388
01:01:53,933 --> 01:01:58,233
If you love her then, 
tomorrow wed her,

1389
01:01:58,266 --> 01:02:01,366
but it would better fit 
your honor to change your mind.

1390
01:02:01,400 --> 01:02:03,266
-May this be so? 
-I will not think it.

1391
01:02:03,300 --> 01:02:05,166
-If you dare not 
trust that you see,

1392
01:02:05,200 --> 01:02:07,000
confess not that you know.

1393
01:02:07,033 --> 01:02:08,433
If you will follow me,

1394
01:02:08,466 --> 01:02:12,066
I will show you enough, 
and when you have seen more

1395
01:02:12,100 --> 01:02:14,700
and heard more, 
proceed accordingly.

1396
01:02:14,733 --> 01:02:17,766
-If I see anything tonight 
why I should not marry her.

1397
01:02:17,800 --> 01:02:20,300
Tomorrow in the congregation 
where I should wed,

1398
01:02:20,333 --> 01:02:21,700
there will I shame her.

1399
01:02:21,733 --> 01:02:24,033
-And as I wooed 
for thee to obtain her,

1400
01:02:24,066 --> 01:02:26,100
I will join with thee 
to disgrace her.

1401
01:02:26,133 --> 01:02:29,433
-I will disparage her no farther 
until you are my witnesses.

1402
01:02:29,466 --> 01:02:32,233
Bear it coldly 
but until midnight

1403
01:02:32,266 --> 01:02:35,666
and let the issue show itself.

1404
01:02:35,700 --> 01:02:38,100
-Oh, day untowardly turned!

1405
01:02:38,133 --> 01:02:40,166
-Oh, mischief 
strangely thwarting!

1406
01:02:40,200 --> 01:02:43,733
-Oh, plague right 
well prevented!

1407
01:02:43,766 --> 01:02:48,900
So will you say when you 
have seen the sequel.

1408
01:02:48,933 --> 01:02:57,333
♪♪

1409
01:02:57,366 --> 01:03:05,800
♪♪

1410
01:03:05,833 --> 01:03:08,133
[ Whistle blows ]

1411
01:03:08,166 --> 01:03:11,300
♪♪

1412
01:03:11,333 --> 01:03:13,333
[ Whistle continues ]

1413
01:03:16,800 --> 01:03:18,266
-Are you good men and true?

1414
01:03:18,300 --> 01:03:22,733
-Yea, or else it were pity but 
they should suffer salvation,

1415
01:03:22,766 --> 01:03:24,233
body and soul.

1416
01:03:24,266 --> 01:03:26,000
-Nay, that were punishment 
too good for them

1417
01:03:26,033 --> 01:03:27,933
if they should have 
any allegiance in them,

1418
01:03:27,966 --> 01:03:30,200
being chosen 
for the Prince's watch.

1419
01:03:30,233 --> 01:03:34,200
-Well, give them their charge, 
neighbor Dogberry.

1420
01:03:34,233 --> 01:03:36,433
-First, who think you 
the most desertless man

1421
01:03:36,466 --> 01:03:38,600
to be constable? 
-Hugh Otecake, sir.

1422
01:03:38,633 --> 01:03:39,966
Or George Seacole... 
-No.

1423
01:03:40,000 --> 01:03:41,466
-...for they can write and read.

1424
01:03:41,500 --> 01:03:42,333
-Hmm.

1425
01:03:42,366 --> 01:03:45,666
Come hither, Neighbor Seacole.

1426
01:03:45,700 --> 01:03:47,000
Hmm.

1427
01:03:47,033 --> 01:03:51,700
God hath blessed you 
with a good name.

1428
01:03:54,633 --> 01:03:56,533
To be a well-favored man 
is the gift of fortune,

1429
01:03:56,566 --> 01:03:58,266
but to write and read 
comes by nature.

1430
01:03:58,300 --> 01:04:00,933
-Both which, Master Constable -- 
-You have.

1431
01:04:00,966 --> 01:04:02,733
I knew it would be your answer.

1432
01:04:02,766 --> 01:04:05,133
Well, for your favor, sir, 
why, give God thanks,

1433
01:04:05,166 --> 01:04:06,366
and make no boast of it,

1434
01:04:06,400 --> 01:04:08,233
and for your writing 
and reading, why,

1435
01:04:08,266 --> 01:04:12,500
let that appear when 
there's no need of such vanity.

1436
01:04:12,533 --> 01:04:16,066
You are thought here to be 
the most senseless and fit man

1437
01:04:16,100 --> 01:04:17,666
for the constable of the watch.

1438
01:04:17,700 --> 01:04:20,700
Therefore, bear you the lantern.

1439
01:04:23,466 --> 01:04:24,566
This is your charge.

1440
01:04:24,600 --> 01:04:26,633
You shall comprehend 
all vagrom men.

1441
01:04:26,666 --> 01:04:29,000
You are to bid any man stand, 
in the Prince's name.

1442
01:04:29,033 --> 01:04:31,233
-How if he will not stand?

1443
01:04:31,266 --> 01:04:34,366
-Why, then take no note of him, 
but let him go

1444
01:04:34,400 --> 01:04:36,833
and presently call the rest 
of the watch together

1445
01:04:36,866 --> 01:04:38,533
and thank God 
you are rid of a knave.

1446
01:04:38,566 --> 01:04:40,833
-If he were not stand 
when he is bidden,

1447
01:04:40,866 --> 01:04:42,666
he is none 
of the Prince's subjects.

1448
01:04:42,700 --> 01:04:44,366
-True, and they are 
to meddle with none

1449
01:04:44,400 --> 01:04:45,966
but the Prince's subjects.

1450
01:04:46,000 --> 01:04:47,933
You shall also make no noise 
in the streets for,

1451
01:04:47,966 --> 01:04:49,400
for the watch 
to babble and to talk

1452
01:04:49,433 --> 01:04:51,733
is most tolerable 
and not to be endured.

1453
01:04:51,766 --> 01:04:53,433
-We would rather sleep 
than talk.

1454
01:04:53,466 --> 01:04:57,033
We know what belongs to a watch.

1455
01:04:57,066 --> 01:05:00,133
-Why, you speak like an ancient 
and most quiet watchman,

1456
01:05:00,166 --> 01:05:02,100
for I cannot see how sleeping 
should offend.

1457
01:05:02,133 --> 01:05:05,500
Only have a care that 
your bills be not stolen.

1458
01:05:05,533 --> 01:05:07,233
Well, you are to call 
at all the alehouses

1459
01:05:07,266 --> 01:05:09,200
and bid those that are drunk, 
get them to bed.

1460
01:05:09,233 --> 01:05:10,766
-How if they will not?

1461
01:05:10,800 --> 01:05:14,166
-Why, then let them alone 
till they are sober.

1462
01:05:14,200 --> 01:05:15,766
If they make you not 
then the better answer,

1463
01:05:15,800 --> 01:05:17,633
you may say they are not the men 
you took them for.

1464
01:05:17,666 --> 01:05:19,400
-Well, sir, I believe -- 
-If you meet a thief,

1465
01:05:19,433 --> 01:05:21,366
you may suspect him 
by the virtue of your office

1466
01:05:21,400 --> 01:05:23,766
to be no true man, 
for such kind of man,

1467
01:05:23,800 --> 01:05:25,200
the less you meddle 
or make with them, why,

1468
01:05:25,233 --> 01:05:26,233
the more is for your honesty.

1469
01:05:26,266 --> 01:05:27,833
-If we know him to be a thief,

1470
01:05:27,866 --> 01:05:29,633
shall we not lay hand?

1471
01:05:29,666 --> 01:05:32,133
-Truly by your office, you may,

1472
01:05:32,166 --> 01:05:35,433
but I think they that 
touch pitch will be defiled.

1473
01:05:35,466 --> 01:05:38,266
The most peaceable way for you, 
if you do take a thief,

1474
01:05:38,300 --> 01:05:40,033
is to let him show himself 
what he is

1475
01:05:40,066 --> 01:05:41,366
and steal out of your company.

1476
01:05:41,400 --> 01:05:44,166
-You have always been 
called merciful, partner.

1477
01:05:44,200 --> 01:05:46,766
-[ Chuckles ] 
Well, masters, goodnight,

1478
01:05:46,800 --> 01:05:49,233
and if there be any manner 
of weight chances, call up me.

1479
01:05:49,266 --> 01:05:50,900
Keep your fellow councils 
and your own,

1480
01:05:50,933 --> 01:05:51,800
and goodnight.

1481
01:05:51,833 --> 01:05:53,333
Come, neighbor.

1482
01:05:55,233 --> 01:05:57,666
-Well, masters, 
we hear our charge.

1483
01:05:57,700 --> 01:06:00,600
Let us go sit here upon 
the church bench till 2:00

1484
01:06:00,633 --> 01:06:01,933
and then off to bed.

1485
01:06:01,966 --> 01:06:02,933
-Hey.

1486
01:06:02,966 --> 01:06:05,200
[ Whistle blows ]

1487
01:06:05,233 --> 01:06:07,866
-One word more, 
honest neighbors.

1488
01:06:07,900 --> 01:06:10,400
I pray you watch about 
Signor Leonato's door,

1489
01:06:10,433 --> 01:06:12,033
for the wedding 
being there tomorrow,

1490
01:06:12,066 --> 01:06:13,833
there's a great coil tonight.

1491
01:06:13,866 --> 01:06:14,900
Adieu.

1492
01:06:14,933 --> 01:06:18,400
Be vigitant, I beseech you.

1493
01:06:29,100 --> 01:06:31,966
-What Conrade? 
-Peace! Stir not.

1494
01:06:32,000 --> 01:06:34,600
-Conrade, I say! 
-Here, man. I'm at thy elbow.

1495
01:06:34,633 --> 01:06:35,966
-Mass, and my elbow itched.

1496
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:37,966
I thought there would 
a scab follow.

1497
01:06:38,000 --> 01:06:39,533
-I will owe thee an answer 
for that

1498
01:06:39,566 --> 01:06:41,933
and now forward with thy tale. 
-Stand thee close then,

1499
01:06:41,966 --> 01:06:45,266
and I will like a true drunkard 
utter all to thee.

1500
01:06:45,300 --> 01:06:48,233
-Some treason, masters, 
yet stay close.

1501
01:06:48,266 --> 01:06:50,066
-Therefore, know I have earned

1502
01:06:50,100 --> 01:06:52,866
a thousand ducats of Don John.

1503
01:06:52,900 --> 01:06:55,266
-Is it possible any villainy 
should be so dear?

1504
01:06:55,300 --> 01:06:57,166
-Thou shouldst rather ask 
if it were possible

1505
01:06:57,200 --> 01:06:59,166
any villainy should be so rich,

1506
01:06:59,200 --> 01:07:01,566
for when rich villains 
have need of poor ones,

1507
01:07:01,600 --> 01:07:04,200
poor ones may make 
what price they will.

1508
01:07:04,233 --> 01:07:05,166
-I wonder at it.

1509
01:07:05,200 --> 01:07:06,333
[ Rattling ]

1510
01:07:06,366 --> 01:07:07,933
-Dost thou not hear somebody?

1511
01:07:07,966 --> 01:07:10,133
-Nah. 
'Twas the vane on the house.

1512
01:07:13,300 --> 01:07:16,566
-Know that I have tonight 
wooed Margaret,

1513
01:07:16,600 --> 01:07:20,866
the Lady Hero's gentlewoman 
by the name of Hero.

1514
01:07:20,900 --> 01:07:24,100
She leans me out at her 
mistress' chamber window,

1515
01:07:24,133 --> 01:07:27,300
bids me a thousand times 
good night.

1516
01:07:27,333 --> 01:07:28,566
I tell this tale vilely.

1517
01:07:28,600 --> 01:07:29,733
I should first tell thee how

1518
01:07:29,766 --> 01:07:32,166
the Prince, Claudio, 
and my master, planted

1519
01:07:32,200 --> 01:07:35,666
and placed and possessed 
by my master, Don John,

1520
01:07:35,700 --> 01:07:39,966
saw afar off in the orchard 
this amiable encounter.

1521
01:07:40,000 --> 01:07:41,700
-And thought they Margaret 
was Hero?

1522
01:07:41,733 --> 01:07:43,400
-Two of them did, 
the Prince and Claudio,

1523
01:07:43,433 --> 01:07:46,500
but the Devil, my master, 
knew she was Margaret,

1524
01:07:46,533 --> 01:07:49,500
and partly by his oaths 
which first possessed them,

1525
01:07:49,533 --> 01:07:53,100
partly by the dark night 
which did deceive them,

1526
01:07:53,133 --> 01:07:55,900
but chiefly by my villainy

1527
01:07:55,933 --> 01:07:59,300
which did confirm 
any slander Don John had made.

1528
01:07:59,333 --> 01:08:02,700
Away went Claudio, enraged, 
swore he would meet her

1529
01:08:02,733 --> 01:08:06,033
as he was appointed next morning 
at the temple,

1530
01:08:06,066 --> 01:08:09,066
and there, 
before the whole congregation,

1531
01:08:09,100 --> 01:08:11,000
shame her with what 
he saw o'ernight

1532
01:08:11,033 --> 01:08:14,000
and sent her home again 
without a husband.

1533
01:08:14,033 --> 01:08:17,200
-We charge you in 
the Prince's name! Stand!

1534
01:08:17,233 --> 01:08:19,533
-Call up the right 
Master Constable!

1535
01:08:19,566 --> 01:08:21,466
[ Whistle blows ]

1536
01:08:21,500 --> 01:08:22,533
-Get -- [ Grunting ]

1537
01:08:22,566 --> 01:08:23,566
-We have hereby recovered

1538
01:08:23,600 --> 01:08:25,399
the most dangerous 
piece of lechery

1539
01:08:25,433 --> 01:08:29,800
that ever was known 
in the commonwealth.

1540
01:08:29,833 --> 01:08:31,399
[ Whistle blows ]

1541
01:08:34,066 --> 01:08:37,100
-Masters, never speak. 
We charge you.

1542
01:08:37,133 --> 01:08:39,333
Let us obey you to go with us.

1543
01:08:39,366 --> 01:08:42,266
-Come. 
We'll obey you.

1544
01:08:42,300 --> 01:08:44,600
[ Whistle blows ]

1545
01:08:44,633 --> 01:08:50,533
♪♪

1546
01:08:50,566 --> 01:08:51,966
-Good Ursula! 
-Uh-huh?

1547
01:08:52,000 --> 01:08:54,033
-Wake my cousin Beatrice 
and desire her to rise.

1548
01:08:54,066 --> 01:08:55,933
-I will, Lady. 
-And bid her come hither.

1549
01:08:55,966 --> 01:08:57,933
-Ooh, well. 
-Oh.

1550
01:08:57,966 --> 01:09:00,366
-[ Chuckles ]

1551
01:09:02,399 --> 01:09:05,266
Troth, I think your other rebato 
were better.

1552
01:09:05,300 --> 01:09:08,500
-No, pray thee, good Meg, 
I'll wear this.

1553
01:09:08,533 --> 01:09:10,000
-By my troth, it's not so good,

1554
01:09:10,033 --> 01:09:12,233
and I warrant your cousin 
will say so.

1555
01:09:12,266 --> 01:09:14,433
-My cousin is a fool, 
and thou art another.

1556
01:09:14,466 --> 01:09:17,666
-Oh? 
-I'll wear none but this.

1557
01:09:17,700 --> 01:09:18,866
[ Both laugh ] 
-Ooh.

1558
01:09:18,899 --> 01:09:21,200
I like the new tire 
within excellently,

1559
01:09:21,233 --> 01:09:23,500
if the hair were 
a thought browner,

1560
01:09:23,533 --> 01:09:26,866
and your gown's a most 
rare fashion, faith.

1561
01:09:26,899 --> 01:09:28,466
-God give me joy to wear it,

1562
01:09:28,500 --> 01:09:30,266
for my heart is exceeding heavy.

1563
01:09:30,300 --> 01:09:32,166
-It will be heavier soon

1564
01:09:32,200 --> 01:09:35,333
by the weight of a man.

1565
01:09:35,366 --> 01:09:37,533
-Fie upon thee!

1566
01:09:37,566 --> 01:09:38,866
Art not ashamed?

1567
01:09:38,899 --> 01:09:42,066
-Of what, lady? 
Of speaking honorably?

1568
01:09:42,100 --> 01:09:44,666
Is not marriage honorable 
in a beggar?

1569
01:09:44,700 --> 01:09:48,366
Is not your lord honorable 
without marriage?

1570
01:09:48,399 --> 01:09:49,700
I think you would have me say,

1571
01:09:49,733 --> 01:09:52,133
"Saving your reverence, 
a husband."

1572
01:09:52,166 --> 01:09:54,766
And bad thinking do not 
wrest true speaking.

1573
01:09:54,800 --> 01:09:57,733
I'll offend nobody.

1574
01:09:57,766 --> 01:10:00,900
Is there any harm in 
"the heavier for a husband"?

1575
01:10:00,933 --> 01:10:02,300
None, I think,

1576
01:10:02,333 --> 01:10:04,466
and it be the right husband 
and the right wife.

1577
01:10:04,500 --> 01:10:06,900
Otherwise, 
'tis light and not heavy.

1578
01:10:06,933 --> 01:10:08,833
-Hmm. 
-Ask my Lady Beatrice else.

1579
01:10:08,866 --> 01:10:09,966
Here she comes.

1580
01:10:10,000 --> 01:10:14,400
-Good morrow, coz! 
-Good morrow, sweet Hero!

1581
01:10:14,433 --> 01:10:15,766
-Why, how now?

1582
01:10:15,800 --> 01:10:17,266
Do you speak in the sick tune?

1583
01:10:17,300 --> 01:10:19,800
-'Tis almost 5:00, cousin! 
-Aaaaah!

1584
01:10:19,833 --> 01:10:21,766
-'Tis time you were ready!

1585
01:10:21,800 --> 01:10:23,533
-Ugh, by my troth,

1586
01:10:23,566 --> 01:10:25,266
I'm exceeding ill, heigh-ho!

1587
01:10:25,300 --> 01:10:28,566
-For a hawk, a horse 
or a husband?

1588
01:10:28,600 --> 01:10:30,400
-For the letter that 
begins them all, H.

1589
01:10:30,433 --> 01:10:33,333
By my troth, I'm sick.

1590
01:10:33,366 --> 01:10:36,400
-Get you some of this distilled 
carduus benedictus

1591
01:10:36,433 --> 01:10:37,666
and lay it to your heart.

1592
01:10:37,700 --> 01:10:40,666
It is the only thing 
for a qualm.

1593
01:10:40,700 --> 01:10:43,500
-Benedictus?

1594
01:10:43,533 --> 01:10:45,566
-Hmm. 
-Why benedictus?

1595
01:10:45,600 --> 01:10:48,233
You have some moral 
in this benedictus?

1596
01:10:48,266 --> 01:10:49,533
-Moral? No.

1597
01:10:49,566 --> 01:10:52,433
By my troth, 
I have no moral meaning.

1598
01:10:52,466 --> 01:10:56,600
You may think perchance that 
I think that you are in love.

1599
01:10:56,633 --> 01:10:58,566
-Ah! 
-Nay, by your Lady,

1600
01:10:58,600 --> 01:11:00,866
I am not such a fool 
to think what I list,

1601
01:11:00,900 --> 01:11:02,433
nor I list not to think 
what I can,

1602
01:11:02,466 --> 01:11:04,133
nor indeed, I cannot think.

1603
01:11:04,166 --> 01:11:06,433
If I were to think 
my heart out of thinking

1604
01:11:06,466 --> 01:11:09,533
that you are in love 
or that you will be in love

1605
01:11:09,566 --> 01:11:12,533
or that you

1606
01:11:09,566 --> 01:11:12,533
can

1607
01:11:09,566 --> 01:11:12,533
be in love.

1608
01:11:12,566 --> 01:11:16,033
Yet, hmm, 
Benedick was such another...

1609
01:11:16,066 --> 01:11:19,333
-Hmm. 
-...and now is he become a man.

1610
01:11:19,366 --> 01:11:21,333
Oh, he swore 
he would never marry,

1611
01:11:21,366 --> 01:11:23,166
and now in despite his heart,

1612
01:11:23,200 --> 01:11:25,033
he eats his meat 
without grudging,

1613
01:11:25,066 --> 01:11:26,900
and how you may be converted, 
I know not,

1614
01:11:26,933 --> 01:11:30,133
yet methinks you look with 
your eyes as other women do.

1615
01:11:30,166 --> 01:11:35,133
-What pace is this 
that thy tongue keeps?

1616
01:11:35,166 --> 01:11:37,000
-Not a false gallop.

1617
01:11:37,033 --> 01:11:39,666
[ Light laughter ]

1618
01:11:39,700 --> 01:11:41,166
[ Indistinct talking ]

1619
01:11:41,200 --> 01:11:43,200
-[ Gasps ] Madam, withdraw!

1620
01:11:43,233 --> 01:11:46,733
The Prince, the Count, 
Signor Benedick, Don John

1621
01:11:46,766 --> 01:11:50,466
and all the gallants of the town 
are come to bid you to church!

1622
01:11:50,500 --> 01:11:51,966
-Help to dress me, good coz,

1623
01:11:52,000 --> 01:11:54,566
good Meg, good Ursula. 
-Oh.

1624
01:11:54,600 --> 01:11:57,600
Come on. 
-Ah.

1625
01:11:57,633 --> 01:12:02,566
-♪ Hey, hey, hey, yeah

1626
01:12:02,600 --> 01:12:05,466
-What would you with me, 
honest neighbor?

1627
01:12:05,500 --> 01:12:07,366
-Marry, sir, I would have 
some confidence with you

1628
01:12:07,400 --> 01:12:08,766
that discerns you nearly.

1629
01:12:08,800 --> 01:12:10,766
-Brief, I pray you, 
for you see,

1630
01:12:10,800 --> 01:12:12,133
it is a busy time with me.

1631
01:12:12,166 --> 01:12:15,366
-Marry, this it is, sir. 
-Yes, in truth, it is, sir.

1632
01:12:15,400 --> 01:12:18,000
-What is it, my good friends? 
-Goodman Verges, sir,

1633
01:12:18,033 --> 01:12:19,766
speaks a little off the matter, 
an old man, sir,

1634
01:12:19,800 --> 01:12:21,700
and his wits are not 
so blunt as, God help,

1635
01:12:21,733 --> 01:12:23,533
I would desire they were, 
but, in faith,

1636
01:12:23,566 --> 01:12:25,200
honest as the skin 
between his brows.

1637
01:12:25,233 --> 01:12:28,066
-Yes, I thank God I am 
as honest as any man living

1638
01:12:28,100 --> 01:12:31,700
that is an old man 
and no honester than I.

1639
01:12:31,733 --> 01:12:33,266
-Comparisons are odorous.

1640
01:12:33,300 --> 01:12:35,100
Palabras,

1641
01:12:33,300 --> 01:12:35,100
Neighbor Verges.

1642
01:12:35,133 --> 01:12:38,566
-Neighbors, you are tedious.

1643
01:12:38,600 --> 01:12:39,833
-It pleases Your Worship 
to say so,

1644
01:12:39,866 --> 01:12:41,733
but we are the poor 
duke's officers,

1645
01:12:41,766 --> 01:12:44,700
but truly for mine own part, 
if I were as tedious as a king,

1646
01:12:44,733 --> 01:12:47,200
I could find it in my heart to 
bestow it all of your worship.

1647
01:12:47,233 --> 01:12:50,700
-[ Chuckles ] All thy 
tediousness on me.

1648
01:12:50,733 --> 01:12:52,666
I would fain know 
what you have to say.

1649
01:12:52,700 --> 01:12:54,666
-Marry, sir, our watch tonight,

1650
01:12:54,700 --> 01:12:56,700
excepting 
Your Worship's presence,

1651
01:12:56,733 --> 01:13:02,600
ha' ta'en a couple 
of as arrant knaves as any.

1652
01:13:02,633 --> 01:13:04,433
-A good old man, sir, 
he will be talking.

1653
01:13:04,466 --> 01:13:07,500
As they say, "When the age 
is in, the wit is out."

1654
01:13:07,533 --> 01:13:09,833
God help us. 
It is a world to see.

1655
01:13:09,866 --> 01:13:11,400
Well said in faith, 
Neighbor Verges.

1656
01:13:11,433 --> 01:13:13,866
Well, God is a good man, 
and two men ride of a horse.

1657
01:13:13,900 --> 01:13:15,133
One must ride behind.

1658
01:13:15,166 --> 01:13:17,633
-I must leave you. 
-One word, sir.

1659
01:13:17,666 --> 01:13:19,833
Our watch, sir, 
have indeed comprehended

1660
01:13:19,866 --> 01:13:21,533
two auspicious persons,

1661
01:13:21,566 --> 01:13:22,900
and we would have them 
this morning

1662
01:13:22,933 --> 01:13:24,300
examined before Your Worship.

1663
01:13:24,333 --> 01:13:26,133
-Well, take their examination 
yourself and bring it me.

1664
01:13:26,166 --> 01:13:28,466
I am now in great haste 
as it may appear unto you.

1665
01:13:28,500 --> 01:13:29,800
-It shall be suffigance.

1666
01:13:29,833 --> 01:13:31,566
-Drink you some wine ere you go. 
Fare you well.

1667
01:13:31,600 --> 01:13:33,066
-My lord, they stay for you

1668
01:13:33,100 --> 01:13:35,400
to give your daughter 
to her husband.

1669
01:13:35,433 --> 01:13:37,566
-I'll wait upon them. 
[ Chuckles ] Hmm.

1670
01:13:37,600 --> 01:13:38,933
I am ready.

1671
01:13:38,966 --> 01:13:40,433
-Go, good partner, go.

1672
01:13:40,466 --> 01:13:41,966
Get you to Francis Seacole.

1673
01:13:42,000 --> 01:13:43,800
Bid him bring his pen 
and inkhorn.

1674
01:13:43,833 --> 01:13:45,466
We are now to examination 
these men.

1675
01:13:45,500 --> 01:13:47,900
-And we must do it wisely!

1676
01:13:47,933 --> 01:13:50,733
-We will spare for no wit, 
I warrant you,

1677
01:13:50,766 --> 01:13:54,400
only get the learned writer 
to set down our excommunication.

1678
01:13:54,433 --> 01:14:03,066
♪♪

1679
01:14:03,100 --> 01:14:11,700
♪♪

1680
01:14:11,733 --> 01:14:14,366
[ Cheers and applause ]

1681
01:14:14,400 --> 01:14:22,566
♪♪

1682
01:14:22,600 --> 01:14:30,766
♪♪

1683
01:14:30,800 --> 01:14:38,966
♪♪

1684
01:14:39,000 --> 01:14:47,200
♪♪

1685
01:14:47,233 --> 01:14:55,400
♪♪

1686
01:14:55,433 --> 01:15:03,666
♪♪

1687
01:15:03,700 --> 01:15:11,866
♪♪

1688
01:15:11,900 --> 01:15:13,900
[ Cheers and applause ]

1689
01:15:14,933 --> 01:15:21,433
-♪ Precious Lord

1690
01:15:21,466 --> 01:15:26,766
♪ Take my hand

1691
01:15:26,800 --> 01:15:33,633
♪ Lead me on

1692
01:15:33,666 --> 01:15:37,833
♪ Let me stand

1693
01:15:37,866 --> 01:15:44,433
♪ I am tired

1694
01:15:44,466 --> 01:15:50,833
♪ I am weak

1695
01:15:50,866 --> 01:15:57,666
♪ I am worn

1696
01:15:57,700 --> 01:16:04,533
♪ Through the storm

1697
01:16:04,566 --> 01:16:12,300
♪ Through the night

1698
01:16:12,333 --> 01:16:17,933
♪ Lead me on

1699
01:16:17,966 --> 01:16:21,833
♪ Through the light

1700
01:16:21,866 --> 01:16:26,500
♪ Take my hand

1701
01:16:26,533 --> 01:16:32,200
♪ Precious Lord

1702
01:16:32,233 --> 01:16:36,933
♪ And lead me

1703
01:16:36,966 --> 01:16:45,100
♪ Home

1704
01:16:45,133 --> 01:16:48,133
[ Cheers and applause ]

1705
01:16:51,766 --> 01:16:55,133
-You come hither, my lord, 
to marry this lady?

1706
01:16:55,166 --> 01:16:56,633
-No.

1707
01:16:56,666 --> 01:16:58,933
-To be married

1708
01:16:56,666 --> 01:16:58,933
to

1709
01:16:56,666 --> 01:16:58,933
her, Friar.

1710
01:16:58,966 --> 01:17:02,500
You

1711
01:16:58,966 --> 01:17:02,500
come to marry her.

1712
01:17:02,533 --> 01:17:05,500
-Lady, you come hither to be 
married to this Count?

1713
01:17:05,533 --> 01:17:06,700
-I do.

1714
01:17:06,733 --> 01:17:08,766
-If either of you know 
any inward impediment

1715
01:17:08,800 --> 01:17:10,400
why you should not be conjoined,

1716
01:17:10,433 --> 01:17:12,533
I charge you on your souls 
to utter it.

1717
01:17:12,566 --> 01:17:15,066
-Know you any, Hero? 
-None, my lord.

1718
01:17:15,100 --> 01:17:17,933
-Know you any, Count?

1719
01:17:17,966 --> 01:17:20,366
-I dare make his answer none.

1720
01:17:20,400 --> 01:17:22,366
-Oh, what men dare do!

1721
01:17:22,400 --> 01:17:24,233
What men may do!

1722
01:17:24,266 --> 01:17:26,533
What men daily do 
not knowing what they do!

1723
01:17:26,566 --> 01:17:27,866
-How now, interjections?

1724
01:17:27,900 --> 01:17:30,700
-Stand thee by, Friar.

1725
01:17:30,733 --> 01:17:31,966
Father, by your leave,

1726
01:17:32,000 --> 01:17:34,133
will you with free 
and unconstrained soul

1727
01:17:34,166 --> 01:17:36,233
give me this maid, 
your daughter?

1728
01:17:36,266 --> 01:17:40,066
-As freely, son, 
as God did give her me.

1729
01:17:40,100 --> 01:17:41,933
-And what have I 
to give you back

1730
01:17:41,966 --> 01:17:43,433
whose worth may counterpoise

1731
01:17:43,466 --> 01:17:45,533
this rich and precious gift?

1732
01:17:45,566 --> 01:17:48,333
-Nothing...

1733
01:17:48,366 --> 01:17:51,300
unless you render her again.

1734
01:17:51,333 --> 01:17:54,500
-Sweet Prince, you learn me 
noble thankfulness.

1735
01:17:56,600 --> 01:17:58,066
There! Leonato! 
-[ Screams ]

1736
01:17:58,100 --> 01:17:59,933
-Take her back again!

1737
01:17:59,966 --> 01:18:02,233
Give not this rotten orange 
to your friend.

1738
01:18:02,266 --> 01:18:05,466
She's but the sign and semblance 
of her honor.

1739
01:18:05,500 --> 01:18:08,400
Behold how like a maid 
she blushes here.

1740
01:18:08,433 --> 01:18:09,800
-[ Whimpering ] 
-Oh, what authority

1741
01:18:09,833 --> 01:18:14,400
and show of truth can cunning 
sin cover itself withal!

1742
01:18:14,433 --> 01:18:16,466
Comes not this blood 
as modest evidence

1743
01:18:16,500 --> 01:18:18,333
to witness simple virtue?

1744
01:18:18,366 --> 01:18:20,133
Would you not swear, 
all you that see her,

1745
01:18:20,166 --> 01:18:23,300
that she were a maid 
by these exterior shows?

1746
01:18:23,333 --> 01:18:24,900
But she is none.

1747
01:18:24,933 --> 01:18:27,633
She knows the heat 
of a luxurious bed.

1748
01:18:27,666 --> 01:18:29,766
Her blush is guiltiness, 
not modesty.

1749
01:18:29,800 --> 01:18:31,333
-What do you mean, my lord?

1750
01:18:31,366 --> 01:18:32,633
-Not to be married,

1751
01:18:32,666 --> 01:18:35,300
not to knit my soul 
to an approved wanton.

1752
01:18:35,333 --> 01:18:36,833
-Dear, my lord, 
if you in your own proof

1753
01:18:36,866 --> 01:18:38,300
have vanquished 
the resistance of her youth

1754
01:18:38,333 --> 01:18:39,566
and made defeat 
of her virginity --

1755
01:18:39,600 --> 01:18:41,000
-I know what you would say.

1756
01:18:41,033 --> 01:18:42,900
If I have known her, 
you will say she did embrace me

1757
01:18:42,933 --> 01:18:46,033
as a husband and so 
extenuate the forehand sin.

1758
01:18:46,066 --> 01:18:48,133
No, Leonato.

1759
01:18:48,166 --> 01:18:50,233
I never tempted her 
with word too large,

1760
01:18:50,266 --> 01:18:52,166
but, as a brother to a sister,

1761
01:18:52,200 --> 01:18:54,400
showed bashful sincerity 
and comely love.

1762
01:18:54,433 --> 01:18:57,433
-And seemed I ever otherwise 
to you?

1763
01:18:57,466 --> 01:19:00,566
-Out on thee, seeming! 
I will write against it.

1764
01:19:00,600 --> 01:19:03,033
You seem to me 
as Dian in her orb,

1765
01:19:03,066 --> 01:19:05,733
as chaste as is the bud 
ere it be blown,

1766
01:19:05,766 --> 01:19:08,233
but you are more intemperate 
in your blood than Venus

1767
01:19:08,266 --> 01:19:10,933
or those pampered animals 
that rage in savage sensuality.

1768
01:19:10,966 --> 01:19:14,566
-Is my lord well 
that he doth speak s-so wide?

1769
01:19:14,600 --> 01:19:16,433
-Sweet Prince, 
why speak not you?

1770
01:19:16,466 --> 01:19:17,600
-What should I speak?

1771
01:19:17,633 --> 01:19:19,466
I stand dishonored 
that have gone about

1772
01:19:19,500 --> 01:19:22,866
to link my dear friend 
to a common stale!

1773
01:19:22,900 --> 01:19:25,500
-Are these things spoken, 
or do I but dream?

1774
01:19:25,533 --> 01:19:28,033
-Sir, they are spoken, 
and these things are true.

1775
01:19:28,066 --> 01:19:29,700
-This looks not like a nuptial.

1776
01:19:29,733 --> 01:19:31,633
-True? Oh, God.

1777
01:19:31,666 --> 01:19:34,233
-Leonato, stand I here?

1778
01:19:34,266 --> 01:19:35,600
Is this the Prince?

1779
01:19:35,633 --> 01:19:37,400
Is this the Prince's brother?

1780
01:19:37,433 --> 01:19:39,966
Is this face Hero's? 
Are our eyes our own?

1781
01:19:40,000 --> 01:19:43,133
-All of this is so, 
but what of this, my lord?

1782
01:19:43,166 --> 01:19:45,766
-Let me but move one question 
to your daughter

1783
01:19:45,800 --> 01:19:47,800
and by that fatherly 
and kindly power

1784
01:19:47,833 --> 01:19:50,300
that you have in her, 
bid her answer truly.

1785
01:19:50,333 --> 01:19:53,266
-I charge thee to do so, 
as thou art my child!

1786
01:19:53,300 --> 01:19:55,433
-[ Voice breaking ] 
Oh, God, defend me!

1787
01:19:55,466 --> 01:19:58,766
How am I beset?!

1788
01:19:58,800 --> 01:20:01,366
What kind of catechizing 
call you this?

1789
01:20:01,400 --> 01:20:03,133
-To make you answer truly 
to your name!

1790
01:20:03,166 --> 01:20:06,466
-Is it not Hero?

1791
01:20:06,500 --> 01:20:08,266
Who can blot that name

1792
01:20:08,300 --> 01:20:10,033
with any just reproach?

1793
01:20:10,066 --> 01:20:11,533
-Marry, that could Hero!

1794
01:20:11,566 --> 01:20:15,200
Hero itself can blot out 
Hero's virtue!

1795
01:20:15,233 --> 01:20:18,333
What man was he talked with you 
yesternight out at your window

1796
01:20:18,366 --> 01:20:20,900
betwixt 12 and 1?

1797
01:20:20,933 --> 01:20:22,966
Now, if you are a maiden, 
answer this.

1798
01:20:23,000 --> 01:20:25,866
-I talked with no man 
at that hour, my lord.

1799
01:20:25,900 --> 01:20:28,333
-Why then are you no maiden?

1800
01:20:28,366 --> 01:20:30,433
Leonato!

1801
01:20:30,466 --> 01:20:32,300
I am sorry you must hear.

1802
01:20:32,333 --> 01:20:34,200
Upon mine honor, 
myself, my brother,

1803
01:20:34,233 --> 01:20:36,200
and this grieved Count 
did see her,

1804
01:20:36,233 --> 01:20:38,800
hear her at that hour last night

1805
01:20:38,833 --> 01:20:40,866
talk with a ruffian 
in her chamber window

1806
01:20:40,900 --> 01:20:43,666
who hath indeed, 
most like a liberal villain,

1807
01:20:43,700 --> 01:20:45,833
confessed the vile encounters

1808
01:20:45,866 --> 01:20:48,066
they have had 
a thousand times in secret!

1809
01:20:48,100 --> 01:20:49,400
-Fie! Fie!

1810
01:20:49,433 --> 01:20:53,066
They are not to be named, 
my lord, not to be spoke of.

1811
01:20:53,100 --> 01:20:55,200
There is not chastity enough 
in language

1812
01:20:55,233 --> 01:20:57,100
without offense to utter them.

1813
01:20:57,133 --> 01:20:59,766
Thus, pretty lady,

1814
01:20:59,800 --> 01:21:03,166
I am sorry for 
thy much misgovernment.

1815
01:21:03,200 --> 01:21:05,100
[ Indistinct shouting ]

1816
01:21:05,133 --> 01:21:07,100
-[ Screaming ]

1817
01:21:07,133 --> 01:21:10,533
[ Sobbing ]

1818
01:21:10,566 --> 01:21:12,733
-Oh, Hero.

1819
01:21:12,766 --> 01:21:15,400
What a Hero hadst thou been 
if half thy outward graces

1820
01:21:15,433 --> 01:21:17,300
had been placed 
about thy thoughts

1821
01:21:17,333 --> 01:21:19,433
and counsels of thy heart,

1822
01:21:19,466 --> 01:21:22,733
but fare thee well, 
most foul, most fair!

1823
01:21:22,766 --> 01:21:26,066
Farewell, thou pure impiety 
and impious purity.

1824
01:21:26,100 --> 01:21:28,166
For thee, I'll lock up 
all the gates of love,

1825
01:21:28,200 --> 01:21:30,233
and on my eyelids 
shall conjecture hang

1826
01:21:30,266 --> 01:21:32,466
to turn all beauty 
into thoughts of harm,

1827
01:21:32,500 --> 01:21:34,633
and never shall it 
more be gracious!

1828
01:21:34,666 --> 01:21:37,766
[ Sobbing continues ]

1829
01:21:37,800 --> 01:21:41,500
-Hath no man's dagger here 
a point for me?

1830
01:21:41,533 --> 01:21:43,133
-[ Gasps ]

1831
01:21:43,166 --> 01:21:45,433
-Oh! Why, how now, cousin?

1832
01:21:45,466 --> 01:21:46,800
Wherefore sink you down?

1833
01:21:46,833 --> 01:21:48,700
-Come! 
Let us go!

1834
01:21:48,733 --> 01:21:51,733
These things come thus to light,

1835
01:21:51,766 --> 01:21:55,033
smother her spirits up!

1836
01:21:55,066 --> 01:21:56,300
-How doth the lady?

1837
01:21:56,333 --> 01:21:58,100
-Dead, I think!

1838
01:21:58,133 --> 01:21:59,533
Help, Uncle!

1839
01:21:59,566 --> 01:22:00,633
Hero!

1840
01:22:00,666 --> 01:22:02,366
Why, Hero?! Uncle!

1841
01:22:02,400 --> 01:22:04,666
Signor Benedick! 
Friar!

1842
01:22:04,700 --> 01:22:08,333
-O Fate, 
take not away thy heavy hand.

1843
01:22:08,366 --> 01:22:10,766
Death is the fairest cover

1844
01:22:10,800 --> 01:22:13,900
for her shame 
that may be wished for.

1845
01:22:13,933 --> 01:22:17,400
-Why, how now, cousin? 
-Have comfort, lady.

1846
01:22:17,433 --> 01:22:18,500
-Dost thou look up?

1847
01:22:18,533 --> 01:22:21,233
-Yea, wherefore should she not?

1848
01:22:21,266 --> 01:22:23,533
-Wherefore?

1849
01:22:23,566 --> 01:22:28,166
Why doth not every earthly thing 
cry shame upon her?

1850
01:22:28,200 --> 01:22:32,666
Could she here deny the story 
that is printed in her blood?

1851
01:22:32,700 --> 01:22:38,333
Why ever... 
wast thou lovely in mine eyes?

1852
01:22:38,366 --> 01:22:41,466
Why had I not 
with charitable hand

1853
01:22:41,500 --> 01:22:44,233
took up a beggar's issue 
at my gate

1854
01:22:44,266 --> 01:22:48,033
who smirched thus 
and mired with infamy?

1855
01:22:48,066 --> 01:22:51,433
I might have said, 
"No part of it is mine.

1856
01:22:51,466 --> 01:22:55,666
This shame derives itself 
from unknown loins."

1857
01:22:55,700 --> 01:22:57,500
-Stand up.

1858
01:22:57,533 --> 01:23:02,533
-[ Sniffles ] But mine, 
and mine I loved,

1859
01:23:02,566 --> 01:23:05,000
and mine I praised,

1860
01:23:05,033 --> 01:23:06,800
mine that I was proud on,

1861
01:23:06,833 --> 01:23:12,833
mine so much that I was 
to myself not mine.

1862
01:23:12,866 --> 01:23:16,366
Valuing of her --

1863
01:23:17,900 --> 01:23:21,166
Why?

1864
01:23:21,200 --> 01:23:24,533
-[ Sobs ] 
-Oh.

1865
01:23:26,500 --> 01:23:29,433
She has fallen into a pit of ink

1866
01:23:29,466 --> 01:23:32,900
that the wide sea 
hath dropped too few

1867
01:23:32,933 --> 01:23:35,166
to wash her clean again

1868
01:23:35,200 --> 01:23:36,966
and salt too little

1869
01:23:37,000 --> 01:23:41,233
which may season give to 
her foul, tainted flesh.

1870
01:23:41,266 --> 01:23:44,433
-[ Sobbing continues ] 
-Sir, sir, be patient.

1871
01:23:44,466 --> 01:23:47,300
For my part, 
I am so attired in wonder

1872
01:23:47,333 --> 01:23:48,700
I know not what to say.

1873
01:23:48,733 --> 01:23:51,400
-On my soul, 
my cousin is belied!

1874
01:23:51,433 --> 01:23:53,600
-Lady, were you her bedfellow 
last night?

1875
01:23:53,633 --> 01:23:56,333
-No, truly not, 
although until last night,

1876
01:23:56,366 --> 01:23:59,300
I have this 12 month 
been her bedfellow.

1877
01:23:59,333 --> 01:24:01,833
-Confirmed! 
Confirmed!

1878
01:24:01,866 --> 01:24:04,500
Oh, that is stronger made 
which was before barred

1879
01:24:04,533 --> 01:24:05,933
with ribs of iron!

1880
01:24:05,966 --> 01:24:08,400
Would the two princes lie?

1881
01:24:08,433 --> 01:24:09,800
And Claudio lie?

1882
01:24:09,833 --> 01:24:13,066
Who loved her so 
that speaking of her foulness

1883
01:24:13,100 --> 01:24:14,400
washed it with tears?

1884
01:24:14,433 --> 01:24:16,166
Hence from her.

1885
01:24:16,200 --> 01:24:18,733
Let her die. 
-Hear me a little,

1886
01:24:18,766 --> 01:24:21,000
for I have only silent been 
so long

1887
01:24:21,033 --> 01:24:24,066
and given way unto 
this course of fortune

1888
01:24:24,100 --> 01:24:26,333
by noting of the lady!

1889
01:24:26,366 --> 01:24:29,466
Trust not my age, my reverence, 
calling nor divinity.

1890
01:24:29,500 --> 01:24:32,333
If this sweet lady lie 
not guiltless here

1891
01:24:32,366 --> 01:24:34,833
under some biting error. 
-Friar, it cannot be.

1892
01:24:34,866 --> 01:24:38,266
Thou seest that the only grace 
that she hath left is that

1893
01:24:38,300 --> 01:24:40,533
she not add to her damnation 
a sin of perjury.

1894
01:24:40,566 --> 01:24:42,100
She not denies it!

1895
01:24:42,133 --> 01:24:43,500
Why seek'st thou then 
to cover with excuse

1896
01:24:43,533 --> 01:24:45,300
that which appears 
in proper nakedness?

1897
01:24:45,333 --> 01:24:48,733
-Lady, what man is he 
you are accused of?

1898
01:24:48,766 --> 01:24:52,466
-They know that do accuse me. 
I know none!

1899
01:24:52,500 --> 01:24:56,666
If I know more of any man alive

1900
01:24:56,700 --> 01:24:59,900
than that which maiden modesty 
doth warrant...

1901
01:24:59,933 --> 01:25:03,600
let all my sins lack mercy.

1902
01:25:03,633 --> 01:25:06,133
-There is some 
strange misprision

1903
01:25:06,166 --> 01:25:08,066
in the princes.

1904
01:25:08,100 --> 01:25:10,700
-Two of them have 
the very bent of honor,

1905
01:25:10,733 --> 01:25:13,033
and if their wisdoms 
be misled in this,

1906
01:25:13,066 --> 01:25:15,733
the practice of it lives 
in John the Bastard,

1907
01:25:15,766 --> 01:25:19,900
whose spirits toil 
in frame of villainies.

1908
01:25:19,933 --> 01:25:23,033
-I know not!

1909
01:25:23,066 --> 01:25:26,633
If they speak but truth of her,

1910
01:25:26,666 --> 01:25:29,300
these hands shall tear her,

1911
01:25:29,333 --> 01:25:32,166
and if they wrong her honor,

1912
01:25:32,200 --> 01:25:34,566
the proudest of them 
shall well hear of it!

1913
01:25:34,600 --> 01:25:36,833
-Pause awhile

1914
01:25:36,866 --> 01:25:40,300
and let my counsel sway you 
in this case.

1915
01:25:40,333 --> 01:25:44,466
Your daughter here 
the princes left for dead.

1916
01:25:44,500 --> 01:25:46,466
Let her awhile be 
secretly kept in

1917
01:25:46,500 --> 01:25:50,033
and publish it 
that she is dead indeed.

1918
01:25:50,066 --> 01:25:51,900
Maintain a mourning ostentation,

1919
01:25:51,933 --> 01:25:54,033
and on your family's 
old monuments

1920
01:25:54,066 --> 01:25:56,033
hang mournful epitaphs

1921
01:25:56,066 --> 01:25:59,533
and do all rites that appertain 
unto a burial.

1922
01:25:59,566 --> 01:26:01,300
-What shall come of this? 
What will this do?

1923
01:26:01,333 --> 01:26:05,333
-Marry, this, well carried, 
shall, on her behalf,

1924
01:26:05,366 --> 01:26:08,400
change slander to remorse!

1925
01:26:08,433 --> 01:26:12,033
She dying, 
as it must be so maintained,

1926
01:26:12,066 --> 01:26:16,100
upon the instant she was accused 
shall be lamented,

1927
01:26:16,133 --> 01:26:19,566
pitied, and excused 
of every hearer,

1928
01:26:19,600 --> 01:26:21,800
for it so falls out 
that what we have,

1929
01:26:21,833 --> 01:26:25,266
we prize not to the worth 
whiles we enjoy it,

1930
01:26:25,300 --> 01:26:29,700
but being lacked and lost, 
why, then we rack the value.

1931
01:26:29,733 --> 01:26:33,900
Then we find the virtue that 
possession would not show us

1932
01:26:33,933 --> 01:26:35,533
whiles it was ours,

1933
01:26:35,566 --> 01:26:37,866
but if all aim but this 
be leveled false,

1934
01:26:37,900 --> 01:26:40,333
the supposition 
of the lady's death

1935
01:26:40,366 --> 01:26:43,133
will quench the wonder 
of her infamy,

1936
01:26:43,166 --> 01:26:45,966
and if it sort not well, 
you may conceal her

1937
01:26:46,000 --> 01:26:49,166
as best befits 
her wounded reputation

1938
01:26:49,200 --> 01:26:51,466
in some reclusive 
and religious life

1939
01:26:51,500 --> 01:26:55,133
out of all eyes, tongues, 
minds, and injuries.

1940
01:26:55,166 --> 01:26:58,200
-Signor Leonato, 
let the friar advise you,

1941
01:26:58,233 --> 01:27:00,333
and though you know 
my inwardness and love

1942
01:27:00,366 --> 01:27:03,800
is very much unto the Prince 
and Claudio...

1943
01:27:03,833 --> 01:27:05,900
yet by mine honor, 
I will deal in this

1944
01:27:05,933 --> 01:27:07,700
as secretly and justly

1945
01:27:07,733 --> 01:27:11,100
as your soul should 
with your body.

1946
01:27:11,133 --> 01:27:17,466
-Being that I flow in grief, 
the smallest twine may lead me.

1947
01:27:17,500 --> 01:27:21,700
-'Tis well consented.

1948
01:27:21,733 --> 01:27:24,866
Presently away.

1949
01:27:24,900 --> 01:27:27,166
For to strange sores,

1950
01:27:27,200 --> 01:27:31,466
strangely they strain the cure.

1951
01:27:33,233 --> 01:27:34,866
Come, lady!

1952
01:27:34,900 --> 01:27:37,866
Die to live!

1953
01:27:37,900 --> 01:27:41,833
[ Cheers and applause ]

1954
01:27:41,866 --> 01:27:44,366
This wedding day perhaps

1955
01:27:44,400 --> 01:27:47,333
is but prolonged.

1956
01:27:47,366 --> 01:27:51,833
Have patience and endure!

1957
01:27:51,866 --> 01:27:53,533
-[ Sobbing ]

1958
01:27:56,000 --> 01:27:57,833
[ Applause ]

1959
01:28:01,900 --> 01:28:04,366
-[ Weeping ]

1960
01:28:13,800 --> 01:28:15,766
-Lady Beatrice...

1961
01:28:15,800 --> 01:28:18,633
have you wept all this while?

1962
01:28:21,166 --> 01:28:23,333
-Yea...

1963
01:28:23,366 --> 01:28:25,733
and I will weep a while longer.

1964
01:28:25,766 --> 01:28:28,133
-I will not desire that. 
-You have no reason.

1965
01:28:28,166 --> 01:28:29,433
I do it freely.

1966
01:28:29,466 --> 01:28:32,000
-Surely, I do believe 
your fair cousin is wronged.

1967
01:28:32,033 --> 01:28:36,000
-How much might the man deserve 
of me that would right her?

1968
01:28:36,033 --> 01:28:38,466
-Is there any way 
to show such friendship?

1969
01:28:38,500 --> 01:28:41,233
-A very even way,

1970
01:28:41,266 --> 01:28:43,700
but no such friend.

1971
01:28:43,733 --> 01:28:46,100
-May a man do it?

1972
01:28:46,133 --> 01:28:48,900
-It is a man's office...

1973
01:28:48,933 --> 01:28:50,700
but not yours.

1974
01:28:52,400 --> 01:28:55,933
-I do love nothing in the world

1975
01:28:55,966 --> 01:28:58,533
so well as you.

1976
01:28:58,566 --> 01:29:01,700
Is not that strange?

1977
01:29:01,733 --> 01:29:05,000
-As strange as the thing 
I know not.

1978
01:29:05,033 --> 01:29:06,466
It were as possible for me

1979
01:29:06,500 --> 01:29:09,900
to say I loved nothing 
so well as you,

1980
01:29:09,933 --> 01:29:11,800
but believe me not, 
yet I lie not.

1981
01:29:11,833 --> 01:29:13,800
I confess nothing 
nor I deny nothing.

1982
01:29:13,833 --> 01:29:16,233
I am sorry for my cousin.

1983
01:29:16,266 --> 01:29:18,333
-By my sword, Beatrice, 
thou lovest me.

1984
01:29:18,366 --> 01:29:19,733
-Do not swear and eat it.

1985
01:29:19,766 --> 01:29:21,666
-I will swear by it 
that you love me,

1986
01:29:21,700 --> 01:29:24,333
and I will make him eat it 
that says I love not you.

1987
01:29:24,366 --> 01:29:25,666
-Will you not eat your word?

1988
01:29:25,700 --> 01:29:29,566
-With no sauce that 
can be devised to it,

1989
01:29:29,600 --> 01:29:33,033
I protest, I love thee.

1990
01:29:33,066 --> 01:29:35,066
-Why then, God, forgive me.

1991
01:29:35,100 --> 01:29:36,566
-What offense, sweet Beatrice?

1992
01:29:36,600 --> 01:29:39,533
-You have stayed me 
in a happy hour.

1993
01:29:39,566 --> 01:29:43,633
I was about to protest that...

1994
01:29:43,666 --> 01:29:44,866
I loved you.

1995
01:29:44,900 --> 01:29:48,900
-And do it with all thy heart.

1996
01:29:54,233 --> 01:29:58,700
-I love you with so much 
of my heart

1997
01:29:58,733 --> 01:30:02,233
that none is left to protest.

1998
01:30:05,066 --> 01:30:06,766
-Come.

1999
01:30:06,800 --> 01:30:09,966
Bid me do anything for thee.

2000
01:30:14,233 --> 01:30:16,433
-Kill Claudio.

2001
01:30:16,466 --> 01:30:18,833
-Ha, not for the wide world.

2002
01:30:18,866 --> 01:30:20,600
-You kill

2003
01:30:18,866 --> 01:30:20,600
me

2004
01:30:18,866 --> 01:30:20,600
to deny it. 
Farewell!

2005
01:30:20,633 --> 01:30:22,700
-Tarry, sweet Beatrice. 
-I am gone, though I am here.

2006
01:30:22,733 --> 01:30:24,666
There is no love in you. 
Nay, let me go.

2007
01:30:24,700 --> 01:30:26,700
-Beatrice -- 
-In faith, I will go.

2008
01:30:26,733 --> 01:30:29,366
-We'll be friends first. 
-You dare easier be friends

2009
01:30:29,400 --> 01:30:31,133
with me than fight 
with mine enemy?

2010
01:30:31,166 --> 01:30:33,666
-Is Claudio thine enemy? 
-Is he not approved

2011
01:30:33,700 --> 01:30:34,933
in the height of villain

2012
01:30:34,966 --> 01:30:38,700
that has slandered, scorned, 
dishonored my kinswoman?

2013
01:30:38,733 --> 01:30:40,366
Oh, that I were a man.

2014
01:30:40,400 --> 01:30:43,800
What bear her in hand 
until they come to take hands

2015
01:30:43,833 --> 01:30:47,466
and then with public accusation, 
uncovered slander,

2016
01:30:47,500 --> 01:30:51,366
unmitigated rancor... 
Oh, God that I were a man,

2017
01:30:51,400 --> 01:30:54,200
I would eat his heart 
in the marketplace.

2018
01:30:54,233 --> 01:30:56,500
-Hear me, Beatrice -- 
-Talk with a man out a window.

2019
01:30:56,533 --> 01:30:58,433
A proper saying. 
-Nay, but, Beatrice --

2020
01:30:58,466 --> 01:31:01,533
Sweet Hero, she is wronged. 
She is slandered.

2021
01:31:01,566 --> 01:31:03,366
She is undone. 
-Beatrice --

2022
01:31:03,400 --> 01:31:07,233
-Oh, that I were a man 
for his sake!

2023
01:31:07,266 --> 01:31:09,166
[ Breathing shakily ]

2024
01:31:09,200 --> 01:31:12,366
Or that I had any friend

2025
01:31:12,400 --> 01:31:16,733
would be man for my sake.

2026
01:31:17,766 --> 01:31:21,666
But manhood is melted 
into curtsies,

2027
01:31:21,700 --> 01:31:23,966
valor into compliment,

2028
01:31:24,000 --> 01:31:28,366
and men are only turned 
into tongue and trim ones, too.

2029
01:31:28,400 --> 01:31:30,566
He is now as valiant as Hercules

2030
01:31:30,600 --> 01:31:32,866
that only tells a lie 
and swears it.

2031
01:31:32,900 --> 01:31:34,833
I cannot be a man with wishing.

2032
01:31:34,866 --> 01:31:39,366
Therefore, I will a die a woman 
with grieving.

2033
01:31:39,400 --> 01:31:42,166
-Tarry, good Beatrice.

2034
01:31:42,200 --> 01:31:44,200
By this hand, I love thee.

2035
01:31:44,233 --> 01:31:46,500
-Use it for my love 
some other way

2036
01:31:46,533 --> 01:31:48,233
than swearing by it.

2037
01:31:48,266 --> 01:31:51,000
-Think you in your soul 
the Count Claudio

2038
01:31:51,033 --> 01:31:53,033
hath wronged Hero? 
-Yea!

2039
01:31:53,066 --> 01:31:57,066
As sure as I have a thought 
or a soul.

2040
01:32:00,066 --> 01:32:02,433
-Enough.

2041
01:32:02,466 --> 01:32:04,366
I am engaged.

2042
01:32:04,400 --> 01:32:07,466
I will challenge him.

2043
01:32:07,500 --> 01:32:09,900
I will kiss your hand,

2044
01:32:09,933 --> 01:32:11,933
and so I leave you.

2045
01:32:14,766 --> 01:32:15,700
-[ Sighs ]

2046
01:32:15,733 --> 01:32:16,833
-By this hand,

2047
01:32:16,866 --> 01:32:20,000
Claudio shall render me 
a dear account.

2048
01:32:20,033 --> 01:32:22,133
As you hear of me...

2049
01:32:22,166 --> 01:32:24,766
so think of me.

2050
01:32:24,800 --> 01:32:26,100
Go.

2051
01:32:26,133 --> 01:32:28,266
Comfort your cousin.

2052
01:32:28,300 --> 01:32:31,633
I must say she is dead.

2053
01:32:31,666 --> 01:32:33,466
And so farewell.

2054
01:32:35,066 --> 01:32:38,033
♪♪

2055
01:32:38,066 --> 01:32:40,600
[ Cheers and applause ]

2056
01:32:43,433 --> 01:32:45,866
[ Cheers and applause ]

2057
01:32:51,300 --> 01:32:54,300
[ Whistle blows ]

2058
01:32:59,866 --> 01:33:01,733
-Is our whole dissembly 
appeared?

2059
01:33:01,766 --> 01:33:04,933
-Oh, a stool for the sexton.

2060
01:33:14,300 --> 01:33:15,633
-[ Clears throat ]

2061
01:33:15,666 --> 01:33:18,400
-Which be the malefactors?

2062
01:33:18,433 --> 01:33:19,900
-Marry, that am I 
and my partner.

2063
01:33:19,933 --> 01:33:21,033
-Nay, that's certain.

2064
01:33:21,066 --> 01:33:22,866
We have the exhibition 
to examine.

2065
01:33:22,900 --> 01:33:27,133
-But which are the offenders 
that are to be examined?

2066
01:33:27,166 --> 01:33:30,033
Let them come before 
Master Constable.

2067
01:33:30,066 --> 01:33:31,933
-Yea, marry, 
let them come before me.

2068
01:33:31,966 --> 01:33:33,266
What is your name, friend?

2069
01:33:33,300 --> 01:33:34,600
-Borachio.

2070
01:33:34,633 --> 01:33:36,333
-Hmm.

2071
01:33:36,366 --> 01:33:38,600
Pray, write down Borachio.

2072
01:33:38,633 --> 01:33:40,166
[ Clears throat ] 
Yours, sirrah?

2073
01:33:40,200 --> 01:33:43,166
-I am a gentleman, sir, 
and my name is Conrade.

2074
01:33:43,200 --> 01:33:46,333
-Write down, 
Master

2075
01:33:43,200 --> 01:33:46,333
Gentleman

2076
01:33:43,200 --> 01:33:46,333
Conrade.

2077
01:33:46,366 --> 01:33:48,500
Masters, do you serve God?

2078
01:33:48,533 --> 01:33:50,566
-Yea, sir. 
-We hope.

2079
01:33:50,600 --> 01:33:52,200
-Write down they hope 
they serve God,

2080
01:33:52,233 --> 01:33:53,633
and write God first, 
for God defend,

2081
01:33:53,666 --> 01:33:56,966
but God should go 
before such villains!

2082
01:33:57,000 --> 01:33:58,833
Masters, it is proved already

2083
01:33:58,866 --> 01:34:00,566
that you are little better 
than false knaves,

2084
01:34:00,600 --> 01:34:02,233
and it will go near to be 
thought so shortly.

2085
01:34:02,266 --> 01:34:05,433
How answer you for yourselves? 
-Marry, sir, we say we are none.

2086
01:34:05,466 --> 01:34:08,066
-[ Chuckles ]

2087
01:34:08,100 --> 01:34:09,733
A marvelous witty fellow, 
I assure you,

2088
01:34:09,766 --> 01:34:11,733
but I will go about with him.

2089
01:34:11,766 --> 01:34:15,766
Come you hither, sirrah, 
a word in your ear.

2090
01:34:15,800 --> 01:34:18,233
Sir, I say to you it is thought 
that you are false knaves.

2091
01:34:18,266 --> 01:34:21,433
-Sir, I say to you, we are none.

2092
01:34:21,466 --> 01:34:23,466
-Well, stand aside.

2093
01:34:23,500 --> 01:34:25,000
'Fore God, 
they are both in a tale.

2094
01:34:25,033 --> 01:34:26,333
Have you writ down 
that they are none?

2095
01:34:26,366 --> 01:34:29,466
-Master Constable, you go 
not the way to examine.

2096
01:34:29,500 --> 01:34:32,800
You must call forth the watch 
that are their accusers.

2097
01:34:32,833 --> 01:34:34,166
-Yea, marry!

2098
01:34:34,200 --> 01:34:37,166
That's the eftest way.

2099
01:34:37,200 --> 01:34:39,166
Let the watch come forth.

2100
01:34:39,200 --> 01:34:41,166
[ Whistle blows ]

2101
01:34:41,200 --> 01:34:43,833
Masters, I charge you 
in the prince's name,

2102
01:34:43,866 --> 01:34:46,500
accuse these men.

2103
01:34:46,533 --> 01:34:49,200
-This man said, sir, 
that Don John,

2104
01:34:49,233 --> 01:34:51,766
the prince's brother, 
was a villain.

2105
01:34:51,800 --> 01:34:53,233
-Write down Prince John 
a villain.

2106
01:34:53,266 --> 01:34:55,733
Why, that is flat perjury to 
call a prince's brother villain.

2107
01:34:55,766 --> 01:34:58,433
-Master Constable? 
-Pray thee, fellow, peace.

2108
01:34:58,466 --> 01:35:01,833
I do not like thy look, 
I promise thee.

2109
01:35:01,866 --> 01:35:03,866
-What heard you him say else?

2110
01:35:03,900 --> 01:35:08,500
-Marry, that he had received 
a thousand ducats of Don John

2111
01:35:08,533 --> 01:35:11,666
for accusing the Lady Hero 
wrongfully.

2112
01:35:11,700 --> 01:35:12,933
-What else, fellow?

2113
01:35:12,966 --> 01:35:14,333
-And that Count Claudio

2114
01:35:14,366 --> 01:35:16,800
did mean upon his words 
to disgrace Hero

2115
01:35:16,833 --> 01:35:19,300
before the whole assembly 
and not marry her.

2116
01:35:19,333 --> 01:35:20,933
-Oh, villain!

2117
01:35:20,966 --> 01:35:23,400
That wilt be condemned 
into everlasting redemption

2118
01:35:23,433 --> 01:35:24,333
for this.

2119
01:35:24,366 --> 01:35:25,966
-What else? 
-This is all.

2120
01:35:26,000 --> 01:35:29,766
-And this is more, masters, 
than you can deny.

2121
01:35:29,800 --> 01:35:33,600
Prince John is this morning 
secretly stolen away.

2122
01:35:33,633 --> 01:35:37,866
Hero was in this manner accused, 
in this very manner refused,

2123
01:35:37,900 --> 01:35:41,800
and upon the grief of it 
suddenly died.

2124
01:35:41,833 --> 01:35:44,800
Master Constable, 
let these men be bound

2125
01:35:44,833 --> 01:35:46,766
and brought to Leonato's.

2126
01:35:46,800 --> 01:35:50,266
I will go before and show him 
their examination.

2127
01:35:50,300 --> 01:35:52,300
-The stool!

2128
01:35:57,166 --> 01:36:00,366
[ Applause ]

2129
01:36:00,400 --> 01:36:01,433
-Come.

2130
01:36:01,466 --> 01:36:03,633
Let them be opinioned.

2131
01:36:06,200 --> 01:36:07,933
-Off, coxcomb!

2132
01:36:07,966 --> 01:36:08,933
-Oh, God's my life.

2133
01:36:08,966 --> 01:36:10,233
Where's the sexton?

2134
01:36:10,266 --> 01:36:12,666
Let him write down 
the prince's officer "coxcomb."

2135
01:36:12,700 --> 01:36:15,600
Come, bind them up, 
thou naught varlet!

2136
01:36:15,633 --> 01:36:18,466
-Away! You are an ass!

2137
01:36:19,566 --> 01:36:21,633
-Dost thou not suspect my place?

2138
01:36:21,666 --> 01:36:24,100
Dost thou not suspect my years?

2139
01:36:24,133 --> 01:36:27,966
Oh, that he were here 
to write me down an ass!

2140
01:36:28,000 --> 01:36:30,433
But, masters, remember 
that I am an ass,

2141
01:36:30,466 --> 01:36:31,866
though it be not written down.

2142
01:36:31,900 --> 01:36:34,466
Yet forget not that I am an ass.

2143
01:36:34,500 --> 01:36:36,133
[ Laughter, applause ]

2144
01:36:36,166 --> 01:36:39,466
I am a wise fellow, 
and which is more an officer,

2145
01:36:39,500 --> 01:36:40,833
and which is more a householder,

2146
01:36:40,866 --> 01:36:44,000
and which is more as pretty 
a piece of flesh as any.

2147
01:36:44,033 --> 01:36:47,333
[ Cheers and applause ]

2148
01:36:47,366 --> 01:36:49,300
And one that knows the law, 
go to.

2149
01:36:49,333 --> 01:36:50,900
And a rich fellow enough, go to,

2150
01:36:50,933 --> 01:36:53,466
and a fellow 
that hath had losses.

2151
01:36:53,500 --> 01:36:55,000
Bring him away!

2152
01:36:55,033 --> 01:36:58,500
Oh, that I had been 
writ down an ass!

2153
01:36:58,533 --> 01:37:00,400
Ha!

2154
01:37:00,433 --> 01:37:03,066
[ Applause ]

2155
01:37:03,100 --> 01:37:07,333
♪♪

2156
01:37:07,366 --> 01:37:09,566
-If you go on thus,

2157
01:37:09,600 --> 01:37:11,800
you will kill yourself.

2158
01:37:11,833 --> 01:37:14,066
And 'tis not wisdom thus to

2159
01:37:14,100 --> 01:37:16,633
second grief against yourself.

2160
01:37:16,666 --> 01:37:20,300
-I pray thee, cease thy counsel 
which falls into mine ears

2161
01:37:20,333 --> 01:37:23,866
as profitless 
as water in a sieve.

2162
01:37:23,900 --> 01:37:27,300
For, brother, men can counsel 
and speak comfort to that grief

2163
01:37:27,333 --> 01:37:29,500
which they themselves not feel.

2164
01:37:29,533 --> 01:37:34,333
But tasting it, [scoffs] 
their counsel turns to passion,

2165
01:37:34,366 --> 01:37:37,533
which before would give 
preceptial medicine to rage.

2166
01:37:37,566 --> 01:37:41,066
Fetter strong madness 
in a silken thread,

2167
01:37:41,100 --> 01:37:43,366
charm ache with air,

2168
01:37:43,400 --> 01:37:45,300
and agony with words.

2169
01:37:45,333 --> 01:37:46,600
No.

2170
01:37:46,633 --> 01:37:49,000
No!

2171
01:37:49,033 --> 01:37:52,366
'Tis all men's office 
to speak patience

2172
01:37:52,400 --> 01:37:55,633
to those that wring 
under the load of sorrow,

2173
01:37:55,666 --> 01:37:59,900
but no man's virtue 
nor sufficiency to be so moral

2174
01:37:59,933 --> 01:38:02,400
when he shall endure 
the like himself.

2175
01:38:02,433 --> 01:38:05,500
Therefore, give me no counsel.

2176
01:38:05,533 --> 01:38:08,600
My griefs cry louder 
than advertisement.

2177
01:38:08,633 --> 01:38:12,200
-Therein do men from children 
nothing differ.

2178
01:38:12,233 --> 01:38:13,900
-I pray thee peace.

2179
01:38:13,933 --> 01:38:15,866
I will be flesh and blood.

2180
01:38:15,900 --> 01:38:17,600
For there was never 
yet philosopher

2181
01:38:17,633 --> 01:38:20,300
that could endure 
the toothache patiently.

2182
01:38:20,333 --> 01:38:23,733
-Yet bend not all the harm 
upon yourself.

2183
01:38:23,766 --> 01:38:27,466
Make those that do offend you 
suffer, too.

2184
01:38:27,500 --> 01:38:30,200
-There, thou speak'st reason.

2185
01:38:30,233 --> 01:38:31,533
Nay, I will do so.

2186
01:38:31,566 --> 01:38:35,166
My soul doth tell me 
that Hero is belied.

2187
01:38:35,200 --> 01:38:37,433
That shall Claudio know, 
and so shall the Prince,

2188
01:38:37,466 --> 01:38:39,533
and all of them 
that thus dishonor her.

2189
01:38:39,566 --> 01:38:42,766
-Here comes the Prince 
and Claudio, hastily.

2190
01:38:42,800 --> 01:38:45,466
-Good e'en. Good e'en. 
-Good day to both of you.

2191
01:38:45,500 --> 01:38:48,733
-Hear you, my lords -- 
-We have some haste, Leonato.

2192
01:38:48,766 --> 01:38:53,400
-Some haste, my lord? 
Well, fare you well, my lord.

2193
01:38:53,433 --> 01:38:56,900
Are you so hasty now?

2194
01:38:56,933 --> 01:38:58,333
Well, all is one.

2195
01:38:58,366 --> 01:39:00,366
-Nay, do not quarrel with us, 
good old man.

2196
01:39:00,400 --> 01:39:03,066
-If he could right himself 
with quarreling,

2197
01:39:03,100 --> 01:39:06,200
some of us would lie low.

2198
01:39:06,233 --> 01:39:10,166
-Who wrongs him? 
-Marry, thou dost wrong me,

2199
01:39:10,200 --> 01:39:11,933
thou dissembler, thou.

2200
01:39:11,966 --> 01:39:14,900
Nay, never lay thy hand 
upon thy sword.

2201
01:39:14,933 --> 01:39:17,100
I fear thee not! 
-Marry, beshrew my hand

2202
01:39:17,133 --> 01:39:19,466
if it should give your age 
such cause of fear.

2203
01:39:19,500 --> 01:39:21,666
In faith, my hand meant 
nothing to my sword.

2204
01:39:21,700 --> 01:39:22,966
-Tush, tush, man!

2205
01:39:23,000 --> 01:39:25,333
Never fleer and jest at me.

2206
01:39:25,366 --> 01:39:28,500
I speak not like a dotard 
or a fool.

2207
01:39:28,533 --> 01:39:30,400
As under privilege of age

2208
01:39:30,433 --> 01:39:32,000
to brag what I have done 
being young,

2209
01:39:32,033 --> 01:39:34,066
or what would do were I not old.

2210
01:39:34,100 --> 01:39:36,566
Know, Claudio, to thy head,

2211
01:39:36,600 --> 01:39:41,800
thou hast so wronged 
mine innocent child and me

2212
01:39:41,833 --> 01:39:47,266
that I am forced 
to lay my reverence by.

2213
01:39:47,300 --> 01:39:48,866
And with gray hairs...

2214
01:39:48,900 --> 01:39:51,100
[ Groans ]

2215
01:39:52,966 --> 01:39:54,833
...and bruise of many days

2216
01:39:54,866 --> 01:39:57,500
do challenge thee to trial 
of a man.

2217
01:39:57,533 --> 01:40:00,933
I say thou hast belied 
my innocent child.

2218
01:40:00,966 --> 01:40:04,500
Thy slander hath gone through 
and through her heart.

2219
01:40:04,533 --> 01:40:09,166
And she lies buried 
with her ancestors in a tomb

2220
01:40:09,200 --> 01:40:11,166
where never yet scandal slept.

2221
01:40:11,200 --> 01:40:15,100
Save this of hers, 
framed be thy villainy.

2222
01:40:15,133 --> 01:40:17,266
-My villainy? 
-Thine, Claudio.

2223
01:40:17,300 --> 01:40:19,600
Thine, I say. 
-You say not right, old man.

2224
01:40:19,633 --> 01:40:23,466
-My lord, my lord.

2225
01:40:23,500 --> 01:40:26,900
I'll prove it on his body 
if he dare.

2226
01:40:26,933 --> 01:40:28,766
-Away! 
I will not have to do with you.

2227
01:40:28,800 --> 01:40:30,333
-Thou hast killed my child!

2228
01:40:30,366 --> 01:40:32,500
If thou kills me, boy,

2229
01:40:32,533 --> 01:40:33,966
thou shalt kill a man!

2230
01:40:34,000 --> 01:40:38,466
-He shall kill two of us!

2231
01:40:38,500 --> 01:40:41,533
Come, sir boy, come!

2232
01:40:41,566 --> 01:40:43,566
Follow me.

2233
01:40:43,600 --> 01:40:47,900
Sir boy, I'll whip you 
from your foining fence.

2234
01:40:47,933 --> 01:40:50,600
Nay, as I am a gentleman, 
I will.

2235
01:40:50,633 --> 01:40:53,233
-Brother -- 
-Content yourself.

2236
01:40:53,266 --> 01:40:56,000
God knows I loved my niece,

2237
01:40:56,033 --> 01:40:57,900
and she is dead,

2238
01:40:57,933 --> 01:40:59,533
slandered to death by villains

2239
01:40:59,566 --> 01:41:02,533
that dare as well 
answer a man indeed

2240
01:41:02,566 --> 01:41:05,833
as I dare take a serpent 
by the tongue.

2241
01:41:05,866 --> 01:41:08,833
Boys, apes, braggarts,

2242
01:41:08,866 --> 01:41:10,933
Jacks, milksops!

2243
01:41:10,966 --> 01:41:12,033
-Brother Anthony!

2244
01:41:12,066 --> 01:41:13,266
-Come, 'tis no matter.

2245
01:41:13,300 --> 01:41:18,000
Do not you meddle. 
Let me deal in this.

2246
01:41:18,033 --> 01:41:21,700
-Gentlemen, both, we will 
not wake your patience.

2247
01:41:21,733 --> 01:41:23,333
My heart is sorry 
for your daughter's death,

2248
01:41:23,366 --> 01:41:25,633
but on my honor, 
she was charged with nothing

2249
01:41:25,666 --> 01:41:27,766
but what was true 
and very full of proof!

2250
01:41:27,800 --> 01:41:29,766
-My lord -- 
-I will not hear you.

2251
01:41:29,800 --> 01:41:33,033
-No?!

2252
01:41:33,066 --> 01:41:35,700
-Brother, come away.

2253
01:41:35,733 --> 01:41:37,100
I will be heard.

2254
01:41:37,133 --> 01:41:39,066
-And shall!

2255
01:41:39,100 --> 01:41:42,933
or some of us will smart for it.

2256
01:41:47,966 --> 01:41:49,200
-See? See?

2257
01:41:49,233 --> 01:41:50,766
Here comes the man 
we went to seek.

2258
01:41:50,800 --> 01:41:53,766
-Now, signior, what news? 
-Good day, my lord.

2259
01:41:53,800 --> 01:41:54,933
-Welcome, signior.

2260
01:41:54,966 --> 01:41:56,866
You are almost come to part 
almost a fray.

2261
01:41:56,900 --> 01:41:58,900
-We had like to have had 
our two noses snapped off

2262
01:41:58,933 --> 01:42:01,000
by two old men without teeth.

2263
01:42:01,033 --> 01:42:03,600
-Leonato and his brother, 
what think'st thou?

2264
01:42:03,633 --> 01:42:06,533
Had we fought, I doubt we should 
have been too young for them.

2265
01:42:06,566 --> 01:42:09,400
-In a false quarrel, 
there is no true valor.

2266
01:42:09,433 --> 01:42:10,666
I came to seek you both.

2267
01:42:10,700 --> 01:42:12,500
-We have been up and down 
to seek thee,

2268
01:42:12,533 --> 01:42:13,966
for we are high-proof melancholy

2269
01:42:14,000 --> 01:42:15,700
and would fain 
have it beaten away.

2270
01:42:15,733 --> 01:42:17,200
Wilt thou use thy wit?

2271
01:42:17,233 --> 01:42:18,933
-It is in my scabbard.

2272
01:42:18,966 --> 01:42:20,133
Shall I draw it?

2273
01:42:20,166 --> 01:42:21,933
-Dost thou wear thy wit 
by thy side?

2274
01:42:21,966 --> 01:42:23,400
-Never any did so,

2275
01:42:23,433 --> 01:42:26,533
though very many have been 
beside their wit.

2276
01:42:26,566 --> 01:42:29,166
I will bid thee draw.

2277
01:42:29,200 --> 01:42:30,500
Draw to pleasure us.

2278
01:42:30,533 --> 01:42:33,633
-As I am an honest man, 
he looks dark.

2279
01:42:33,666 --> 01:42:37,000
Art thou sick or angry? 
-What courage, man!

2280
01:42:37,033 --> 01:42:40,866
-Sir, I pray you choose 
another subject.

2281
01:42:40,900 --> 01:42:44,333
-By this light, 
I think he be angry indeed.

2282
01:42:44,366 --> 01:42:47,533
-Shall I speak a word 
in your ear?

2283
01:42:47,566 --> 01:42:49,666
-God bless me from a challenge.

2284
01:42:52,833 --> 01:42:56,066
-You are a villain! 
I jest not.

2285
01:42:56,100 --> 01:42:58,733
I will make it good how you dare 
with what you dare

2286
01:42:58,766 --> 01:43:01,033
and when you dare.

2287
01:43:01,066 --> 01:43:02,266
Do me right,

2288
01:43:02,300 --> 01:43:04,833
or I will protest 
your cowardice.

2289
01:43:04,866 --> 01:43:07,266
You have killed a sweet lady,

2290
01:43:07,300 --> 01:43:11,300
and her death shall 
fall heavy on you!

2291
01:43:11,333 --> 01:43:13,000
Let me hear from you.

2292
01:43:13,033 --> 01:43:15,100
-Well, I will meet you 
so I may have good cheer.

2293
01:43:15,133 --> 01:43:17,433
-Fare you well, boy.

2294
01:43:17,466 --> 01:43:20,133
You know my mind.

2295
01:43:20,166 --> 01:43:23,300
I will leave you now 
to your gossip-like humor.

2296
01:43:23,333 --> 01:43:25,533
You break jests as braggarts 
do their blades,

2297
01:43:25,566 --> 01:43:29,533
which, God be thanked, hurt not.

2298
01:43:29,566 --> 01:43:31,233
My lord, 
for your many courtesies,

2299
01:43:31,266 --> 01:43:32,833
I thank you.

2300
01:43:32,866 --> 01:43:36,100
I must discontinue your company.

2301
01:43:36,133 --> 01:43:38,833
Your brother, the bastard, 
is fled.

2302
01:43:38,866 --> 01:43:44,800
-You have among you killed 
a sweet, innocent lady.

2303
01:43:44,833 --> 01:43:47,766
For my Lord Lackbeard there, 
he and I shall meet.

2304
01:43:47,800 --> 01:43:50,366
Till then...

2305
01:43:50,400 --> 01:43:52,400
peace be with him.

2306
01:43:54,800 --> 01:43:57,233
-He is in earnest. 
-In most profound earnest,

2307
01:43:57,266 --> 01:43:58,966
and I'll warrant you 
for the love of Beatrice.

2308
01:43:59,000 --> 01:44:01,133
-And hath challenged thee. 
-Most sincerely!

2309
01:44:01,166 --> 01:44:02,166
-But soft you, let me be.

2310
01:44:02,200 --> 01:44:04,333
Did he not say my brother 
was fled?

2311
01:44:04,366 --> 01:44:05,700
[ Whistle blows ]

2312
01:44:05,733 --> 01:44:08,600
-Come you, sir. 
-How now?

2313
01:44:08,633 --> 01:44:11,000
Two of my brother's men bound, 
Borachio one!

2314
01:44:11,033 --> 01:44:12,866
-Hearken after their offense, 
my lord.

2315
01:44:12,900 --> 01:44:14,666
-Officers, what offense 
have these men done?

2316
01:44:14,700 --> 01:44:16,300
-Marry, sir, they have 
committed false report.

2317
01:44:16,333 --> 01:44:17,666
Moreover, they have 
spoken untruths.

2318
01:44:17,700 --> 01:44:18,833
Secondarily, they are slanders.

2319
01:44:18,866 --> 01:44:20,466
Sixth and lastly, 
they have belied a lady.

2320
01:44:20,500 --> 01:44:22,500
Thirdly, they have verified 
unjust things.

2321
01:44:22,533 --> 01:44:25,966
And to conclude, 
they are lying knaves!

2322
01:44:26,000 --> 01:44:28,666
[ Applause ]

2323
01:44:30,400 --> 01:44:32,100
-First, I ask thee, 
what they have done.

2324
01:44:32,133 --> 01:44:33,666
Thirdly, I ask thee, 
what's their offense?

2325
01:44:33,700 --> 01:44:35,200
Sixth and lastly, 
why they are committed.

2326
01:44:35,233 --> 01:44:38,066
And to conclude, 
what you lay to their charge.

2327
01:44:40,466 --> 01:44:41,866
Who have you offended, masters,

2328
01:44:41,900 --> 01:44:43,800
that you are thus bound 
to your answer?

2329
01:44:43,833 --> 01:44:47,333
This learned constable is 
too cunning to be understood.

2330
01:44:50,166 --> 01:44:52,800
What's you're offense?!

2331
01:44:52,833 --> 01:44:56,133
-Sweet Prince, let me go 
no farther to mine answer.

2332
01:44:56,166 --> 01:44:59,500
Do you hear me 
and let this count kill me?

2333
01:44:59,533 --> 01:45:03,133
For I have deceived 
even your very eyes.

2334
01:45:03,166 --> 01:45:04,933
What your wisdoms 
could not discover,

2335
01:45:04,966 --> 01:45:09,000
these shallow fools 
have brought to light,

2336
01:45:09,033 --> 01:45:11,466
who in the night

2337
01:45:11,500 --> 01:45:14,166
overheard me confessing 
to this man how Don John,

2338
01:45:14,200 --> 01:45:18,166
your brother, incensed me 
to slander the Lady Hero

2339
01:45:18,200 --> 01:45:19,600
how you were brought 
into the orchard

2340
01:45:19,633 --> 01:45:23,400
and saw me court Margaret 
in Hero's garments,

2341
01:45:23,433 --> 01:45:26,233
how you disgraced her 
when you should marry her.

2342
01:45:26,266 --> 01:45:27,966
My villainy, 
they have upon record,

2343
01:45:28,000 --> 01:45:30,366
which I had rather seal 
with my death

2344
01:45:30,400 --> 01:45:32,966
than repeat over to my shame.

2345
01:45:33,000 --> 01:45:37,900
The lady is dead upon mine and 
my master's false accusation.

2346
01:45:37,933 --> 01:45:41,766
And briefly, I desire nothing 
but the reward of a villain.

2347
01:45:45,000 --> 01:45:46,500
-[ Sobs ]

2348
01:45:48,833 --> 01:45:51,066
-Runs not this speech like 
iron through your blood?

2349
01:45:51,100 --> 01:45:53,433
-I have drunk poison 
whilst he uttered it.

2350
01:45:53,466 --> 01:45:55,166
-But did my brother 
set thee on to this?

2351
01:45:55,200 --> 01:45:58,166
-Yea, and paid me richly 
for the practice of it.

2352
01:45:58,200 --> 01:46:01,166
-He is composed 
and framed of treachery,

2353
01:46:01,200 --> 01:46:03,833
and fled he is 
upon this villainy.

2354
01:46:03,866 --> 01:46:05,666
-Sweet Hero,

2355
01:46:05,700 --> 01:46:07,800
now thy image doth appear 
in the rare semblance

2356
01:46:07,833 --> 01:46:09,633
that I loved it first.

2357
01:46:09,666 --> 01:46:11,666
-Come, bring away 
the plaintiffs.

2358
01:46:11,700 --> 01:46:13,366
By this time, 
our sexton hath reformed

2359
01:46:13,400 --> 01:46:14,900
Signior Leonato of the matter.

2360
01:46:14,933 --> 01:46:17,166
And, masters, 
do not forget to specify,

2361
01:46:17,200 --> 01:46:20,700
when time and place shall serve, 
that I am an ass!

2362
01:46:20,733 --> 01:46:22,900
[ Laughter ]

2363
01:46:22,933 --> 01:46:24,466
-Which is the villain?

2364
01:46:24,500 --> 01:46:27,100
Let me see his eyes, that when 
I note another man like him,

2365
01:46:27,133 --> 01:46:28,066
I may avoid him.

2366
01:46:28,100 --> 01:46:29,466
Which of these is he?

2367
01:46:29,500 --> 01:46:31,866
-If you would know your wronger, 
look on me.

2368
01:46:31,900 --> 01:46:34,466
-Art thou the slave that

2369
01:46:34,500 --> 01:46:36,400
with thy breath

2370
01:46:36,433 --> 01:46:40,066
hast killed mine innocent child?

2371
01:46:40,100 --> 01:46:42,633
-Yea, even I alone.

2372
01:46:42,666 --> 01:46:44,600
-No, not so, villain.

2373
01:46:44,633 --> 01:46:46,800
Thou belie'st thyself.

2374
01:46:46,833 --> 01:46:49,766
Here stand a pair 
of honorable men.

2375
01:46:49,800 --> 01:46:51,833
A third is fled 
that had a hand in it.

2376
01:46:51,866 --> 01:46:55,366
I thank you, princes, 
for my daughter's death.

2377
01:46:55,400 --> 01:46:58,333
Record it with your high 
and worthy deeds.

2378
01:46:58,366 --> 01:47:00,766
'Twas bravely done, 
if you bethink you of it.

2379
01:47:00,800 --> 01:47:02,366
-I know not how 
to pray your patience,

2380
01:47:02,400 --> 01:47:04,433
yet I must speak.

2381
01:47:04,466 --> 01:47:06,233
Choose your revenge yourself.

2382
01:47:06,266 --> 01:47:07,533
Impose me to what penance

2383
01:47:07,566 --> 01:47:09,500
your invention 
can lay upon my sin,

2384
01:47:09,533 --> 01:47:11,300
yet sinned I not 
but in mistaking.

2385
01:47:11,333 --> 01:47:13,166
-By my soul, nor I,

2386
01:47:13,200 --> 01:47:15,200
and yet to satisfy 
this good old man,

2387
01:47:15,233 --> 01:47:17,333
I would bend under 
any heavy weight

2388
01:47:17,366 --> 01:47:18,766
that he'll enjoin me to.

2389
01:47:18,800 --> 01:47:22,666
-I cannot bid you bid 
my daughter live.

2390
01:47:22,700 --> 01:47:24,533
That were impossible.

2391
01:47:24,566 --> 01:47:27,033
[ Laughter ]

2392
01:47:27,066 --> 01:47:30,933
But I pray you both possess 
the people here

2393
01:47:30,966 --> 01:47:33,566
how innocent she died.

2394
01:47:33,600 --> 01:47:39,133
And if your love can labor ought 
in sad invention,

2395
01:47:39,166 --> 01:47:43,533
hang her an epitaph 
upon her tomb

2396
01:47:43,566 --> 01:47:45,933
and sing it to her bones.

2397
01:47:45,966 --> 01:47:47,433
Sing it tonight!

2398
01:47:47,466 --> 01:47:50,100
Tomorrow morning, 
come you to my house.

2399
01:47:50,133 --> 01:47:53,600
And since you could not 
be my son-in-law,

2400
01:47:53,633 --> 01:47:56,533
be yet my nephew.

2401
01:47:56,566 --> 01:47:58,500
My brother hath a daughter,

2402
01:47:58,533 --> 01:48:03,100
almost the copy of my child...

2403
01:48:03,133 --> 01:48:04,466
that's dead.

2404
01:48:06,233 --> 01:48:08,133
She alone is heir to both of us.

2405
01:48:08,166 --> 01:48:10,066
Give her the right you should 
have given her cousin,

2406
01:48:10,100 --> 01:48:12,366
and so dies my revenge.

2407
01:48:12,400 --> 01:48:13,866
-Oh, noble sir!

2408
01:48:13,900 --> 01:48:16,266
Your overkindness doth 
wring tears from me.

2409
01:48:16,300 --> 01:48:17,400
I do embrace your offer

2410
01:48:17,433 --> 01:48:19,500
and dispose for henceforth 
of poor Claudio.

2411
01:48:19,533 --> 01:48:21,033
-Tomorrow then, 
I expect your coming.

2412
01:48:21,066 --> 01:48:22,266
Tonight, I take my leave.

2413
01:48:22,300 --> 01:48:23,900
This naughty man

2414
01:48:23,933 --> 01:48:25,733
shall face-to-face 
be brought to Margaret,

2415
01:48:25,766 --> 01:48:28,733
who I believe was packed in 
all this wrong,

2416
01:48:28,766 --> 01:48:31,166
hired to it by your brother.

2417
01:48:31,200 --> 01:48:34,166
-No, by my soul, she was not,

2418
01:48:34,200 --> 01:48:36,133
nor knew not what she did 
when she spoke to me,

2419
01:48:36,166 --> 01:48:38,533
but always hath been 
just and virtuous

2420
01:48:38,566 --> 01:48:40,633
in anything that 
I do know by her.

2421
01:48:40,666 --> 01:48:42,633
-Moreover, sir, 
this plaintiff here,

2422
01:48:42,666 --> 01:48:44,466
the offender, did call me ass.

2423
01:48:44,500 --> 01:48:45,800
I beseech you, 
let it be remembered

2424
01:48:45,833 --> 01:48:47,500
in his punishment.

2425
01:48:49,200 --> 01:48:51,700
-I thank thee for thy care 
and honest pain.

2426
01:48:51,733 --> 01:48:54,500
-Your worship speaks like a most 
thankful and reverent youth,

2427
01:48:54,533 --> 01:48:56,500
and I praise God for you.

2428
01:48:56,533 --> 01:48:58,533
-There's for thy pain.

2429
01:48:58,566 --> 01:49:00,933
-God save the foundation.

2430
01:49:04,100 --> 01:49:05,633
[ Laughter ]

2431
01:49:08,166 --> 01:49:09,000
-Go!

2432
01:49:09,033 --> 01:49:10,533
I discharge thee 
of thy prisoner,

2433
01:49:10,566 --> 01:49:11,700
and I thank thee.

2434
01:49:11,733 --> 01:49:13,500
-I leave an arrant knave 
with your worship,

2435
01:49:13,533 --> 01:49:14,733
which I would 
beseech your worship

2436
01:49:14,766 --> 01:49:17,166
to correct yourself 
for the example of others.

2437
01:49:17,200 --> 01:49:18,733
God keep your worship!

2438
01:49:18,766 --> 01:49:25,233
I wish your worship well.

2439
01:49:25,266 --> 01:49:28,166
[ Laughter ]

2440
01:49:28,200 --> 01:49:30,433
God restore you to health!

2441
01:49:30,466 --> 01:49:32,366
I humbly give you 
leave to depart,

2442
01:49:32,400 --> 01:49:34,200
and if a merry meeting 
may be wished,

2443
01:49:34,233 --> 01:49:35,666
God prohibit it!

2444
01:49:35,700 --> 01:49:36,933
Come, neighbor.

2445
01:49:36,966 --> 01:49:38,933
-Until tomorrow morning, 
my lords, fare you well.

2446
01:49:38,966 --> 01:49:40,166
-Farewell, my lords.

2447
01:49:40,200 --> 01:49:43,433
We'll look for you tomorrow. 
-We will not fail.

2448
01:49:43,466 --> 01:49:45,033
-Tonight, I'll mourn with Hero.

2449
01:49:45,066 --> 01:49:46,400
-Bring you these fellows on.

2450
01:49:46,433 --> 01:49:49,100
We'll talk with Margaret 
how her acquaintance grew

2451
01:49:49,133 --> 01:49:51,700
with this lewd fellow.

2452
01:49:51,733 --> 01:49:53,600
-♪ Na, na, na

2453
01:49:53,633 --> 01:49:56,566
♪ Na, na, na, na

2454
01:49:56,600 --> 01:50:01,033
♪ Na, na, na, na, na

2455
01:50:01,066 --> 01:50:02,733
♪ Na, na, na

2456
01:50:02,766 --> 01:50:04,433
♪ Na, na, na, na

2457
01:50:04,466 --> 01:50:05,566
♪ Na, na --

2458
01:50:05,600 --> 01:50:07,166
♪ N-- No!

2459
01:50:07,200 --> 01:50:09,400
♪ No, no

2460
01:50:09,433 --> 01:50:11,866
♪ No, no, no, no, no, no

2461
01:50:11,900 --> 01:50:13,733
♪ No, no, no, no

2462
01:50:13,766 --> 01:50:15,500
♪ No, no, no, no, no, no, no

2463
01:50:15,533 --> 01:50:17,466
♪ No, no, no, no, no

2464
01:50:17,500 --> 01:50:19,900
♪ No, no, no, no, no, no

2465
01:50:19,933 --> 01:50:22,333
-Pray thee, 
sweet Mistress Margaret.

2466
01:50:22,366 --> 01:50:24,433
Deserve well at my hands 
by helping me

2467
01:50:24,466 --> 01:50:25,966
to the speech of Beatrice.

2468
01:50:26,000 --> 01:50:29,433
-Will you then write

2469
01:50:26,000 --> 01:50:29,433
me

2470
01:50:26,000 --> 01:50:29,433
a sonnet 
in praise of

2471
01:50:26,000 --> 01:50:29,433
my

2472
01:50:26,000 --> 01:50:29,433
beauty?

2473
01:50:29,466 --> 01:50:31,533
-In so high a style, Margaret,

2474
01:50:31,566 --> 01:50:33,600
that no man living 
shall come over it,

2475
01:50:33,633 --> 01:50:36,266
for in most comely truth, 
thou deservest it.

2476
01:50:36,300 --> 01:50:37,766
-To have no man come over me!

2477
01:50:37,800 --> 01:50:40,433
Why, shall I always 
keep below stairs?

2478
01:50:40,466 --> 01:50:42,466
-Thy wit is as quick 
as the greyhound's mouth.

2479
01:50:42,500 --> 01:50:44,366
It catches. 
-[ Chuckles ]

2480
01:50:44,400 --> 01:50:47,266
And yours as blunt 
as the fencer's foils,

2481
01:50:47,300 --> 01:50:49,433
which hit but hurt not.

2482
01:50:49,466 --> 01:50:51,400
-A most manly wit, Margaret.

2483
01:50:51,433 --> 01:50:53,733
It will not hurt a woman.

2484
01:50:53,766 --> 01:50:55,866
And so, I pray thee,

2485
01:50:55,900 --> 01:50:57,733
call Beatrice.

2486
01:50:57,766 --> 01:50:59,766
-Okay.

2487
01:51:02,566 --> 01:51:05,000
-[ Sighs ]

2488
01:51:05,033 --> 01:51:07,766
♪ Oh, oh, oh

2489
01:51:07,800 --> 01:51:13,233
♪ Oh, don't you love, 
don't you love me no more ♪

2490
01:51:13,266 --> 01:51:16,933
♪ Know that I'm fire

2491
01:51:16,966 --> 01:51:19,000
♪ Stop playing

2492
01:51:19,033 --> 01:51:22,000
♪ Know you can't let me go

2493
01:51:22,033 --> 01:51:26,466
♪ Why you saying 
your love is expired? ♪

2494
01:51:26,500 --> 01:51:29,933
♪ I can tell when you're lying

2495
01:51:29,966 --> 01:51:32,733
♪ I know how you feel

2496
01:51:32,766 --> 01:51:34,933
♪ Yeah, I know

2497
01:51:34,966 --> 01:51:38,533
♪ Stop singing 
all those sad songs ♪

2498
01:51:38,566 --> 01:51:43,233
♪ Come and get this 
glad song, baby ♪

2499
01:51:43,266 --> 01:51:46,233
♪ Na, na, na, na, na, na, na

2500
01:51:46,266 --> 01:51:49,533
♪ Na, na, na, ney, ney

2501
01:51:49,566 --> 01:51:52,333
♪ Na, na, na, na, na, na, na

2502
01:51:52,366 --> 01:51:55,833
♪ Mm, you know you 
love me, baby ♪

2503
01:51:55,866 --> 01:51:59,033
♪ Baby, baby, baby, baby

2504
01:51:59,066 --> 01:52:02,266
♪ Lady, lady, lady, lady

2505
01:52:02,300 --> 01:52:03,600
♪ I'm your fool

2506
01:52:03,633 --> 01:52:04,700
♪ I'm your fool

2507
01:52:04,733 --> 01:52:07,966
♪ I'm your fool

2508
01:52:08,000 --> 01:52:10,366
In school?

2509
01:52:10,400 --> 01:52:12,566
[ Laughter ]

2510
01:52:12,600 --> 01:52:15,166
I mean in singing, 
but in loving,

2511
01:52:15,200 --> 01:52:16,666
Leander the good swimmer,

2512
01:52:16,700 --> 01:52:19,000
Troilus, 
the first employer of panders

2513
01:52:19,033 --> 01:52:21,366
and a whole bookful 
of those quondam carpetmongers

2514
01:52:21,400 --> 01:52:25,266
whose names yet run smoothly in 
the even road of a blank verse.

2515
01:52:25,300 --> 01:52:28,100
Why, they were never 
so truly turned over and over

2516
01:52:28,133 --> 01:52:30,166
as my poor self in love.

2517
01:52:30,200 --> 01:52:33,133
Marry, I cannot 
show it in rhyme.

2518
01:52:33,166 --> 01:52:34,966
I have tried.

2519
01:52:35,000 --> 01:52:38,833
I can find out no rhyme 
to "lady" but "baby,"

2520
01:52:38,866 --> 01:52:40,600
an innocent rhyme;

2521
01:52:40,633 --> 01:52:43,333
for "scorn," "horn," 
a hard rhyme;

2522
01:52:43,366 --> 01:52:45,800
for "school," "fool,"

2523
01:52:45,833 --> 01:52:47,200
a babbling rhyme,

2524
01:52:47,233 --> 01:52:49,533
very ominous endings.

2525
01:52:49,566 --> 01:52:52,100
No, I was not born 
under a rhyming planet,

2526
01:52:52,133 --> 01:52:54,900
nor I cannot woo 
in festival terms.

2527
01:52:54,933 --> 01:52:58,700
-[ Sighs ] 
-Sweet Beatrice?

2528
01:52:58,733 --> 01:53:00,933
Wouldst thou come 
when I called thee?

2529
01:53:00,966 --> 01:53:03,500
-Yes, signior, 
and depart when you bid me.

2530
01:53:03,533 --> 01:53:04,800
-Ooh!

2531
01:53:04,833 --> 01:53:08,066
Stay but till then! 
-Then is spoken.

2532
01:53:08,100 --> 01:53:09,400
Fare you well now.

2533
01:53:09,433 --> 01:53:11,366
-[ Chuckles ] 
-And yet, ere I go,

2534
01:53:11,400 --> 01:53:13,166
let me go with that I came,

2535
01:53:13,200 --> 01:53:16,500
which is in knowing what hath 
passed between you and Claudio.

2536
01:53:16,533 --> 01:53:19,200
-Only foul words.

2537
01:53:19,233 --> 01:53:20,800
And thereupon,

2538
01:53:20,833 --> 01:53:23,066
I will kiss thee. 
-Mnm-mnm.

2539
01:53:23,100 --> 01:53:25,500
Foul words is but foul wind,

2540
01:53:25,533 --> 01:53:26,700
and fould wind 
is but foul breath,

2541
01:53:26,733 --> 01:53:28,900
and foul breath is noisome.

2542
01:53:28,933 --> 01:53:31,800
Therefore, 
I will depart unkissed.

2543
01:53:31,833 --> 01:53:34,433
-Thou hast frighted the word 
out of his right sense,

2544
01:53:34,466 --> 01:53:37,066
so forcible is thy wit.

2545
01:53:37,100 --> 01:53:39,466
But I must tell thee plainly,

2546
01:53:39,500 --> 01:53:41,833
Claudio undergoes my challenge.

2547
01:53:41,866 --> 01:53:43,666
And either I must 
shortly hear from him,

2548
01:53:43,700 --> 01:53:46,666
or I will subscribe him 
a coward.

2549
01:53:46,700 --> 01:53:50,866
And now, I pray thee, tell me,

2550
01:53:50,900 --> 01:53:54,966
for which of my bad parts

2551
01:53:55,000 --> 01:53:57,400
didst thou first fall in love 
with me?

2552
01:53:57,433 --> 01:53:58,466
-[ Laughs ]

2553
01:53:58,500 --> 01:54:00,333
-For them all together,

2554
01:54:00,366 --> 01:54:02,366
which maintained so politic

2555
01:54:02,400 --> 01:54:04,600
a state of evil 
that they will not admit

2556
01:54:04,633 --> 01:54:07,633
any good part 
to intermingle with them.

2557
01:54:07,666 --> 01:54:11,333
But for which of my...

2558
01:54:11,366 --> 01:54:16,000
good parts did thy first 
suffer love for me?

2559
01:54:16,033 --> 01:54:19,700
-Suffer love! 
A good epithet!

2560
01:54:19,733 --> 01:54:23,366
I do suffer love indeed, 
for I love thee against my will.

2561
01:54:23,400 --> 01:54:25,533
-In spite of your heart, 
I think.

2562
01:54:25,566 --> 01:54:28,300
Alas, poor heart, 
if you spite it for my sake,

2563
01:54:28,333 --> 01:54:29,600
I will spite it for yours,

2564
01:54:29,633 --> 01:54:32,633
for I will never love 
that which my friend hates.

2565
01:54:32,666 --> 01:54:36,533
-Thou and I are too wise 
to woo peaceably.

2566
01:54:36,566 --> 01:54:39,633
Now tell me, 
how doth your cousin?

2567
01:54:39,666 --> 01:54:41,400
-Very ill.

2568
01:54:41,433 --> 01:54:43,500
-And how do you?

2569
01:54:43,533 --> 01:54:46,100
-Very ill, too.

2570
01:54:46,133 --> 01:54:48,000
-Serve God,

2571
01:54:48,033 --> 01:54:49,966
love me,

2572
01:54:50,000 --> 01:54:51,933
and mend. 
-Madam!

2573
01:54:51,966 --> 01:54:54,466
-There will I leave you, 
for here comes one in haste.

2574
01:54:54,500 --> 01:54:55,633
-[ Breathing heavily ]

2575
01:54:55,666 --> 01:54:57,800
-Oh, Madam, you --

2576
01:54:57,833 --> 01:55:01,500
[ Laughter ]

2577
01:55:01,533 --> 01:55:03,300
-Madam?

2578
01:55:03,333 --> 01:55:04,533
Madam!

2579
01:55:04,566 --> 01:55:06,400
You must come to your uncle.

2580
01:55:06,433 --> 01:55:10,100
It has been proved, my Lady Hero 
hath been falsely accused,

2581
01:55:10,133 --> 01:55:12,633
the Prince and Claudio 
mightily abused,

2582
01:55:12,666 --> 01:55:14,666
and Don John 
is the author of all,

2583
01:55:14,700 --> 01:55:16,233
who is fled and gone.

2584
01:55:16,266 --> 01:55:17,766
Will you come presently?

2585
01:55:17,800 --> 01:55:20,866
-[ Panting ]

2586
01:55:20,900 --> 01:55:23,033
-Will you go hear this news, 
Signior?

2587
01:55:23,066 --> 01:55:25,966
-I will live in thy heart, 
die in thy lap,

2588
01:55:26,000 --> 01:55:27,833
and be be buried in thy eyes.

2589
01:55:27,866 --> 01:55:31,200
And moreover, I will go 
with thee to thy uncle's.

2590
01:55:31,233 --> 01:55:33,366
♪♪

2591
