we rendered up this woe.

2640
01:59:02,300 --> 01:59:06,333
-Did I not tell you 
she was innocent?

2641
01:59:06,366 --> 01:59:07,433
[ Chuckles ]

2642
01:59:07,466 --> 01:59:09,733
-So, are the prince and Claudio,

2643
01:59:09,766 --> 01:59:13,766
who accused her upon the error 
which you heard debated.

2644
01:59:29,366 --> 01:59:32,433
[ Applause ]

2645
01:59:37,900 --> 01:59:42,633
But [clears throat] Margaret 
was in some fault for this,

2646
01:59:42,666 --> 01:59:45,200
although against her will 
as it appears

2647
01:59:45,233 --> 01:59:47,933
in the true course 
of all the question.

2648
01:59:47,966 --> 01:59:52,866
-Well, I am glad 
all things sort so well.

2649
01:59:52,900 --> 01:59:54,166
-And so am I,

2650
01:59:54,200 --> 01:59:57,333
being else by faith enforced 
to call young Claudio

2651
01:59:57,366 --> 01:59:58,900
to a reckoning for it.

2652
01:59:58,933 --> 02:00:01,033
-Well, daughter, 
and gentlewomen all,

2653
02:00:01,066 --> 02:00:03,066
withdraw you into a chamber 
by yourselves.

2654
02:00:03,100 --> 02:00:06,933
And when I send for you, 
come hither masked.

2655
02:00:06,966 --> 02:00:08,266
[ Chuckles ]

2656
02:00:08,300 --> 02:00:10,333
The Prince and Claudio 
have promised upon this hour

2657
02:00:10,366 --> 02:00:11,266
to visit me.

2658
02:00:11,300 --> 02:00:12,466
Brother, you know your office.

2659
02:00:12,500 --> 02:00:16,566
You must be father 
to your brother's daughter

2660
02:00:16,600 --> 02:00:18,533
and give her to young Claudio.

2661
02:00:18,566 --> 02:00:21,633
-Which I will do 
with confirmed countenance.

2662
02:00:21,666 --> 02:00:24,766
-Friar, I must entreat 
your pains, I think.

2663
02:00:24,800 --> 02:00:26,866
-To do what, Signior?

2664
02:00:26,900 --> 02:00:30,400
-To bind me or undo me, 
one of them.

2665
02:00:30,433 --> 02:00:33,166
Signior Leonato, 
truth it is, good Signior.

2666
02:00:33,200 --> 02:00:35,666
Your niece regards me 
with an eye of favor.

2667
02:00:35,700 --> 02:00:38,200
-That eye my daughter lent her, 
'tis most true.

2668
02:00:38,233 --> 02:00:41,700
-And I do with an eye of love 
requite her.

2669
02:00:41,733 --> 02:00:43,300
-The sight whereof 
I believe you had from me,

2670
02:00:43,333 --> 02:00:46,233
the Prince, and Claudio, 
but what's your will?

2671
02:00:46,266 --> 02:00:49,666
-Your answer, sir, 
is enigmatical.

2672
02:00:49,700 --> 02:00:51,766
But for my will,

2673
02:00:51,800 --> 02:00:54,700
my will is your goodwill 
may stand with ours,

2674
02:00:54,733 --> 02:00:57,033
this day, to be conjoined

2675
02:00:57,066 --> 02:01:00,233
in the state of honorable

2676
02:01:00,266 --> 02:01:03,466
m-- [ Laughs ]

2677
02:01:03,500 --> 02:01:05,933
In the state of honorable...

2678
02:01:05,966 --> 02:01:07,733
m--

2679
02:01:11,100 --> 02:01:13,000
[ Whispers ] Marriage.

2680
02:01:13,033 --> 02:01:17,366
In which, good Friar, 
I shall desire your help.

2681
02:01:17,400 --> 02:01:19,666
-My heart is with your liking.

2682
02:01:19,700 --> 02:01:21,600
-And my heart.

2683
02:01:21,633 --> 02:01:23,600
Here comes the Prince 
and Claudio.

2684
02:01:23,633 --> 02:01:25,433
-Good morrow 
to this fair assembly.

2685
02:01:25,466 --> 02:01:26,866
-Good morrow, count. 
Good morrow, Claudio.

2686
02:01:26,900 --> 02:01:28,233
We here attend you.

2687
02:01:28,266 --> 02:01:31,100
Are you yet determined 
today to marry

2688
02:01:31,133 --> 02:01:32,466
with my brother's daughter?

2689
02:01:32,500 --> 02:01:35,000
-I'll hold my mind. 
-Brother, call her forth.

2690
02:01:35,033 --> 02:01:37,033
Here's the Friar, ready.

2691
02:01:40,066 --> 02:01:41,800
-Good morrow, Benedick.

2692
02:01:41,833 --> 02:01:45,100
Why, what's the matter that 
you have such a February face,

2693
02:01:45,133 --> 02:01:48,000
so full of frost, of storm, 
and cloudiness?

2694
02:01:48,033 --> 02:01:52,366
♪♪

2695
02:01:52,400 --> 02:01:55,566
-Here comes other reck'nings.

2696
02:01:55,600 --> 02:02:00,566
-♪ Today I'll make a promise

2697
02:02:00,600 --> 02:02:05,166
♪ To share with you my life

2698
02:02:05,200 --> 02:02:08,766
♪ Everything I give to you

2699
02:02:08,800 --> 02:02:13,533
♪ For I am yours 
and you are mine ♪

2700
02:02:13,566 --> 02:02:17,766
-♪ Where you go, I will go

2701
02:02:17,800 --> 02:02:22,200
♪ Knowing you'll be by my side

2702
02:02:22,233 --> 02:02:25,800
♪ I will leave 
the world behind ♪

2703
02:02:25,833 --> 02:02:30,266
-♪ No matter where you are, 
remember ♪

2704
02:02:30,300 --> 02:02:34,566
♪ I'll never be too far away

2705
02:02:34,600 --> 02:02:39,000
♪ And when the good times 
turn to bad times ♪

2706
02:02:39,033 --> 02:02:43,233
♪ Know that my heart 
will still remain ♪

2707
02:02:43,266 --> 02:02:46,933
-♪ And as the days 
turn to years ♪

2708
02:02:46,966 --> 02:02:50,966
-♪ To years 
-♪ My love will never change

2709
02:02:51,000 --> 02:02:52,400
-♪ Oh

2710
02:02:52,433 --> 02:02:56,933
♪ And my heart belongs 
to only you ♪

2711
02:02:57,633 --> 02:03:00,966
-♪ No matter where you are, 
remember ♪

2712
02:03:01,000 --> 02:03:05,233
-♪ I'll never be too far away

2713
02:03:05,266 --> 02:03:09,300
-♪ And when the good times 
turn to bad times ♪

2714
02:03:09,333 --> 02:03:13,900
-♪ Know that my heart 
will still remain ♪

2715
02:03:13,933 --> 02:03:17,500
♪ And as the days 
turn to years ♪

2716
02:03:17,533 --> 02:03:22,900
-♪ To years 
-♪ My love will never change

2717
02:03:22,933 --> 02:03:29,533
-♪ And my heart belongs 
to only you ♪

2718
02:03:29,566 --> 02:03:34,800
♪ Always

2719
02:03:34,833 --> 02:03:38,466
-♪ Only you

2720
02:03:38,500 --> 02:03:44,300
♪ Always

2721
02:03:44,333 --> 02:03:47,200
[ Cheers and applause ]

2722
02:03:50,066 --> 02:03:52,633
-Which is the lady 
I must seize upon?

2723
02:04:00,300 --> 02:04:01,700
-[ Clears throat ]

2724
02:04:09,166 --> 02:04:10,833
Mnm-mnm, mm.

2725
02:04:12,633 --> 02:04:17,333
-This same is she, 
and I do give you her.

2726
02:04:17,366 --> 02:04:18,800
-Why, then she's mine.

2727
02:04:18,833 --> 02:04:20,066
Sweet, let me see your face.

2728
02:04:20,100 --> 02:04:22,000
-No!

2729
02:04:22,033 --> 02:04:23,766
That you shall not 
till you take her hand

2730
02:04:23,800 --> 02:04:28,266
before this friar 
and swear to marry her.

2731
02:04:28,300 --> 02:04:30,966
[ Laughter ]

2732
02:04:34,433 --> 02:04:37,133
-Give me your hand 
before this holy friar.

2733
02:04:43,500 --> 02:04:46,400
I am your husband, 
if you like of me.

2734
02:04:46,433 --> 02:04:50,366
-And when I lived, 
I was your other wife.

2735
02:04:50,400 --> 02:04:54,233
And when you loved, 
you were my other husband.

2736
02:04:56,966 --> 02:05:00,500
-Another Hero! 
-Nothing certainer.

2737
02:05:00,533 --> 02:05:03,933
One Hero died defiled, 
but I do live.

2738
02:05:06,400 --> 02:05:09,900
[ Cheers and applause ]

2739
02:05:11,633 --> 02:05:15,733
And surely as I live, 
I am a maiden.

2740
02:05:15,766 --> 02:05:17,633
-The former Hero,

2741
02:05:17,666 --> 02:05:19,233
Hero that is dead!

2742
02:05:19,266 --> 02:05:22,400
-She died my lord, 
but whiles her slander lived.

2743
02:05:22,433 --> 02:05:26,066
-All this amazement 
can I qualify

2744
02:05:26,100 --> 02:05:29,233
when after that 
the holy rites are ended,

2745
02:05:29,266 --> 02:05:31,633
I'll tell you largely 
of fair Hero's death.

2746
02:05:31,666 --> 02:05:33,833
Meantime, 
let wonder seem familiar

2747
02:05:33,866 --> 02:05:36,233
and to the chapel, 
let us presently.

2748
02:05:36,266 --> 02:05:39,566
-Oh! Soft and fair, friar.

2749
02:05:39,600 --> 02:05:41,566
Which is Beatrice?

2750
02:05:41,600 --> 02:05:43,766
[ Laughter ]

2751
02:05:46,666 --> 02:05:49,833
-I answer to that name. 
What is your will?

2752
02:05:56,333 --> 02:05:59,500
-Do not you love me?

2753
02:06:01,133 --> 02:06:03,600
-Why no. [ Chuckles ]

2754
02:06:03,633 --> 02:06:04,966
No more than reason.

2755
02:06:05,000 --> 02:06:06,333
-Why then, your uncle,

2756
02:06:06,366 --> 02:06:09,133
the prince, and Claudio 
have been deceived.

2757
02:06:09,166 --> 02:06:11,833
They swore you did. 
-Do not

2758
02:06:09,166 --> 02:06:11,833
you

2759
02:06:09,166 --> 02:06:11,833
love

2760
02:06:09,166 --> 02:06:11,833
me?

2761
02:06:11,866 --> 02:06:14,966
-Troth, nah.

2762
02:06:15,000 --> 02:06:16,466
No more than reason.

2763
02:06:16,500 --> 02:06:20,000
-Why, then my cousin, Margaret, 
and Ursula are much deceived,

2764
02:06:20,033 --> 02:06:21,400
for they did swear you did.

2765
02:06:21,433 --> 02:06:22,866
-They swore you were 
almost sick for me.

2766
02:06:22,900 --> 02:06:25,966
-They swore you were 
well-nigh dead for me.

2767
02:06:26,000 --> 02:06:27,566
[ Laughter ]

2768
02:06:27,600 --> 02:06:29,533
-'Tis no such matter.

2769
02:06:29,566 --> 02:06:33,266
Then you... 
do

2770
02:06:29,566 --> 02:06:33,266
not

2771
02:06:29,566 --> 02:06:33,266
love me?

2772
02:06:33,300 --> 02:06:35,366
-No!

2773
02:06:35,400 --> 02:06:39,066
But truly, 
in friendly recompense.

2774
02:06:41,100 --> 02:06:44,300
-Come, cousin, I am sure 
you love the gentleman.

2775
02:06:44,333 --> 02:06:46,900
-And I'll be sworn upon't 
that he loves her,

2776
02:06:46,933 --> 02:06:48,900
for here's a paper written 
in his hand...

2777
02:06:48,933 --> 02:06:50,633
-Aye, oh! 
-...a halting sonnet

2778
02:06:50,666 --> 02:06:52,600
of his own pure brain

2779
02:06:52,633 --> 02:06:55,200
fashioned to Beatrice.

2780
02:06:55,233 --> 02:06:56,733
-And here's another,

2781
02:06:56,766 --> 02:06:58,300
writ in my cousin's hand,

2782
02:06:58,333 --> 02:06:59,700
stolen from her pocket,

2783
02:06:59,733 --> 02:07:02,666
containing her affection 
unto Benedick.

2784
02:07:02,700 --> 02:07:06,033
[ Laughter ]

2785
02:07:12,833 --> 02:07:14,966
-[ Giggles ]

2786
02:07:15,000 --> 02:07:16,466
[ Laughter ]

2787
02:07:22,400 --> 02:07:25,266
[ Light laughter ]

2788
02:07:25,300 --> 02:07:28,033
-A miracle!

2789
02:07:28,066 --> 02:07:32,066
Here's our own hands 
against our hearts.

2790
02:07:32,100 --> 02:07:33,266
Come.

2791
02:07:33,300 --> 02:07:35,633
I will have thee,

2792
02:07:35,666 --> 02:07:39,300
but by this light, 
I take thee for pity.

2793
02:07:39,333 --> 02:07:41,033
-I would not deny you,

2794
02:07:41,066 --> 02:07:44,333
but by this good day, 
I yield upon great persuasion,

2795
02:07:44,366 --> 02:07:46,000
and partly to save your life,

2796
02:07:46,033 --> 02:07:48,933
for I was told you 
were in a consumption.

2797
02:07:48,966 --> 02:07:50,433
[ Laughter ]

2798
02:07:50,466 --> 02:07:52,800
-Peace!

2799
02:07:52,833 --> 02:07:55,333
I will stop your mouth.

2800
02:07:57,866 --> 02:08:00,700
[ Cheers and applause ]

2801
02:08:02,766 --> 02:08:06,533
-How dost thou, Benedick, 
the married man?

2802
02:08:06,566 --> 02:08:08,700
[ Cheers and applause ]

2803
02:08:08,733 --> 02:08:12,633
-In brief, 
since I do purpose to marry,

2804
02:08:12,666 --> 02:08:14,233
I will think nothing 
to any purpose

2805
02:08:14,266 --> 02:08:16,833
that the world 
can say against it.

2806
02:08:16,866 --> 02:08:20,266
And therefore, never flout at me 
for what I have said against it.

2807
02:08:20,300 --> 02:08:22,566
For man is a giddy thing,

2808
02:08:22,600 --> 02:08:25,400
and this is my conclusion.

2809
02:08:25,433 --> 02:08:27,333
Claudio, for thy part,

2810
02:08:27,366 --> 02:08:29,900
I did think to have beaten thee,

2811
02:08:29,933 --> 02:08:33,333
but in that thou art like 
to be my kinsman...

2812
02:08:33,366 --> 02:08:35,200
live unbruised

2813
02:08:35,233 --> 02:08:37,500
and love my cousin.

2814
02:08:37,533 --> 02:08:40,366
-I had well hoped thou 
would have denied Beatrice

2815
02:08:40,400 --> 02:08:42,200
that I might have cudgeled thee 
out of thy single life

2816
02:08:42,233 --> 02:08:43,933
to make thee a double-dealer,

2817
02:08:43,966 --> 02:08:47,466
which, out of question, 
thou wilt be if my cousin do not

2818
02:08:47,500 --> 02:08:49,100
look exceeding narrowly to thee.

2819
02:08:49,133 --> 02:08:52,133
-Come, come! 
We are friends.

2820
02:08:52,166 --> 02:08:54,266
Let us have a dance 
ere we are married,

2821
02:08:54,300 --> 02:08:56,500
that we might lighten 
our own hearts

2822
02:08:56,533 --> 02:08:58,900
and our wives' heels.

2823
02:08:58,933 --> 02:09:01,466
-We'll have dancing afterwards.

2824
02:09:01,500 --> 02:09:03,600
-First, of my word!

2825
02:09:03,633 --> 02:09:05,666
Prince, thou art sad.

2826
02:09:05,700 --> 02:09:07,033
Get thee a wife.

2827
02:09:07,066 --> 02:09:08,466
Get thee a wife!

2828
02:09:08,500 --> 02:09:11,133
[ All cheering ]

2829
02:09:11,166 --> 02:09:13,966
-My lord, your brother John 
is taken in flight

2830
02:09:14,000 --> 02:09:15,766
and brought with armed men back.

2831
02:09:15,800 --> 02:09:18,466
-Think not on him till tomorrow.

2832
02:09:18,500 --> 02:09:20,933
I'll devise 
the brave punishments

2833
02:09:20,966 --> 02:09:22,833
